{"abstract":"BACKGROUND: Persistent postsurgical pain (PPSP) following thoracic surgery affects 40%-60% of patients undergoing lung resection due to malignancies. Postoperative pain-related symptoms are common, leading to limitations in activities of daily living (ADL) and deterioration in physical function, which significantly impacts quality of life. Pain-related limitations are of interest, as postsurgical pain may present as a target for intervention to improve postoperative rehabilitation. This study aimed to evaluate the association between PPSP and ADL limitations during the first 12 postoperative months after surgery for lung cancer. METHODS: A total of 124 patients undergoing surgery for lung cancer were followed for 12 months. Every 2 months, participants reported ADL limitations attributed to PPSP. Cumulative pain impairment scores were calculated from reported limitations in 14 daily activities, and recovery trajectory patterns were analysed. RESULTS: Daily activities most affected by PPSP were carrying bags, arm elevation, climbing stairs, cleaning floors and coughing, with >50% reporting limitations across all assessment times. Reported pain intensities were generally mild (NRS≤3), but still associated with significant impairment. Some recovery was observed in patients reporting pain at rest, but PPSP was consistently associated with higher cumulative pain impairment scores at all assessments during the 12-month follow-up period. CONCLUSIONS: Findings indicate that persistent postsurgical pain, even of mild intensity, is associated with significant limitations in daily activities up to 12 months post-surgery. Some improvement in pain-related impairment was observed, although limitations remained significantly higher in patients reporting persistent postsurgical pain, as compared to pain-free patients. SIGNIFICANCE: Surgery remains a cornerstone in the treatment of early-stage lung cancer. Despite advances in minimally invasive techniques and rehabilitation, persisting postsurgical pain and pain-related limitations in daily activities may endure. This study investigated specifically the pain-related limitations in activities of daily living and described recovery trajectories during the first 12 postoperative months. Patients with persistent postsurgical pain experienced multiple limitations compared to pain-free patients. Although partial recovery was observed, impairments remained significant for up to 12 months after surgery.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Danielsen, Allan Vestergaard","Andreasen, Jan Jesper","Dinesen, Birthe","Hansen, John","Petersen, Kristian Kjær","Duch, Kirsten","Simonsen, Carsten","Arendt-Nielsen, Lars"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-770752"],"filters":{"added":"2025-01","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Danielsen, Allan Vestergaard"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"pain related impairment in daily activities after lung cancer surgery a 000000000001 year prospective cohort study","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC 4.0","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1002/ejp.4749","version":"Published Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["Department of Cardiothoracic Surgery, Aalborg University Hospital. Speciall\\u00E6ge Heinrich Kopps Research Grant. Center for Neuroplasticity and Pain (CNAP), supported by the Danish National Research Foundation (Grant number: DNRF121)."],"id":"S01-000.00-770752","identifier":[{"id":"85208171367","type":"scopus"},{"id":"39497325","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["aau-9c2287da-e7b1-46aa-b7e1-ce601cb24def"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-DFA53704B2A8909B936F0EA92830D0AE"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC 4.0","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1002/ejp.4749","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC 4.0","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/769153889/Danielsen_et_al._2025_._Pain-related_impairment_in_daily_activities_after_lung_cancer_surgery_-_A_1-year_prospective_cohort_study.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Aalborg University Hospital","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Aalborg University Hospital, The Department of Cardiovascular Surgery","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Allan V.","key":"danielsenpau","last":"Danielsen","locid":"62558cbd-9413-448b-bd5b-3b5757700912","name":"Danielsen, Allan Vestergaard","name_org":"Danielsen, Allan V.","orcid":"0000-0002-3025-7873","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jan J.","key":"andreasenpau","last":"Andreasen","locid":"64f82f01-dc7b-4ed4-873a-940774d8921e","name":"Andreasen, Jan Jesper","name_org":"Andreasen, Jan J.","orcid":"0000-0002-2382-3734","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Birthe","key":"dinesenpau","last":"Dinesen","locid":"22de2dad-03e3-4bc9-8d55-94736e7d5941","name":"Dinesen, Birthe","orcid":"0000-0001-5893-9676","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"John","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","locid":"ae89da32-d0ea-4a39-8295-a7cc351013f6","name":"Hansen, John","orcid":"0000-0003-4989-8117","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Kristian K.","key":"petersenpau","last":"Petersen","locid":"03b38a92-c53c-4b31-a786-05e4893a3e14","name":"Petersen, Kristian Kjær","name_org":"Petersen, Kristian K.","orcid":"0000-0003-4506-000X","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Kirsten S.","key":"duchpau","last":"Duch","locid":"952b4bf9-4968-4e9f-8f30-204e8c36d539","name":"Duch, Kirsten","name_org":"Duch, Kirsten S.","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Carsten","key":"simonsenpau","last":"Simonsen","locid":"3dd5ccae-c8de-43a9-bbaf-37118d8cc1f5","name":"Simonsen, Carsten","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Lars","key":"arendtnielsenpau","last":"Arendt-Nielsen","locid":"1794f9ec-22f1-47af-96c1-88c23c3b06a2","name":"Arendt-Nielsen, Lars","orcid":"0000-0003-0892-1579","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["39497325"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1002/ejp.4749","issn":["10903801","15322149"],"issn_org":["10903801"],"issue":"3","journal":"European Journal of Pain","paperid":"e4749","publisher":"Wiley","status":"p","title":"European Journal of Pain","volume":"29"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85208171367"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-9c2287da-e7b1-46aa-b7e1-ce601cb24def"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Pain-related impairment in daily activities after lung cancer surgery: A 1-year prospective cohort study","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-770752","year":"2025","yearsub":"2025"}
{"abstract":"Transgender and gender diverse (TGD) individuals face numerous challenges in their daily lives, including a higher prevalence of mental health issues and lower quality of life (QoL) levels compared to cisgender individuals. A common intervention shown to have a positive effect on mental well-being and QoL of TGD individuals is gender-affirming hormone therapy (GAHT). However, the short- and long-term outcomes of GAHT on mental health and QoL are not yet fully explored. Therefore, this study aimed to investigate QoL both in individuals assigned male at birth (AMAB) and individuals assigned female at birth (AFAB) receiving GAHT, and control groups not receiving GAHT. Additionally, this study aimed to investigate the relationship between sex hormone levels and QoL outcomes.This study used a cross-sectional design. TGD individuals were recruited from the Centre for Gender Identity, Aalborg University Hospital. The WHOQOL-BREF questionnaire was used to investigate four QoL domains. MANOVA and post-hoc t-tests were performed to analyse QoL domain scores between the GAHT- and control groups. Additionally, linear regression analyses were performed to examine the relationship between QoL scores and levels of oestradiol and testosterone for AMAB and AFAB individuals, respectively.360 individuals were included in the study. Individuals receiving GAHT had significantly higher QoL scores than controls for both the AMAB (p = 0.005) and AFAB (p = 0.021) group, with the largest differences observed in the psychological domain (D2). AFAB individuals had significantly higher QoL scores than AMAB individuals in both the GAHT and control groups (p = 0.010; p = 0.042, respectively), with a notable difference in the social domain (D3) within the GAHT group. No significant linear relationship was found between sex hormone levels and QoL scores.TGD individuals receiving GAHT had significantly higher QoL than those not receiving GAHT. Also, a higher QoL was found for individuals AFAB compared to individuals AMAB. This study highlights the advantages of offering GAHT to TGD individuals and differences based on assigned sex at birth. However, future longitudinal studies are crucial to investigate the short- and long-term effects of GAHT.None.","author_count":9,"contributors":["Petersen, Emma Elisabeth Skovby","Kiy, F","Kesmodel, Ulrik Schiøler","Pop, Maria Lucia","Telléus, Gry Kjærsdam","Stensballe, Allan","Dal, Jakob","Højgaard, Astrid Ditte","Winterdahl, Michael"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-814573"],"event":{"end":"2025-02-25","place":"Wien, at","start":"2025-02-20","title":"European Society for Sexual Medicine (ESSM) Congress 2025","year":"2025"},"filters":{"added":"2025-08","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"relationship between gender affirming hormone therapy and quality of life among transgender individuals","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dca","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-814573","ids":["aau-772d9a17-1c90-4eae-be86-e8973822d514"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-2-9DACDE8C9DFFBE314167A1FC75805206"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Aalborg University Hospital","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Aalborg University Hospital, Sexological Centre"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"E","key":"petersenpau","last":"Petersen","locid":"9ce460ef-5441-4f6e-a966-5424a4d839d2","name":"Petersen, Emma Elisabeth Skovby","name_org":"Petersen, E","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"F","key":"kiypau","last":"Kiy","locid":"2f2aaff3-cbbb-4537-b9ec-6cb358a0317d","name":"Kiy, F","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"U S","key":"kesmodelpau","last":"Kesmodel","locid":"874905db-9134-43c7-83be-94f4fc6d8b62","name":"Kesmodel, Ulrik Schiøler","name_org":"Kesmodel, U S","orcid":"0000-0003-3868-106X","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"M L","key":"poppau","last":"Pop","locid":"680123db-f301-4313-8320-89cda9ede2b1","name":"Pop, Maria Lucia","name_org":"Pop, M L","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"G Kjaersdam","key":"telléuspau","last":"Telléus","locid":"156daec5-475f-48d0-aee8-4bfcf2cb7941","name":"Telléus, Gry Kjærsdam","name_org":"Telléus, G Kjaersdam","orcid":"0000-0003-2329-3988","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"A","key":"stensballepau","last":"Stensballe","locid":"31ce2dbc-d5bc-4266-8c26-1b38838c7346","name":"Stensballe, Allan","name_org":"Stensballe, A","orcid":"0000-0002-9888-1955","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"J","key":"dalpau","last":"Dal","locid":"2e86cdf8-de5b-4bcf-b705-d5ac5f184cf2","name":"Dal, Jakob","name_org":"Dal, J","orcid":"0000-0002-0610-7867","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"A","key":"højgaardpau","last":"Højgaard","locid":"b29eeeec-d1b1-4971-afd7-a63fdadaa241","name":"Højgaard, Astrid Ditte","name_org":"Højgaard, A","orcid":"0000-0002-8866-8181","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"M","key":"winterdahlpau","last":"Winterdahl","locid":"d71237b0-810c-4582-9898-ca5503b724ad","name":"Winterdahl, Michael","name_org":"Winterdahl, M","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1093/jsxmed/qdaf077.261","issn":["17436095","17436109"],"issn_org":["17436095"],"issue":"Suppl. 2","journal":"Journal of Sexual Medicine","paperid":"qdaf077.261","publisher":"Oxford University Press","status":"p","title":"Journal of Sexual Medicine","volume":"22"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-772d9a17-1c90-4eae-be86-e8973822d514"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Relationship between gender-affirming hormone therapy and quality of life among transgender individuals","type":"Conference Abstract","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-814573","year":"2025","yearsub":"2025"}
{"abstract":"Plastic accumulation has become a major global concern due to the lack of efficient and environmentally friendly strategies to manage the end-of-life of these materials. Among the most used families of plastics is polyurethane (PU), which is valued for its versatility and low production cost. A promising strategy to address the end-of-life challenges of PU is employing efficient PU-degrading enzymes. Notably, an extracellular lipase from the I.3 family originating from Pseudomonas sp. MIS38 has shown significant promise in this regard. In this study, we investigated the enzyme’s capability to hydrolyze a PU fragment. Employing QM/MM computational methodologies, we studied the hydrolysis mechanism of MIS38 lipase and found it to follow the prototypical serine esterase mechanism involving acylation and deacylation stages. The rate-limiting step occurred between the formation of the acyl-enzyme intermediate and the formation of the second tetrahedral intermediate. The Gibbs activation barrier for this step was 19.67 kcal·mol–1, confirming the lipase’s potential to biodegrade PU efficiently. More importantly, we observed that the enzyme preferentially cleaved the C–N bond instead of the C–O bond. This preference was due to the arrangement of the active site and the substrate, which made C–N the more favorable cleavable site. Furthermore, we find that the C–O group is not a suitable cleavable bond due to steric hindrances. This study suggests that the mechanism of urethane bond hydrolysis is more complex than currently assumed because bond cleavage is context-dependent and may differ depending on the enzyme and the substrate.","author_count":12,"contributors":["Teixeira, Luís M.C.","Paiva, Pedro","Johansen, Martin B.","Sommerfeldt, Andreas","Petersen, Allan R.","Rotilio, Laura","Sandahl, Alexander","Morth, Jens Preben","Westh, Peter","Otzen, Daniel E.","Fernandes, Pedro A.","Ramos, Maria J."],"cuid":["S01-000.00-827466"],"filters":{"added":"2025-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Portugal"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","University of Porto"],"keyword":["Catalysis","Enzyme","Hydrolase","Lipase","Plastic","Polyurethane","QM MM"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"hydrolysis of the urethane bond catalyzed by i pseudomonas i sp mis000000000038 lipase a qm mm mechanistic insight","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/105013485495","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-827466","identifier":[{"id":"105013485495","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-3154569e-b6dc-435a-993b-14d76a8faa61"],"keyword":["Catalysis","Enzyme","Hydrolase","Lipase","PURase","Plastic","Polyurethane","QM/MM"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-BDAEF30E29AA9268A43CDD92CDCE3FC5"],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"pt","key":"university of porto","loc":["Portugal","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Porto","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Biotechnology and Biomedicine","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Biotechnology and Biomedicine, Section for Protein Chemistry and Enzyme Technology","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Biotechnology and Biomedicine, Section for Protein Chemistry and Enzyme Technology, DTU Structural Biology Core","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Biotechnology and Biomedicine, Section for Protein Chemistry and Enzyme Technology, Structural Enzymology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Luís M.C.","key":"teixeirapau","last":"Teixeira","name":"Teixeira, Luís M.C.","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Pedro","key":"paivapau","last":"Paiva","name":"Paiva, Pedro","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Martin B.","key":"johansenpau","last":"Johansen","name":"Johansen, Martin B.","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Andreas","key":"sommerfeldtpau","last":"Sommerfeldt","name":"Sommerfeldt, Andreas","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Allan R.","key":"petersenpau","last":"Petersen","name":"Petersen, Allan R.","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Laura","key":"rotiliopau","last":"Rotilio","locid":"5302aebd-6243-4275-871b-ea4c5d002423","name":"Rotilio, Laura","orcid":"0000-0001-5260-6483","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Alexander","key":"sandahlpau","last":"Sandahl","name":"Sandahl, Alexander","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"J. Preben","key":"morthpau","last":"Morth","locid":"5c6aef5e-424e-4d99-8a1f-ba28b86e759b","name":"Morth, Jens Preben","name_org":"Morth, J. Preben","orcid":"0000-0003-4077-0192","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Peter","key":"westhpau","last":"Westh","locid":"dde168d3-8694-4a17-84f3-afeb385e96bd","name":"Westh, Peter","orcid":"0000-0002-6185-0637","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Daniel E.","key":"otzenpau","last":"Otzen","name":"Otzen, Daniel E.","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Pedro A.","key":"fernandespau","last":"Fernandes","name":"Fernandes, Pedro A.","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Maria J.","key":"ramospau","last":"Ramos","name":"Ramos, Maria J.","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1021/acscatal.5c03228","issn":["21555435"],"journal":"ACS Catalysis","pages":"14728-14740","publisher":"American Chemical Society","status":"p","title":"ACS Catalysis","volume":"15"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-105013485495"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-3154569e-b6dc-435a-993b-14d76a8faa61"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Hydrolysis of the Urethane Bond Catalyzed by <i>Pseudomonas</i> sp. MIS38 Lipase : A QM/MM Mechanistic Insight","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-827466","year":"2025","yearsub":"2025"}
{"abstract":"Severe intestinal mucositis (IM) increases the risk of bloodstream infections (BSI) and inflammatory toxicity during acute lymphoblastic leukaemia (ALL) induction treatment. However, the implications of IM in subsequent ALL therapy phases after achieving remission remain unknown. This study investigated the relationship between IM (measured by plasma citrulline and the chemokine CCL20) and the development of BSI and systemic inflammation (reflected by C-reactive protein, CRP) in children with ALL during high-dose methotrexate (HDMTX) treatment, an important part of ALL consolidation therapy. The study compared patients treated according to the NOPHO ALL 2008 protocol (n = 52) and the ALLTogether1 protocol (n = 42), both with identical HDMTX procedures but different scheduling. One week post-HDMTX, citrulline dropped to median levels of 14.5 and 16.9 μM for patients treated according to the NOPHO ALL 2008 and ALLTogether1 protocols, respectively (p = 0.11). In a protocol and neutrophil count-adjusted analysis, hypocitrullinaemia (<10 μmol/L) was associated with increased odds of BSI within 3 weeks from HDMTX (OR = 26.2, p = 0.0074). Patients treated according to the NOPHO ALL 2008 protocol exhibited increased mucosal- and systemic inflammation post-HDMTX compared to patients treated according to ALLTogether1, with increased CCL20 (14.6 vs. 3.7 pg/mL, p < 0.0001) and CRP levels (10.0 vs. 1.0 mg/L, p < 0.0001). Both citrulline and CCL20 correlated with CRP for these patients (rs = −0.44, p = 0.0016 and rs = 0.35, p = 0.016, respectively). These results suggest that hypocitrullinaemia following HDMTX increases the risk of BSI, confirming previous observations from more intensive treatments. Moreover, these data indicate that the patients' vulnerability to mucositis and inflammatory toxicity after chemotherapy varies with treatment protocol.","author_count":12,"contributors":["Weischendorff, Sarah","de Pietri, Silvia","Rathe, Mathias","Schmiegelow, Kjeld","Frandsen, Thomas Leth","Petersen, Malene Johanne","Weimann, Allan","Nielsen, Claus Henrik","Enevold, Christian","Kocadag, Helin Berna","Moser, Claus","Müller, Klaus"],"cuid":["S02-088.68-785452"],"filters":{"added":"2025-02","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"corresponding_author":["Weischendorff, Sarah"],"keyword":["Acute lymphoblastic leukaemia","Adolescent","Antineoplastic Combined Chemotherapy Protocols adverse effects","Bloodstream infections","C Reactive Protein analysis","CCL20","Child","Child Preschool","Citrulline","Female","Humans","Infant","Inflammation","Male","Methotrexate adverse effects","Mucositis chemically induced","Precursor Cell Lymphoblastic Leukemia Lymphoma drug therapy","Systemic inflammation","high dose methotrexate","intestinal mucositis"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"intestinal mucositis systemic inflammation and bloodstream infections following high dose methotrexate treatment in childhood acute lymphoblastic leukaemia comparison between the nopho all 000000002008 protocol and the alltogether000000000001 protocol","src":["ku","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1002/ijc.35136","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-088.68-785452","identifier":[{"id":"85201260159","type":"scopus"},{"id":"39150399","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-579a408c-072a-4294-95ad-efc6fd123dc2","sdu-52fddf8c-d97c-4edb-ad3f-bc181f6eb848"],"keyword":["Adolescent","Antineoplastic Combined Chemotherapy Protocols/adverse effects","C-Reactive Protein/analysis","CCL20","Child","Child, Preschool","Citrulline","Female","Humans","Infant","Inflammation","Male","Methotrexate/adverse effects","Mucositis/chemically induced","Precursor Cell Lymphoblastic Leukemia-Lymphoma/drug therapy","acute lymphoblastic leukaemia","bloodstream infections","high-dose methotrexate","intestinal mucositis","systemic inflammation"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-9A097A58209F3597E92252C739C1D837"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/411638560/Intl_Journal_of_Cancer_2024_Weischendorff_Intestinal_mucositis_systemic_inflammation_and_bloodstream_infections.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/276022738/Intl_Journal_of_Cancer_-_2024_-_Weischendorff_-_Intestinal_mucositis_systemic_inflammation_and_bloodstream_infections.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1002/ijc.35136","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital - Rigshospitalet"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research","SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research, KI, OUH, Research unit of Paediatrics (Odense)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities