"title":"Relationship Between Gender-Affirming Hormone Therapy, Quality of Life, and Sex Hormone Concentrations in Transgender Individuals","type":"Conference Abstract","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-814853","year":"2025","yearsub":"2025"}
{"abstract":"AIMS: The aim of this study was to compare the final approval decision and time from submission to final decision for new drug applications and applications for extension of indications to the EMA and the FDA within cancer drugs. METHODS: We performed a retrospective analysis on antineoplastic drug applications with a final decision in both the EMA and the FDA from January 1, 2018, to December 31, 2022. For each included drug application, we collected data from the EMA website and the Drugs@FDA database. RESULTS: A total of 48 new drug applications and 94 applications for extension were included. Agreement in the final decision between the EMA and the FDA was found in 94% of new drug applications and 96% of applications for extension. For new drug applications, the time from submission to approval in the EMA and the FDA were median (interquartile range, IQR) 424 (394-481) days and 216 (169-243) days, respectively. For extensions, the median time from submission to approval in the EMA and the FDA were 295 (245-348) days and 176 (140-183) days, respectively. CONCLUSIONS: We found a high agreement in final approval decisions for cancer drug applications between the EMA and the FDA both for new drug applications and applications for extension. The time from submission to the final decision was markedly shorter in the FDA than in the EMA, albeit the difference was smaller for extensions than for new drug applications. The results indicate that the longer time from submission to decision in the EMA than in the FDA has limited influence on the final approval decisions.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Cramer, Allan","Sørup, Freja Karuna Hemmingsen","Christensen, Hanne Rolighed","Petersen, Tonny Studsgaard","Karstoft, Kristian"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-818525"],"filters":{"added":"2025-08","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"cancer drug applications to the ema and the fda a comparison of new drugs and extension of indication in terms of approval decisions and time in review","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1111/bcp.16391","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-818525","identifier":[{"id":"39777429","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC12035586","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"85214533068","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-0e126a37-aab0-43b5-adf2-52db6eec852a"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-200AD375C9DE52E302EAC8D9D04C6119"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1111/bcp.16391","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/451243331/Brit_J_Clinical_Pharma_-_2025_-_Cramer_-_Cancer_drug_applications_to_the_EMA_and_the_FDA_A_comparison_of_new_drugs_and.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital - Bispebjerg and Frederiksberg"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Clinical Pharmacology","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Allan","key":"cramerpau","last":"Cramer","name":"Cramer, Allan","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Freja Karuna Hemmingsen","key":"søruppau","last":"Sørup","name":"Sørup, Freja Karuna Hemmingsen","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Hanne Rolighed","key":"christensenpau","last":"Christensen","name":"Christensen, Hanne Rolighed","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","first":"Tonny Studsgaard","key":"petersenpau","last":"Petersen","locid":"95e21f85-7cd9-443d-88c7-cc0b6e7bc844","name":"Petersen, Tonny Studsgaard","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","first":"Kristian","key":"karstoftpau","last":"Karstoft","locid":"80f306e9-a560-493c-b7d4-4e18b694660f","name":"Karstoft, Kristian","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["39777429"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1111/bcp.16391","issn":["02643774","03065251"],"issn_org":["02643774"],"issue":"5","journal":"British Journal of Clinical Pharmacology","pages":"1431-1438","status":"p","title":"British Journal of Clinical Pharmacology","volume":"91"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85214533068"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-0e126a37-aab0-43b5-adf2-52db6eec852a"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Cancer drug applications to the EMA and the FDA : A comparison of new drugs and extension of indication in terms of approval decisions and time in review","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-818525","year":"2025","yearsub":"2025"}
{"abstract":"Objectives: The present study examines the quality of life (QoL) of transgender and gender-diverse individuals receiving versus not receiving gender-affirming hormone therapy (GAHT) in those assigned male at birth (AMAB) and assigned female at birth (AFAB). It also explores the relationship between QoL and concentrations of oestradiol and testosterone. Methods: This cross-sectional study used the WHOQOL-BREF questionnaire to assess QoL. Participants were categorised into four groups based on assigned sex at birth (AMAB or AFAB) and GAHT status, with non-GAHT participants serving as controls. MANOVA and t-tests were used to compare QoL between groups, and linear regression analyses examined associations between QoL and oestradiol/ testosterone concentrations in AMAB and AFAB participants. Results: The study included 360 participants: 169 AMAB (143 receiving GAHT and 26 controls) and 191 AFAB (141 receiving GAHT and 50 controls). GAHT recipients had significantly higher QoL than controls in both AMAB (p < 0.01) and AFAB (p = 0.02) groups, particularly in the psychological health domain (D2). AFAB participants reported higher overall QoL than AMAB in both GAHT (p = 0.01) and control (p = 0.04) groups, with significance in the social relationship domain among GAHT participants. No significant relationship was found between oestradiol concentrations and QoL for participants AMAB. However, a significant relationship between testosterone concentrations and QoL was observed only in the social relationship domain (D3) for participant AFAB. Conclusion: This study highlights the benefits of GAHT for QoL and differences in QoL between individuals AMAB and AFAB.","author_count":9,"contributors":["Petersen, Emma Elisabeth Skovby","Kiy, F","Kesmodel, Ulrik Schiøler","Pop, Maria Lucia","Telléus, Gry Kjærsdam","Stensballe, Allan","Dal, Jakob","Højgaard, Astrid Ditte","Winterdahl, Michael"],"cuid":["S02-100.00-813459"],"filters":{"added":"2025-08","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"corresponding_author":["Petersen, E. E.S."],"keyword":["Gonadal Steroid Hormones","Oestradiol","Quality of Life","Testosterone","Transgender Persons"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-NDR"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-NDR","DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"gender affirming hormone therapy quality of life and the role of oestradiol and testosterone in transgender individuals","src":["aau","au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1017/neu.2025.10018","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-100.00-813459","identifier":[{"id":"105007513485","type":"scopus"},{"id":"40468835","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["aau-c95a472a-acd4-464b-9de1-227d0707637e","au-eb5f7b59-11af-4c3a-8e3b-1d948373ccbb"],"keyword":["Gonadal Steroid Hormones","Oestradiol","Quality of life","Testosterone","Transgender persons"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-F231CA571714F5C15F607C4FAE63AE4C"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1017/neu.2025.10018","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Aalborg University Hospital","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Aalborg University Hospital, Sexological Centre"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"north denmark region","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"