{"author_count":7,"contributors":["Sperling, Phillip Kaasgaard","Vollert, J.","Giordano, Rocco","Danielsen, Allan Vestergaard","Rasmussen, Bodil Steen","Bisgaard, Jannie","Petersen, Kristian Kjær"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-814864"],"event":{"end":"2025-04-26","place":"Lyon, fr","start":"2025-04-24","title":"EFIC Congress 2025 – Pain in Europe XIV. The 14th Congress of the European Pain Federation EFIC","year":"2025"},"filters":{"added":"2025-08","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"country":["United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","University of Exeter"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"predicting chronic postsurgical pain following video assisted thoracoscopic surgery an exploratory analysis of predictors and prediction models","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dca","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://europeanpainfederation.eu/wp-content/uploads/2025/06/ABSTRACT-BOOK-EFIC-2025_Final.pdf","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-814864","ids":["aau-caece6ef-6870-43d3-a22b-3975e96d5ef4"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Local-1-1-4CA96F7D75ADAD5AFE42E93CF39BA4AF"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Aalborg University Hospital","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Aalborg University Hospital, Department of Anaesthesiology and Intensive Care","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Department of Health Science and Technology","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Department of Health Science and Technology, Center for Neuroplasticity and Pain","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Department of Health Science and Technology, Translational Pain Neuroscience and Precision Health"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"gb","key":"university of exeter","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Exeter","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Phillip Kaasgaard","key":"sperlingpau","last":"Sperling","locid":"b879adbf-3b17-499e-9304-d651c181f265","name":"Sperling, Phillip Kaasgaard","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"J.","key":"vollertpau","last":"Vollert","name":"Vollert, J.","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Rocco","key":"giordanopau","last":"Giordano","locid":"201beefd-2ee8-4758-9607-6a6da835d1ca","name":"Giordano, Rocco","orcid":"0000-0003-1331-129X","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Allan Vestergaard","key":"danielsenpau","last":"Danielsen","locid":"62558cbd-9413-448b-bd5b-3b5757700912","name":"Danielsen, Allan Vestergaard","orcid":"0000-0002-3025-7873","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Bodil Steen","key":"rasmussenpau","last":"Rasmussen","locid":"3162c449-94c3-4d28-8dbb-c134d6eb76e1","name":"Rasmussen, Bodil Steen","orcid":"0000-0003-2190-145X","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jannie","key":"bisgaardpau","last":"Bisgaard","locid":"e1e14c45-509f-4834-8090-e614d309986b","name":"Bisgaard, Jannie","orcid":"0000-0001-6499-9691","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Kristian Kjær-Staal","key":"petersenpau","last":"Petersen","locid":"03b38a92-c53c-4b31-a786-05e4893a3e14","name":"Petersen, Kristian Kjær","name_org":"Petersen, Kristian Kjær-Staal","orcid":"0000-0003-4506-000X","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"pages":"382-383","status":"p","subtitle":"Comorbidity of Chronic Pain and Mental Health Disorders: Breaking the Cycle","title":"Abstract Book 14th Congress of The European Pain Federation EFIC"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-caece6ef-6870-43d3-a22b-3975e96d5ef4"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Predicting Chronic Postsurgical Pain Following Video-Assisted Thoracoscopic Surgery : An Exploratory Analysis of Predictors and Prediction Models","type":"Conference Abstract","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-814864","year":"2025","yearsub":"2025"}
{"abstract":"Objectives: Several studies have observed associations between unfavorable levels of blood glucose metabolic markers (i.e., fasting glucose, fasting insulin, glycated hemoglobin (HbA1c), and insulin resistance (HOMA-IR)) and functional somatic disorder (FSD). However, such associations have not yet been systematically analyzed in a general population-based sample using various FSD delimitations simultaneously. The aim of this study was to assess whether an unfavorable glucose metabolism is associated with FSD. Design: Cross-sectional population-based study Setting: Ten municipalities in the western part of greater Copenhagen area in Denmark Participants: A total of 8183 men and women aged 18–76 years were included. Various delimitations of FSD, i.e., chronic fatigue (CF), chronic widespread pain (CWP), irritable bowel (IB), and bodily distress syndrome (BDS), were measured using validated self-administrated questionnaires. In a stratified subsample, BDS was also assessed by diagnostic interviews. Outcome measures: Logistic regression models were estimated for each delimitation of FSD as outcome and fasting glucose, fasting insulin, HbA1c, and estimated insulin resistance. Results were adjusted for age, sex (model 1), lifestyle, and social factors (model 2) and presented as odds ratios (OR) with 95 % confidence intervals (CI). Results: When only adjusting for sex and age, positive associations were found between all FSD delimitations and glucose, insulin, and HbA1c, except for between IB and HbA1c. Positive associations were also found between all questionnaire-based BDS groups, and men with BDS confirmed by diagnostic interviews and elevated insulin resistance. After adjusting for lifestyle and social factors, associations remained significant between both CF and glucose and HbA1c and between multi-organ BDS and glucose and HbA1c. Further, CF, single-organ BDS, multi-organ BDS, and women with overall-BDS also remained associated with increased levels of insulin resistance. Conclusion: FSD seems to be associated with especially an increase in plasma insulin levels and increased levels of insulin resistance. Elevated levels of blood glucose and HbA1c among all FSD groups could also completely be explained by unhealthy lifestyle. Prospective studies are needed for further clarification of the clinical relevance of this observation.","author_count":11,"contributors":["Dantoft, Thomas Meinertz","Jørgensen, Sine Wanda","Wellnitz, Kaare Bro","Ørnbøl, Eva","Gormsen, Lise Kirstine","Fink, Per","Linneberg, Allan","Jørgensen, Niklas Rye","Petersen, Marie Weinreich","Bjerregaard, Anne Ahrendt","Jørgensen, Torben"],"cuid":["S02-100.00-785074"],"filters":{"added":"2025-02","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"corresponding_author":["Dantoft, Thomas Meinertz"],"keyword":["Cross sectional population based study","Epidemiology","Functional somatic disorders","Glucose metabolism","Insulin Resistance"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-ZEA"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-ZEA","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"unfavourable glucose metabolism is associated with functional somatic disorders a cross sectional general population based study the danfund study","src":["au","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.psyneuen.2024.107258","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-100.00-785074","identifier":[{"id":"39673833","type":"pmid"},{"id":"001388680600001","type":"wos"},{"id":"85211749709","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-4d6fbabe-8c92-4f15-8f45-f2e1c6eb602d","ku-9268f72a-67c4-4cc6-8050-d0a9e631c279"],"keyword":["Cross-sectional population-based study","Epidemiology","Functional somatic disorders","Glucose metabolism","Insulin resistance"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-097043B1FC606E7D0B5C967C3C9CBC68"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.psyneuen.2024.107258","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/416572839/1_s2.0_S0306453024003032_main.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Bispebjerg og Frederiksberg Universitets Hospital"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"region zealand","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-ZEA","l3nl":"Region Zealand","l3nn":"Region Zealand","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Region Zealand","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital - Næstved, Slagelse and Ringsted"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-ZEA","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - Clinic for Functional Disorder"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"4","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Internal Medicine: Geriatrics"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Thomas Meinertz","key":"dantoftthomasmeinertzpau","last":"Dantoft","name":"Dantoft, Thomas Meinertz","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Sine Wanda","key":"jørgensensinewandapau","last":"Jørgensen","name":"Jørgensen, Sine Wanda","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Kaare Bro","key":"wellnitzkaarebropau","last":"Wellnitz","locid":"b8b866d1-0a6f-4a5f-a956-fa0e76b877ac","name":"Wellnitz, Kaare Bro","orcid":"0000-0001-5882-5118","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Eva","key":"ørnbølevapau","last":"Ørnbøl","locid":"e781e74a-aaa8-439f-ae9f-274a3abb6dae","name":"Ørnbøl, Eva","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Lise","key":"gormsenlisekirstinepau","last":"Gormsen","locid":"5516e253-cc95-468b-b53d-b6d1758f9884","name":"Gormsen, Lise Kirstine","name_org":"Gormsen, Lise","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Per","key":"finkperpau","last":"Fink","locid":"22d646ca-5dee-456c-ae39-6c0687a18ce8","name":"Fink, Per","orcid":"0000-0003-2921-4099","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 4","first":"Allan","key":"linnebergallanpau","last":"Linneberg","locid":"09da8aa6-fd95-4ace-a2f1-19f38d7d3f9e","name":"Linneberg, Allan","orcid":"0000-0002-0994-0184","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4 1","first":"Niklas Rye","key":"jørgensenniklasryepau","last":"Jørgensen","locid":"3dc68a95-e26c-4b82-a4f0-7548313f8045","name":"Jørgensen, Niklas Rye","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Marie Weinreich","key":"petersenmarieweinreichpau","last":"Petersen","locid":"9dacce30-6a88-4fa2-a71a-87cccaf540af","name":"Petersen, Marie Weinreich","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Anne Ahrendt","key":"bjerregaardanneahrendtpau","last":"Bjerregaard","name":"Bjerregaard, Anne Ahrendt","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 4","first":"Torben","key":"jørgensentorbenpau","last":"Jørgensen","locid":"368044df-7d2b-4204-9103-8c0272f1baca","name":"Jørgensen, Torben","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["39673833"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.psyneuen.2024.107258","issn":["03064530","18733360"],"issn_org":["03064530"],"journal":"Psychoneuroendocrinology","paperid":"107258","publisher":"Elsevier Ltd","status":"p","title":"Psychoneuroendocrinology","volume":"172"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85211749709"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","Central Denmark Region","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Region Zealand","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-4d6fbabe-8c92-4f15-8f45-f2e1c6eb602d","ku-9268f72a-67c4-4cc6-8050-d0a9e631c279"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Unfavourable glucose metabolism is associated with functional somatic disorders. A cross-sectional general population-based study : The DanFunD study","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-100.00-785074","year":"2025","yearsub":"2025"}
{"abstract":"Aim of the study: This study aimed to apply a Bayesian probabilistic framework to the Intravenous vs. Intraosseous Vascular Access for Out-of-Hospital Cardiac Arrest (IVIO) trial data to evaluate the likelihood of benefit for each vascular access method while incorporating various prior beliefs. Methods: The IVIO trial was a randomised trial comparing intraosseous to intravenous access in 1,479 adults with non-traumatic out-of-hospital cardiac arrest. Bayesian analyses were pre-planned in the protocol and conducted using both non-informative and informative priors to calculate posterior probabilities for sustained return of spontaneous circulation, 30-day survival, and 30-day survival with a favourable neurologic outcome. Results: Using non-informative priors for return of spontaneous circulation, the posterior probabilities that the effect of either vascular access exceeds the hypothesised difference were 1.2% (risk ratio > 1.27, favouring intraosseous access) and < 0.1% (risk ratio < 0.79 [1/1.27], favouring intravenous access). For 30-day survival and survival with a favourable neurologic outcome, the posterior probability that the risk ratio for intraosseous compared to intravenous access is between 0.83 (1/1.2) and 1.2 was 58% and 55%, respectively. For all analyses with informative priors, the results did not provide probabilities strongly favouring either intraosseous or intravenous access. Conclusions: The probability of a clinically meaningful difference in return of spontaneous circulation between intraosseous and intravenous access for out-of-hospital cardiac arrest was very low, while results for 30-day outcomes were uncertain, with no strong evidence favouring either method. Trial registration: EU Clinical Trials number: 2022-500744-38-00. ClinicalTrials.gov number: NCT05205031.","author_count":50,"contributors":["Fink Vallentin, Mikael","Holmberg, Mathias J","Granfeldt, Asger","Klitgaard, Thomas Lass","Mikkelsen, Søren","Folke, Fredrik","Christensen, Helle Collatz","Povlsen, Amalie Ling","Petersen, Alberthe Hjort","Winther, Sofie","Frilund, Lea Wildt","Meilandt, Carsten","Winther, Kristian Blumensaadt","Bach, Allan","Dissing, Thomas H","Terkelsen, Christian Juhl","Christensen, Steffen","Rasmussen, Line Kirkegaard","Mortensen, Lone Riis","Loldrup, Mads Ladefoged","Elkmann, Thomas","Nielsen, Anders Gunnar","Runge, Charlotte","Klæstrup, Elise","Holm, Jimmy Højberg","Bak, Mikkel","Nielsen, Lars-Gustav Rahbek","Pedersen, Mette","Kjærgaard-Andersen, Gunhild","Hansen, Peter Martin","Brøchner, Anne Craveiro","Christensen, Erika Frischknecht","Nielsen, Frederik Mølgaard","Nissen, Christian Gade","Bjørn, Jeppe Waldstrøm","Burholt, Peter","Obling, Laust E R","Duus Holle, Sarah Louise","Russell, Lene","Alstrøm, Henrik","Hestad, Søren","Fogtmann, Tanja Hesse","Hove Buciek, Jens Ulrik","Jakobsen, Karina","Krag, Mette","Sandgaard, Michael","Sindberg, Birthe","Andersen, Lars W"],"cuid":["S04-099.92-813490"],"filters":{"added":"2025-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":4,"corresponding_author":["Andersen, Lars W."],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-NDR","DI-HO-OTH","DI-HO-SDR","DI-HO-ZEA"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-NDR","DI-HO-OTH","DI-HO-SDR","DI-HO-ZEA","DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"intraosseous vs intravenous access during out of hospital cardiac arrest a bayesian secondary analysis of a randomised clinical trial","src":["aau","au","ku","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.resuscitation.2025.110634","version":"Published Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["Trial funding was provided by the Novo Nordisk Foundation, the Tryg Foundation, Aarhus University, The Independent Research Fund Denmark, and Snedkermester Sophus Jacobsen og hustru Astrid Jacobsens Fond through The Danish Heart Foundation."],"id":"S04-099.92-813490","identifier":[{"id":"40348355","type":"pmid"},{"id":"105005228141","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-e68c8f10-9ad1-4a01-81de-4b51369bfa46","au-fa2050a7-514f-4a11-addf-730b6ac997fa","ku-27f32f4c-65d5-48ad-803c-0a6d145e6b9e","sdu-3d826c1e-e5ba-45a1-82b6-7444dcfa4c2d"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-6-3478607746F2D1002A6CAC4A0495B7EF"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.resuscitation.2025.110634","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY 4.0","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/792002317/Vallentin_et_al._2025_Intraosseous_vs._intravenous_access_during_out-of-hospital_cardiac_arrest.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/451610723/1-s2.0-S0300957225001467-main.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/290905516/Open_Access_Version.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - Anaesthesiology and Operation, Intensive care","Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - Præhospitalet"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"central denmark region","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CDR"