"O. B.","key":"petersenolavbjørnpau","last":"Petersen","locid":"14bd27e7-8ad4-4a3a-9e27-33f17addfee4","name":"Petersen, Olav Bjørn","name_org":"Petersen, O. B.","rank":15,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["37743648"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1002/uog.27497","issn":["09607692","14690705"],"issn_org":["14690705"],"issue":"4","journal":"Ultrasound in obstetrics & gynecology : the official journal of the International Society of Ultrasound in Obstetrics and Gynecology","pages":"514-521","publisher":"John Wiley and Sons Ltd","status":"p","title":"Ultrasound in obstetrics & gynecology : the official journal of the International Society of Ultrasound in Obstetrics and Gynecology","title_org":"Ultrasound in Obstetrics & Gynecology","volume":"63"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85189209517"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","Central Denmark Region","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","North Denmark Region","Region of Southern Denmark","Universities","University of Copenhagen","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-ab055300-b0c6-46ef-abee-9410d8a4ea74","au-7f21f002-6d76-44c3-8222-25e68a63678a","ku-11eea924-da4e-4ff2-a782-a61c1a560aab","sdu-c7b60bcf-6413-406b-a5e4-7e2d60255a50"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University","AU Aarhus University","KU University of Copenhagen","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Quadruplet pregnancy outcome with and without fetal reduction: Danish national cohort study 2008-2018 and comparison with dichorionic twins","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S04-094.32-734991","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"BACKGROUND: Recently, in an open pilot study, we found up to two years, a potential pain-relieving effect of intra-articular gold micro-particles using the patient's synovial fluid for patients with knee osteoarthritis (KOA). During the study the excluded group of patients, due to multisite pain, co-morbidities, and other exclusion criteria., received intra-articular gold micro-particles using hyaluronic acid,. We aimed to identify if pre-treatment characteristics influence the global outcome two years after intra-articular treatment for painful KOA with gold microparticles using hyaluronic acid. METHODS: Using hyaluronic acid as the carrier, 136 patients with KOA received intraarticular injections with 20 mg gold microparticles (72.000 particles, 20-40 μm in diameter). In the analysis, we included the Global Rating of Change Scale, Pain Detect Questionnaire (PDQ), Body Mass Index (BMI), and Kellgren & Lawrence score at the inclusion, Western Ontario, and McMaster Universities Osteoarthritis Index (WOMAC) sub-scores for pain, stiffness, and function at inclusion and two years. RESULTS: On the Global Rating Change Scale, 69.1% of patients reported a positive effect, 28.7% no effect, and 2.2% worse. PDQ and the three WOMAC subscores all improved at two years of follow-up. PDQ ≥ 13 (P = 0.028), BMI (P = 0.022) and Kellgren & Lawrence grade 4 (P = 0.028) at inclusion reduced the effect with a minor odds ratio compared to the baseline effect of treatment (P = 0.025). WOMAC subscores at inclusion did not influence the outcome (P > 0.5). CONCLUSIONS: Severe osteoarthritis, obesity, and neuropathic pain, reduced the effect of intra-articular gold microparticles for knee OA. TRIAL REGISTRATION: The study followed the principles of the Declaration of Helsinki and was approved by the local ethics committee of the North Denmark Region by 27/07/2016 (N-20,160,045). The regional data protection agency approved the project by 06/07/2016 (2008-58-0028, ID 2016 - 116) and registered in ClinicalTrial.Gov by 04/01/2018 (NCT03389906).","author_count":8,"contributors":["Rasmussen, Sten","Petersen, Kristian Kjær","Aboo, Christopher","Andersen, Jacob Skallerup","Skjoldemose, Emilie","Jørgensen, Nia Kristine","Stensballe, Allan","Arendt-Nielsen, Lars"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-725608"],"filters":{"added":"2024-05","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Rasmussen, Sten"],"keyword":["Gold microparticles","Hyaluronic acid","Intra articular injection","Knee osteoarthritis","Outcomes"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"intra articular injection of gold micro particles with hyaluronic acid for painful knee osteoarthritis","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY 4.0","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/s12891-024-07321-4","version":"Published Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["Department of Clinical Medicine provided funding for this study. Center for Neuroplasticity and Pain (CNAP) (Lars Arendt-Nielsen) provided funding for this study. CNAP is supported by the Danish National Research Foundation (DNRF121) and the Danish Rheumatism Association (R204-A7645). The Danish National Mass Spectrometry Platform for Functional Proteomics (PRO-MS; grant no. 5072-00007B); The Obelske family foundation, the Svend Andersen Foundation, and the SparNord foundation are acknowledged for grants to the analytical platform, enabling parts of this study."],"id":"S01-000.00-725608","identifier":[{"id":"85187531025","type":"scopus"},{"id":"38475764","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["aau-3a096b64-ba95-46e4-b9fd-b6c0782e6624"],"keyword":["Gold microparticles","Hyaluronic acid","Intra-articular injection","Knee osteoarthritis","Outcomes"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-1DB66E714DD622C24FD23BBB4F6C2ACF"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY 4.0","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/s12891-024-07321-4","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY 4.0","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/678684971/s12891-024-07321-4.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Aalborg University Hospital","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Aalborg University Hospital, Department of Orthopaedic Surgery","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Sten","key":"rasmussenpau","last":"Rasmussen","locid":"05d1d595-13be-4295-8ad1-8d29206859c8","name":"Rasmussen, Sten","orcid":"0000-0002-8664-352X","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Kristian Kjaer","key":"petersenpau","last":"Petersen","locid":"03b38a92-c53c-4b31-a786-05e4893a3e14","name":"Petersen, Kristian Kjær","name_org":"Petersen, Kristian Kjaer","orcid":"0000-0003-4506-000X","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Christopher","key":"aboopau","last":"Aboo","locid":"231dbe9b-9dd3-46c5-86e0-311cda7a37f5","name":"Aboo, Christopher","orcid":"0000-0001-7295-7459","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jacob Skallerup","key":"andersenpau","last":"Andersen","locid":"08c304cd-7865-4f96-9a93-64b48d329321","name":"Andersen, Jacob Skallerup","orcid":"0000-0002-9519-7146","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Emilie","key":"skjoldemosepau","last":"Skjoldemose","locid":"f5a367cb-6a55-4dc4-832e-dd18abea4b5a","name":"Skjoldemose, Emilie","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Nia Kristine","key":"jørgensenpau","last":"Jørgensen","locid":"f8ea96ba-5838-4e30-a004-049bb2fe91a0","name":"Jørgensen, Nia Kristine","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Allan","key":"stensballepau","last":"Stensballe","locid":"31ce2dbc-d5bc-4266-8c26-1b38838c7346","name":"Stensballe, Allan","orcid":"0000-0002-9888-1955","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Lars","key":"arendtnielsenpau","last":"Arendt-Nielsen","locid":"1794f9ec-22f1-47af-96c1-88c23c3b06a2","name":"Arendt-Nielsen, Lars","orcid":"0000-0003-0892-1579","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["38475764"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1186/s12891-024-07321-4","issn":["14712474"],"issue":"1","journal":"BMC Musculoskeletal Disorders","paperid":"211","publisher":"BioMed Central","status":"p","title":"BMC Musculoskeletal Disorders","volume":"25"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85187531025"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-3a096b64-ba95-46e4-b9fd-b6c0782e6624"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Intra-articular injection of gold micro-particles with hyaluronic acid for painful knee osteoarthritis","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-725608","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"Background: Reference intervals covering the whole life span for all the metabolites in the steroid hormone biosynthesis quantified by sensitive and robust analytical methods are sparse or not existing. Objective: To develop a state-of-the-art LC-MS/MS method for simultaneous quantification of multiple steroid metabolites and to establish detailed sex- and age-specific reference intervals for 16 steroid metabolites. Materials and method: An isotope diluted LC-MS/MS method was developed for simultaneous quantitation of 16 steroid hormones. Serum samples from cross-sectional cohorts of healthy infants, children, adolescents, and adults aged 0.17 months to 77 years (n = 2458) were analysed. Results: With this novel, specific, and sensitive LC-MS/MS method, it was possible to quantify progesterone, 17-hydroxypregnenolone, 17-hydroxyprogesterone, dehydroepiandrosterone sulfate, androstenedione, testosterone, dihydrotestosterone, 11-deoxycorticosterone, corticosterone, 11-deoxycortisol, cortisol, and cortisone in ≥90 % of the samples, while estrone sulfate, aldosterone and dehydroepiandrosterone were quantified in 77 %, 75 % and 60 % of the samples, respectively. 21-deoxycortisol was only detectable in 2.5 % of samples from healthy subjects. Sex- and age-dependent fluctuations observed in minipuberty, puberty and adulthood including the menopausal transition were modelled. This enabled us to establish valid reference intervals from birth to late adult life for both males and females. Conclusion: Detailed sex- and age-specific reference intervals of multiple, simultaneously quantified steroid metabolites by a novel and specific LC-MS/MS method provides a valuable tool for clinical practice and for future research.","author_count":17,"contributors":["Frederiksen, Hanne","Johannsen, Trine Holm","Andersen, Stine Ehlern","Petersen, Jørgen Holm","Busch, Alexander Siegfried","Ljubicic, Marie Lindhardt","Fischer, Margit Bistrup","Upners, Emmie N.","Hagen, Casper P.","Main, Katharina M.","Aksglaede, Lise","Jørgensen, Niels","Lund Kårhus, Line","Linneberg, Allan","Andersson, Anna Maria","Flück, Christa E.","Juul, Anders"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-748862"],"filters":{"added":"2024-08","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"country":["Switzerland"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","University Hospital Bern","University of Bern"],"keyword":["Infant","LC MS MS","Puberty","Reference interval","Sex difference","Steroid hormone"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"sex and age specific reference intervals of 000000000016 steroid metabolites quantified simultaneously by lc ms ms in sera from 000000002458 healthy subjects aged 000000000000 to 000000000077 years","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-748862","identifier":[{"id":"85197766961","type":"scopus"},{"id":"38977173","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-a9ea465f-f6dc-46b7-87da-f0420992c8d2"],"keyword":["Infant","LC-MS/MS","Puberty","Reference interval","Sex difference","Steroid hormone"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-8B519260B63D7E3CAC07ABA67E1F478A"],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital - Rigshospitalet"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":