open-2023-073909","issn":["20446055"],"issue":"2","journal":"BMJ Open","paperid":"e073909","publisher":"BMJ Publishing Group","status":"p","title":"BMJ Open","volume":"14"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85184683050"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","Central Denmark Region","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-ffdc7e2d-e085-43e3-a9e8-a0fb0d195454","ku-3a19251e-3acc-40b5-a41c-91a583f80a6b"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Is reduced heart rate variability associated with functional somatic disorders? : A cross-sectional population-based study; DanFunD","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-099.04-716172","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"Despite chemotherapy-induced intestinal mucositis being a main risk factor for blood stream infections (BSIs), no studies have investigated mucositis severity to predict BSI at fever onset during acute leukemia treatment. This study prospectively evaluated intestinal mucositis severity in 85 children with acute leukemia, representing 242 febrile episodes (122 with concurrent neutropenia) by measuring plasma levels of citrulline (reflecting enterocyte loss), regenerating islet-derived-protein 3α (REG3α, an intestinal antimicrobial peptide) and CCL20 (a mucosal immune regulatory chemokine) along with the general neutrophil chemo-attractants CXCL1 and CXCL8 at fever onset. BSI was documented in 14% of all febrile episodes and in 20% of the neutropenic febrile episodes. In age-, sex-, diagnosis- and neutrophil count-adjusted analyses, decreasing citrulline levels and increasing REG3α and CCL20 levels were independently associated with increased odds of BSI (OR = 1.6, 1.5 and 1.7 per halving/doubling, all p < 0.05). Additionally, higher CXCL1 and CXCL8 levels increased the odds of BSI (OR = 1.8 and 1.7 per doubling, all p < 0.0001). All three chemokines showed improved diagnostic accuracy compared to C-reactive protein and procalcitonin. These findings underline the importance of disrupted intestinal integrity as a main risk factor for BSI and suggest that objective markers for monitoring mucositis severity may help predicting BSI at fever onset.","author_count":10,"contributors":["Weischendorff, Sarah","Rathe, Mathias","Petersen, Malene Johanne","Weimann, Allan","Enevold, Christian","Nielsen, Claus H.","Als-Nielsen, Bodil","Nygaard, Ulrikka","Moser, Claus","Müller, Klaus"],"cuid":["S02-100.00-716322"],"filters":{"added":"2024-02","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"corresponding_author":["Weischendorff, Sarah"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"markers of intestinal mucositis to predict blood stream infections at the onset of fever during treatment for childhood acute leukemia","src":["ku","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/s41375-023-02077-7","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-100.00-716322","identifier":[{"id":"85175548212","type":"scopus"},{"id":"37919603","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC10776407","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["ku-025fb3eb-bb4d-4b14-a25f-5a1e5dc1cac7","sdu-07ed038e-b452-4cf2-9072-c86aff05bb50"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-F948BC20289B35253B62CA77FC49AE70"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/379176622/Fulltext.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/s41375-023-02077-7","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/245487758/s41375_023_02077_7.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Rigshospitalet"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research","SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research, KI, OUH, Research unit of Paediatrics (Odense)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Paediatrics"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Sarah","key":"weischendorffpau","last":"Weischendorff","name":"Weischendorff, Sarah","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Mathias","key":"rathepau","last":"Rathe","locid":"a4c4c033-05e3-4322-b889-64044b7143db","name":"Rathe, Mathias","orcid":"0000-0002-7533-3112","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Malene Johanne","key":"petersenpau","last":"Petersen","name":"Petersen, Malene Johanne","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Allan","key":"weimannpau","last":"Weimann","name":"Weimann, Allan","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Christian","key":"enevoldpau","last":"Enevold","name":"Enevold, Christian","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Claus H.","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","name":"Nielsen, Claus H.","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Bodil","key":"alsnielsenpau","last":"Als-Nielsen","name":"Als-Nielsen, Bodil","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 3","first":"Ulrikka","key":"nygaardpau","last":"Nygaard","locid":"43b2e239-ddc1-4676-a8db-0a0f23906813","name":"Nygaard, Ulrikka","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 3","first":"Claus","key":"moserpau","last":"Moser","locid":"c253e3b6-b6c2-4633-9c44-2ccfcef5d5e8","name":"Moser, Claus","orcid":"0000-0002-7664-8570","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 3","first":"Klaus","key":"müllerpau","last":"Müller","locid":"b909f13e-79e3-4363-aaff-e5a5ecbdf7ce","name":"Müller, Klaus","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["37919603"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1038/s41375-023-02077-7","issn":["08876924","14765551"],"issn_org":["08876924"],"issue":"1","journal":"Leukemia","pages":"14-20","publisher":"Springer","status":"p","title":"Leukemia","volume":"38"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85175548212"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Region of Southern Denmark","Universities","University of Copenhagen","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-025fb3eb-bb4d-4b14-a25f-5a1e5dc1cac7","sdu-07ed038e-b452-4cf2-9072-c86aff05bb50"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Markers of intestinal mucositis to predict blood stream infections at the onset of fever during treatment for childhood acute leukemia","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-100.00-716322","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"BACKGROUND: Evidence of incidence of functional somatic disorders (FSD) is hampered by unclear delimitations of the conditions and little is known about the possible interchangeability between syndromes. Further, knowledge on remission and persistence of FSD in the general population is limited. We aimed to assess the natural course of various FSD over 5 years in the general population. METHODS: A follow-up study (Danish Study of Functional Disorders-DanFunD) was conducted in a random sample of the general population comprising 5,738 participants aged 18-76 years at baseline. Both at baseline and five-year follow-up, participants filled in validated questionnaires on symptoms to delimitate two approaches of FSD, the bodily distress syndrome (BDS) and four functional somatic syndromes (FSS): irritable bowel (IB), chronic fatigue (CF), chronic widespread pain (CWP), and multiple chemical sensitivity (MCS). RESULTS: Both BDS and FSS showed a five-year incidence around 11%. Incidence of the individual FSS varied from 0.8% (MCS) to 5.7% (CF). BDS and FSS showed a remission proportion close to 50%. We found a high degree of interchangeability between each FSS varying from 15.0% to 23.4%. CONCLUSION: We identified a marked fluctuation pattern of FSD during a five-year period, with a high degree of interchangeability between each FSS. The study stresses the importance of large population-based cohorts with transparent delimitation of FSD in future research to understand these complex conditions.","author_count":14,"contributors":["Schovsbo, Signe U","Kårhus, Line L","Bjerregaard, Anne A","Petersen, Marie Weinreich","Frostholm, Lisbeth","Fink, Per","Carstensen, Tina","Eplov, Lene F","Benros, Michael E","Brix, Susanne","Madsen, Anja L","Linneberg, Allan","Dantoft, Thomas M","Jørgensen, Torben"],"cuid":["S03-093.46-767419"],"filters":{"added":"2025-01","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":3,"corresponding_aut