ordentoft, Merete","rank":16,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Liselotte V","key":"petersenpau","last":"Petersen","locid":"ba9cb39d-0fd4-4e02-94fc-ce861a4b6d62","name":"Petersen, Liselotte","name_org":"Petersen, Liselotte V","orcid":"0000-0002-0479-5379","rank":17,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Florian","key":"privépau","last":"Privé","locid":"c1a6ae6f-a0f8-451a-8fd5-dc834bd5d423","name":"Privé, Florian","orcid":"0000-0002-3138-2078","rank":18,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5","first":"Julia","key":"sidorenkopau","last":"Sidorenko","name":"Sidorenko, Julia","rank":19,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Kristin","key":"skogstrandpau","last":"Skogstrand","name":"Skogstrand, Kristin","rank":20,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3 4","first":"Thomas","key":"wergepau","last":"Werge","locid":"905c01bb-6319-4ce6-a38e-ceb5bf73d2f6","name":"Werge, Thomas","rank":21,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5 10","first":"Naomi R.","key":"wraypau","last":"Wray","name":"Wray, Naomi R.","rank":22,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 3","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Bjarni J","key":"vilhjálmssonpau","last":"Vilhjálmsson","locid":"35c047ab-0899-4434-91bb-121e4878ec76","name":"Vilhjálmsson, Bjarni J","orcid":"0000-0003-2277-9249","rank":23,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 5 11","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"John J","key":"mcgrathpau","last":"McGrath","locid":"c7c66599-ed0f-4eac-8077-28a55f808894","name":"McGrath, John J","orcid":"0000-0002-4792-6068","rank":24,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["38116117"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.xgen.2023.100457","issn":["2666979X"],"issue":"12","journal":"Cell Genomics","pages":"100457","paperid":"100457","publisher":"Cell Press","status":"p","title":"Cell Genomics","volume":"3"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85179497801"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Governmental Institutions","All Hospitals","All Non-Profit Organisations","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","Central Denmark Region","DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-GV-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-NP","DI-NP-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Governmental Institutions","Hospitals","Non-Profit Organisations","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-7aa3292a-a1a8-4780-bbe1-cc4eb7867193","ku-461b035d-e3fa-4c7b-98e3-e718bf5a57d4"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"The correlates of neonatal complement component 3 and 4 protein concentrations with a focus on psychiatric and autoimmune disorders","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-100.00-724707","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"Background: MicroRNAs (miRNAs) can modulate several biological systems, including the pain system. This study aimed to evaluate the temporal expression of circulating miRNAs in the plasma of healthy volunteers as a marker for epigenetic changes before and after an acute, experimental, pain provocation by intramuscular hypertonic saline injection. Methods: Twenty volunteers were randomly allocated into two groups and received either hypertonic (pain) or isotonic (control) saline injection in the first dorsal interosseous muscle of their dominant hand. Pain intensity was continuously recorded for 20 minutes after injection on a VAS scale from 0 to 100 (0 indicates no pain and 100 the worst imaginable pain). Blood samples were taken at baseline, 30 minutes, 3 hours, and 24 hours post-injection, and plasma was separated. MiRNA extracts were used for RNA sequencing with the Illumina NextSeq platform. MiRNA transcripts were compared between the pain and the no-pain, control group at every time point. Significant differences were considered when folds were >2 and the False Discovery Rate was p < 0.05. Results: After 30 minutes, 4 miRNAs were significantly altered in the pain group compared to controls, which increased to 24 after 3 hours and to 42 after 24 hours from baseline (p < 0.0001). Two miRNAs were consistently upregulated throughout the experiment. Enrichment analysis showed significant miRNAs involved in brain perception of pain, brain signalling and response to stimuli. Conclusions: This exploratory study is the first to report on the temporal expression of circulating miRNAs after an acute, human experimental muscle pain model. Significance: This exploratory study evaluated the temporal profile of circulating miRNAs in the plasma of healthy subjects after acute experimental pain. Several miRNAs were altered in subjects at the times of follow-up after the acute pain model when compared to controls. MiRNAs previously associated with pain processes were altered in the pain group. Our results, by showing the fast and prolonged modifications of miRNA elicited by the acute experimental pain model, add new perspectives to the topic of epigenetics and pain.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Giordano, Rocco","Gerra, M. C.","Okutani, Hiroai","Lo Vecchio, Silvia","Stensballe, Allan","Petersen, Kristian Kjær","Arendt-Nielsen, Lars"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-093813"],"filters":{"added":"2023-02","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, East","Europe, EU","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Arendt-Nielsen, Lars"],"country":["Italy","Japan"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Hyogo Medical University","University of Parma"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the temporal expression of circulating micrornas after acute experimental pain in humans","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY 4.0","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1002/ejp.2062","version":"Published Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["The authors thank DNASense (Aalborg, Denmark), Mads Toft Søndergaard, Ph.D., Chief Executive Officer DNASense Aalborg, Denmark and Henrik Bech Kjeldal, Ph.D. Chief Information Officer DNASense Aalborg, Denmark for miRNAs quantification and following statistical analysis. The Center for Neuroplasticity and Pain (CNAP) is supported by the Danish National Research Foundation (DNRF121)."],"id":"S01-000.00-093813","identifier":[{"id":"85144030367","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-96ea40df-647e-43ea-9be6-a588f43e76ed"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-129FAF303A6CC7C26C10BE0288238AC6"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY 4.0","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/515132725/European_Journal_of_Pain_2022_Giordano_The_temporal_expression_of_circulating_microRNAs_after_acute_experimental_pain_1_.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY 4.0","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1002/ejp.2062","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Department of Health Science and Technology","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Department of Health Science and Technology, Center for Neuroplasticity and Pain","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Department of Health Science and Technology, Translational Biomarkers in Pain and Precision Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"it","key":"university of parma","loc":["Italy","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Parma","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"jp","key":"hyogo medical university","loc":["Japan","Asia, East","OECD"],"name":"Hyogo Medical University","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"R.","key":"giordanopau","last":"Giordano","locid":"201beefd-2ee8-4758-9607-6a6da835d1ca","name":"Giordano, Rocco","name_org":"Giordano, R.","orcid":"0000-0003-1331-129X","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"M. C.","key":"gerrapau","last":"Gerra","name":"Gerra, M. C.","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 3","corresponding":null,"first":"H.","key":"okutanipau","last":"Okutani","locid":"6f4831d8-c0c2-405e-bdf6-33c7f7238d02","name":"Okutani, Hiroai","name_org":"Okutani, H.","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"S.","key":"lovecchiopau","last":"Lo Vecchio","locid":"fdf43775-9c5a-4dfe-8860-0e85594e9422","name":"Lo Vecchio, Silvia","name_org":"Lo Vecchio, S.","orcid":"0000-0001-6548-2459","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"A.","key":"stensballepau","last":"Stensballe","locid":"31ce2dbc-d5bc-4266-8c26-1b38838c7346","name":"Stensballe, Allan","name_org":"Stensballe, A.","orcid":"0000-0002-9888-1955","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"K. K.","key":"petersenpau","last":"Petersen","locid":"03b38a92-c53c-4b31-a786-05e4893a3e14","name":"Petersen, Kristian Kjær","name_org":"Petersen, K. K.","orcid":"0000-0003-4506-000X","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"L.","key":"arendtnielsenpau","last":"Arendt-Nielsen","locid":"1794f9ec-22f1-47af-96c1-88c23c3b06a2","name":"Arendt-Nielsen, Lars","name_org":"Arendt-Nielsen, L.","orcid":"0000-0003-0892-1579","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1002/ejp.2062","issn":["10903801","15322149"],"issn_org":["10903801"],"issue":"3","journal":"European Journal of Pain","pages":"366-377","publisher":"Wiley","status":"p","title":"European Journal of Pain","volume":"27"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85144030367"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-96ea40df-647e-43ea-9be6-a588f43e76ed"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"The temporal expression of circulating microRNAs after acute experimental pain in humans","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-093813","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"BACKGROUND: Diagnostic uncertainty in patients with dyspnea is associated with worse outcomes. We hypothesized that prehospital point-of-care ultrasound (POCUS) can improve diagnostic accuracy. METHODS: Prospective observational study of adult patients suffering dyspnea. Prehospital critical care physicians registered a suspected diagnosis based on clinical examination alone, performed POCUS of the heart and lungs, and finally registered suspected diagnoses based on their clinical examination supplemented with POCUS. Pre- and post-POCUS diagnoses were compared to endpoint committee adjudicated diagnoses. The primary outcome was improved sensitivity for diagnosing acute heart failure. Secondary outcomes included other diagnostic accuracy measures in relation to acute heart failure and other causes of dyspnea. RESULTS: In total, 214 patients were included. The diagnosis of acute heart failure was suspected in 64/214 (30%) of patients before POCUS and 64/214 (30%) patients after POCUS, but POCUS led to reclassification in 53/214 (25%) patients. The endpoint committee adjudicated the diagnosis of acute heart failure in 87/214 (41%) patients. The sensitivity for the diagnosis of acute heart failure was 58% (95% CI 46%-69%) before POCUS compared to 65% (95% CI 53%-75%) after POCUS (p = 0.12). ROC AUC for the diagnosis acute heart failure was 0.72 (95% CI 0.66-0.78) before POCUS compared to 0.79 (0.73-0.84) after POCUS (p < 0.001). ROC AUC for the diagnosis acute exacerbation (AE) of chronic obstructive pulmonary disease (COPD) or asthma was 0.87 (0.82-0.91) before POCUS and 0.93 (0.88-0.97) after POCUS (p < 0.001). A POCUS finding of any of severely reduced left ventricular function, bilateral B-lines or bilateral pleural effusion demonstrated the highest sensitivity for acute heart failure at 88% (95% CI 79%-94%), whereas the combination of all of these three findings yielded the highest specificity at 99% (95% CI 95%-100%). CONCLUSION: Supplementary prehospital POCUS leads to an improvement of diagnostic accuracy of both heart failure and AE-COPD/-asthma overall described by ROC AUC, but the increase in sensitivity for the diagnoses of acute heart failure did not reach statistical significance. Tailored use of POCUS findings optimizes diagnostic accuracy for rule-out and rule-in of acute heart failure. TRIAL REGISTRATION: Registered in Clinical Trials, 05.04.2019 (identifier: NCT03905460) https://clinicaltrials.gov/ct2/show/study/NCT03905460?term=NCT03905460&cond=Dyspnea&cntry=DK&draw=2&rank=1 .","author_count":10,"contributors":["Gundersen, Elise Arem","Juhl-Olsen, Peter","Bach, Allan","Rostgaard-Knudsen, Martin","Nielsen, Bent Roni Ranghøj","Skaarup, Søren Helbo","Petersen, Henrik Ømark","Fjølner, Jesper","Poulsen, Morten Gustav Gerstrøm","Bøtker, Morten Thingemann"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-264579"],"filters":{"added":"2023-03","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Dyspnea","Heart failure","Point of care ultrasound","Prehospital"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-NDR"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-NDR","DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"prehospital ultrasound in undifferentiated dyspnea prelude a prospective clinical observational study","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC0","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/s13049-023-01070-4","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-264579","identifier":[{"id":"PMC9899351","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"85147390921","type":"scopus"},{"id":"36740691","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["au-ecf4840c-e92d-451e-82d8-4cdf1c4cefe0"],"keyword":["Dyspnea","Heart failure","Point-of-care ultrasound","Prehospital"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-F423E38D6BDA5A37BA71ED63A93BEA5D"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC0","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/s13049-023-01070-4","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - Anæstesiologisk afdeling, Viborg"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"north denmark region","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-NDR","l3nl":"North Denmark Region","l3nn":"North Denmark Region","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"North Denmark Region","namevar":["The North Denmark Region"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-NDR","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"central denmark region","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CDR","l3nl":"Central Denmark Region","l3nn":"Central Denmark Region","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Central Denmark Region","namevar":["Ortopædkirurgisk afdeling, Regionshospitalet Horsens"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CDR","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Elise Arem","key":"gundersenpau","last":"Gundersen","locid":"3541da15-cb42-4253-bbc0-196bc08ec456","name":"Gundersen, Elise Arem","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Peter","key":"juhlolsenpau","last":"Juhl-Olsen","locid":"9da91e58-316c-45e5-8f41-02b8b23a8c32","name":"Juhl-Olsen, Peter","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Allan","key":"bachpau","last":"Bach","name":"Bach, Allan","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Martin","key":"rostgaardknudsenpau","last":"Rostgaard-Knudsen","name":"Rostgaard-Knudsen, Martin","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Bent Roni Ranghøj","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"896f4a21-d29c-4ad9-b0ef-4e7f8616c234","name":"Nielsen, Bent Roni Ranghøj","orcid":"0000-0001-9228-3869","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Søren Helbo","key":"skaaruppau","last":"Skaarup","locid":"eb023a98-d316-4b44-bf12-469c0f2d00cd","name":"Skaarup, Søren Helbo","orcid":"0000-0001-7975-7441","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Henrik Ømark","key":"petersenpau","last":"Petersen","name":"Petersen, Henrik Ømark","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jesper","key":"fjølnerpau","last":"Fjølner","locid":"b5deb983-b5ff-43a4-af7e-d8088e316818","name":"Fjølner, Jesper","orcid":"0000-0003-3371-0503","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Morten Gustav Gerstrøm","key":"poulsenpau","last":"Poulsen","name":"Poulsen, Morten Gustav Gerstrøm","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Morten Thingemann","key":"bøtkerpau","last":"Bøtker","locid":"626b3aff-f412-4560-a703-9ad54f701c09","name":"Bøtker, Morten Thingemann","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["36740691"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1186/s13049-023-01070-4","issn":["17577241"],"issue":"1","journal":"Scandinavian Journal of Trauma, Resuscitation and Emergency Medicine","paperid":"6","publisher":"BioMed Central","status":"p","title":"Scandinavian Journal of Trauma, Resuscitation and Emergency Medicine","volume":"31"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85147390921"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Central Denmark Region","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","North Denmark Region","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-ecf4840c-e92d-451e-82d8-4cdf1c4cefe0"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"PrehospitaL Ultrasound in Undifferentiated DyspnEa (PreLUDE) : a prospective, clinical, observational study","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-264579","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"CONTEXT: Supraphysiological serum insulin-like growth-factor-I (IGF-I) concentrations have been a matter of concern in children treated with growth hormone (GH) because high IGF-I levels were associated with risk of later disease in former epidemiological studies. OBJECTIVE: To determine whether a single IGF-I measurement reliably reflects lifetime IGF-I exposure we evaluated intraindividual longitudinal tracking of IGF-I and IGF-binding-protein-3 (IGFBP-3) levels and we estimated cumulative lifetime exposure to IGF-I in healthy and GH-treated individuals. METHODS: We included 6,459 healthy participants (cross-sectional = 5,326; longitudinal = 1,133) aged 0----76 years (9,963 serum samples) and nine patients born small-for-gestational-age (SGA) with 238 serum samples during GH treatment.Intraindividual tracking of IGF-I and IGFBP-3 (SDS) was determined by intraclass correlation coefficients (ICC). Cumulative lifetime IGF-I exposure was estimated by area under the curve of the predicted SDS-trajectory from 0-76 years. RESULTS: For IGF-I (SDS), ICCs were 0.50 (95% CI: 0.47-0.53) for male and 0.53 (0.50-0.56) for female participants. Lifetime IGF-I exposure was significantly higher in female (mean 12,723 ± 3,691 SD) than in male participants (12,563 ± 3,393); p = 0.02. In SGA children, treatment with GH increased the lifetime exposure to IGF-I from 9,512 ± 1,889 to 11,271 ± 1,689, corresponding to an increase in lifetime IGF-I trajectory from -0.89 SD ± 0.57 to -0.35 SD ± 0.49. CONCLUSION: Since IGF-I and IGFBP-3 levels track throughout life, a single measurement reliably reflects lifetime exposure. GH therapy increased the lifetime exposure to IGF-I only slightly and it remained below the average lifetime exposure in the reference population.","author_count":10,"contributors":["Kjaer, Anna Sophie L","Jensen, Rikke Beck","Petersen, Jørgen Holm","Linneberg, Allan","Kårhus, Line Lund","Henriksen, Louise Scheutz","Johannsen, Trine Holm","Main, Katharina M.","Hoffman, Andrew R","Juul, Anders"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-488962"],"filters":{"added":"2023-03","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","OECD"],"country":["United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Stanford University"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"tracking and cumulative lifetime exposure to igf i in 000000000006 000000000459 healthy individuals and in sga children treated with gh","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/408435166/dgac605.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-488962","identifier":[{"id":"85148249861","type":"scopus"},{"id":"36250350","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-9fc75963-96a1-45c2-bc38-1e33abf81fc5"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-01B054FFBC7E4D3ADEA6304E9E94AE56"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/408435166/dgac605.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital - Rigshospitalet"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Public Health, Section of Biostatistics"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"us","key":"stanford university","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"Stanford University","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Anna Sophie L","key":"kjaerpau","last":"Kjaer","name":"Kjaer, Anna Sophie L","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Rikke Beck","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","name":"Jensen, Rikke Beck","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","first":"Jørgen H","key":"petersenpau","last":"Petersen","locid":"33c1c5b2-2e1e-4259-b4d7-04657a2bdb9b","name":"Petersen, Jørgen Holm","name_org":"Petersen, Jørgen H","orcid":"0000-0003-3979-7443","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Allan","key":"linnebergpau","last":"Linneberg","locid":"09da8aa6-fd95-4ace-a2f1-19f38d7d3f9e","name":"Linneberg, Allan","orcid":"0000-0002-0994-0184","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Line Lund","key":"kårhuspau","last":"Kårhus","name":"Kårhus, Line Lund","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Louise Scheutz","key":"henriksenpau","last":"Henriksen","name":"Henriksen, Louise Scheutz","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Trine Holm","key":"johannsenpau","last":"Johannsen","name":"Johannsen, Trine Holm","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","first":"Katharina M","key":"mainpau","last":"Main","locid":"1770eebd-1659-4088-b44c-c9de22a4bb0b","name":"Main, Katharina M.","name_org":"Main, Katharina M","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Andrew R","key":"hoffmanpau","last":"Hoffman","name":"Hoffman, Andrew R","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","first":"Anders","key":"juulpau","last":"Juul","locid":"f9b11983-c7c8-4111-b119-4de471572898","name":"Juul, Anders","orcid":"0000-0002-0534-4350","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["36250350"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1210/clinem/dgac605","issn":["0021972X","19457197"],"issn_org":["0021972X"],"issue":"3","journal":"Journal of Clinical Endocrinology and Metabolism","pages":"642-652","status":"p","title":"Journal of Clinical Endocrinology and Metabolism","title_org":"The Journal of clinical endocrinology and metabolism","volume":"108"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85148249861"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-9fc75963-96a1-45c2-bc38-1e33abf81fc5"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Tracking and Cumulative Lifetime Exposure to IGF-I in 6,459 Healthy Individuals and in SGA Children Treated with GH","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-488962","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"The present study reveals the effects of symmetry on how the distribution and flow of energy play out on the decomposition of small halocarbons. Unimolecular decay of the freons CHFCl2 and CF2Cl2 when ionized has been investigated. Mass spectrometric results that encompass isotope effects (peak heights) and energy distribution in the exit channel (peak shapes) are interpreted by computational methods. Non-statistical processes of electronic predissociation and isolated state decay are shown to be directly associated with molecular symmetry.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Petersen, Allan Christian","Sølling, Theis Ivan"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-720807"],"filters":{"added":"2024-02","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, Middle East"],"country":["Saudi Arabia"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","King Fahd University of Petroleum and Minerals"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"dissociation processes of ionized freons chfcl sub 000000000002 sub sup sup and cf sub 000000000002 sub cl sub 000000000002 sub sup sup in the gas phase","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"Andet","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/405330824/Dissociation_processes_o.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-720807","identifier":[{"id":"37921250","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85176115310","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-7b244f9c-8f44-4412-8796-ff7b41844a7c"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-870534BCAD0B3DCE5721306F46B77234"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"Andet","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/405330824/Dissociation_processes_o.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["University of Copenhagen"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"sa","key":"king fahd university of petroleum and minerals","loc":["Saudi Arabia","Asia, Middle East"],"name":"King Fahd University of Petroleum and Minerals","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Allan Christian","key":"petersenpau","last":"Petersen","name":"Petersen, Allan Christian","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","first":"Theis Ivan","key":"søllingpau","last":"Sølling","locid":"5db24645-70db-461f-a061-dd6612993ec8","name":"Sølling, Theis Ivan","orcid":"0000-0003-1710-9072","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["37921250"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1063/5.0169883","issn":["00219606","10897690"],"issn_org":["00219606"],"issue":"17","journal":"Journal of Chemical Physics","paperid":"174306","status":"p","title":"Journal of Chemical Physics","volume":"159"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85176115310"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-7b244f9c-8f44-4412-8796-ff7b41844a7c"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Dissociation processes of ionized freons : CHFCl<sub>2</sub><sup>+</sup> and CF<sub>2</sub>Cl<sub>2</sub><sup>+</sup> in the gas phase","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-720807","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"Background: Diabetes and its cardiovascular complications are a growing concern worldwide. Recently, some studies have demonstrated that relative risk of heart failure (HF) is higher in women with type 1 diabetes (T1DM) than in men. This study aims to validate these findings in cohorts representing five countries across Europe. Methods: This study includes 88,559 (51.8% women) participants, 3,281 (46.3% women) of whom had diabetes at baseline. Survival analysis was performed with the outcomes of interest being death and HF with a follow-up time of 12 years. Sub-group analysis according to sex and type of diabetes was also performed for the HF outcome. Results: 6,460 deaths were recorded, of which 567 were amongst those with diabetes. Additionally, HF was diagnosed in 2,772 individuals (446 with diabetes). A multivariable Cox proportional hazard analysis showed that there was an increased risk of death and HF (hazard ratio (HR) of 1.73 [1.58–1.89] and 2.12 [1.91–2.36], respectively) when comparing those with diabetes and those without. The HR for HF was 6.72 [2.75–16.41] for women with T1DM vs. 5.80 [2.72–12.37] for men with T1DM, but the interaction term for sex differences was insignificant (p for interaction 0.45). There was no significant difference in the relative risk of HF between men and women when both types of diabetes were combined (HR 2.22 [1.93–2.54] vs. 1.99 [1.67–2.38] respectively, p for interaction 0.80). Conclusion: Diabetes is associated with increased risks of death and heart failure, and there was no difference in relative risk according to sex.","author_count":16,"contributors":["Chadalavada, Sucharitha","Reinikainen, Jaakko","Andersson, Jonas","Di Castelnuovo, Augusto","Iacoviello, Licia","Jousilahti, Pekka","Kårhus, Line Lund","Linneberg, Allan","Söderberg, Stefan","Tunstall-Pedoe, Hugh","Lekadir, Karim","Aung, Nay","Jensen, Magnus T.","Kuulasmaa, Kari","Niiranen, Teemu J.","Petersen, Steffen E."],"cuid":["S01-000.00-731257"],"filters":{"added":"2024-05","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"country":["Finland","Italy","Spain","Sweden","United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Barts Health NHS Trust","Finnish Institute for Health and Welfare","Health Data Research UK","IRCCS Istituto Neurologico Mediterraneo Neuromed - Pozzilli (IS)","Mediterranea Cardiocentro","National Institute for Health and Care Research","Queen Mary University of London","Umeå University","University of Barcelona","University of Dundee","University of Insubria","University of Turku"],"keyword":["Diabetes","Epidemiology","Heart failure","Sex differences"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"OT":["Steno Diabetes Centre, Gentofte, Denmark."],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"diabetes and heart failure associations in women and men results from the morgam consortium","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3389/fcvm.2023.1136764","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-731257","identifier":[{"id":"PMC10167048","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"37180793","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85158846031","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-5c31ac6c-3f7e-4ba0-ad4e-b16020106b59"],"keyword":["MORGAM","diabetes","epidemiology","heart failure","sex differences"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-11BCA21D5B42D6B4CD04EAD80F1282A6"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/388332280/fcvm_10_1136764.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3389/fcvm.2023.1136764","v