e Lund","key":"kårhuspau","last":"Kårhus","name":"Kårhus, Line Lund","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"8 9","first":"Allan","key":"linnebergpau","last":"Linneberg","locid":"09da8aa6-fd95-4ace-a2f1-19f38d7d3f9e","name":"Linneberg, Allan","orcid":"0000-0002-0994-0184","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","first":"Stefan","key":"söderbergpau","last":"Söderberg","name":"Söderberg, Stefan","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"10","first":"Hugh","key":"tunstallpedoepau","last":"Tunstall-Pedoe","name":"Tunstall-Pedoe, Hugh","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"11","first":"Karim","key":"lekadirpau","last":"Lekadir","name":"Lekadir, Karim","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","first":"Nay","key":"aungpau","last":"Aung","name":"Aung, Nay","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 12","first":"Magnus T.","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","name":"Jensen, Magnus T.","rank":13,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Kari","key":"kuulasmaapau","last":"Kuulasmaa","name":"Kuulasmaa, Kari","rank":14,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3 13","first":"Teemu J.","key":"niiranenpau","last":"Niiranen","name":"Niiranen, Teemu J.","rank":15,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2 14 15","first":"Steffen E.","key":"petersenpau","last":"Petersen","name":"Petersen, Steffen E.","rank":16,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["37180793"],"pub":{"doi":"10.3389/fcvm.2023.1136764","issn":["2297055X"],"journal":"Frontiers in Cardiovascular Medicine","paperid":"1136764","status":"p","title":"Frontiers in Cardiovascular Medicine","volume":"10"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85158846031"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-5c31ac6c-3f7e-4ba0-ad4e-b16020106b59"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Diabetes and heart failure associations in women and men : Results from the MORGAM consortium","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-731257","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"Background: Patients receiving total hip arthroplasty (THA) due to metastatic bone disease of the hip (MBD) are at an increased risk of post-operative joint dislocation compared to other populations. Different joint solutions have been developed with the purpose of reducing the dislocation risk compared to regular THAs. One of these solutions, the constrained liner (CL), has been used increasingly at our department in recent years. This design, however, is prone to polyethylene wear and higher revision rates. An alternative is the dual mobility cup (DM), which has been shown to reduce the risk of dislocation in other high-risk populations. Few studies have investigated DM for THA due to MBD, and no studies have directly compared these two treatments in this population. We therefore decided to conduct a trial to investigate whether DM is non-inferior to CL regarding the post-operative joint dislocation risk in patients receiving THA due to MBD. Materials and methods: This study is a single-center, randomized, open-label, two-arm, non-inferiority trial. We will include 146 patients with MBD of the hip who are planned for THA at the Department of Orthopedic Surgery, Rigshospitalet. Patients with previous osteosynthesis or endoprosthetic surgery of the afflicted hip, or who are planned to receive partial pelvic reconstruction or total femoral replacement, will be excluded. Patients will be stratified by whether subtrochanteric bone resection will be performed and allocated to either CL or DM in a 1:1 ratio. The primary outcome is the 6 months post-operative joint dislocation rate. Secondary outcomes include overall survival, implant survival, the rate of other surgical- and post-operative complications, and quality of life and functional outcome scores. Discussion: This study is designed to investigate whether DM is non-inferior to CL regarding the risk of post-operative dislocation in patients receiving THA due to MBD. To our knowledge, this trial is the first of its kind. Knowledge gained from this trial will help guide surgeons in choosing a joint solution that minimizes the risk of dislocation and, ultimately, reduces the need for repeat surgeries in this patient population. Trial registration: ClinicalTrials.gov Identifier: NCT05461313. Registered on July 15 2022. This trial is reported according to the items in the WHO Trial Registration Data Set (Version 1.3.1).","author_count":6,"contributors":["Iljazi, Afrim","Sørensen, Michala Skovlund","Weber, Kolja Sebastian","Villadsen, Allan","Eriksson, Frank","Petersen, Michael Mørk"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-405949"],"filters":{"added":"2023-05","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Dual mobility","Metastatic cancer","Total hip arthroplasty"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"fully constrained acetabular liner vs dual mobility hip joint in the surgical treatment of metastatic bone disease of the hip study protocol for a randomized open label two arm non inferiority trial evaluating the post operative hip dislocation rate","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/s13063-023-07237-9","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-405949","identifier":[{"id":"36934286","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC10024853","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"85150665889","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-14f556d7-13d1-48b3-bbd2-5768bbfc69d1"],"keyword":["Constrained liner","Dual mobility","Metastatic cancer","Pathologic fracture","Total hip arthroplasty"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-EE07BB1E47397CCD0565FC43F2ADF275"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/s13063-023-07237-9","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/341220236/Fulltext.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital - Rigshospitalet"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2","country":"dk","first":"Afrim","key":"iljazipau","last":"Iljazi","locid":"c2dbb056-88ec-420b-9455-e0d1770d1e50","name":"Iljazi, Afrim","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Michala Skovlund","key":"sørensenpau","last":"Sørensen","name":"Sørensen, Michala Skovlund","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Kolja Sebastian","key":"weberpau","last":"Weber","name":"Weber, Kolja Sebastian","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Allan","key":"villadsenpau","last":"Villadsen","name":"Villadsen, Allan","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Frank","key":"erikssonpau","last":"Eriksson","locid":"c99962f5-7e96-426f-8471-ce34aeafbf18","name":"Eriksson, Frank","orcid":"0000-0003-3641-745X","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 1","first":"Michael Mørk","key":"petersenpau","last":"Petersen","locid":"9eb5f936-2e76-4f2f-917e-a3b50f56f0e6","name":"Petersen, Michael Mørk","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["36934286"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1186/s13063-023-07237-9","issn":["14686708","17456215"],"issn_org":["17456215"],"issue":"1","journal":"Trials","paperid":"204","status":"p","title":"Trials","volume":"24"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85150665889"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-14f556d7-13d1-48b3-bbd2-5768bbfc69d1"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Fully constrained acetabular liner vs. dual mobility hip joint in the surgical treatment of metastatic bone disease of the hip : study protocol for a randomized, open-label, two-arm, non-inferiority trial evaluating the post-operative hip dislocation rate","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-405949","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"Type 2 diabetes (T2D) is a large disease burden worldwide and represents an increasing and complex challenge for all societies. For the individual, (T2D) is a complex, multi-dimensional, and long-term challenge to manage, and it is challenging to establish and maintain good communication between the patient and healthcare professionals. This paper presents DiaFocus, which is a mobile health (mHealth) sensing application for long-term ambulatory management of T2D. DiaFocus supports an adaptive collection of physiological, behavioral, and contextual data in combination with ecological assessments of psycho-social factors. This data is used for improving patient-clinician communication during consultations. DiaFocus is built using a generic data collection framework for mobile and wearable sensing and is highly extensible and customizable. We deployed DiaFocus in a 6-week feasibility study involving 12 patients with T2D. The patients found the DiaFocus approach and system useful and usable for diabetes management. Most patients would use such a system, if available as part of their treatment. Analysis of the collected data shows that mobile sensing is feasible for longitudinal ambulatory assessment of T2D, and helped identify the most appropriate target users being early diagnosed and technically literate T2D patients.","author_count":13,"contributors":["Bardram, Jakob Eyvind","Cramer-Petersen, Claus Lundgaard","Maxhuni, Alban","Christensen, Mads V.S.","Bækgaard, Per","Persson, Dan Roland","Lind, Nanna","Christensen, Merete B.","Nørgaard, Kirsten","Khakurel, Jayden","Skinner, Timothy C.","Kownatka, Dagmar","Jones, Allan"],"cuid":["S02-088.49-673000"],"filters":{"added":"2023-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"country":["Finland","Germany","Switzerland"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","F. Hoffmann-La Roche","Roche Diabetes Care GmbH","University of Turku"],"level":"sci","mra":["med","sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-STENO"],"OT":["Steno Diabetes Centre, Gentofte, Denmark."],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-STENO","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"diafocus a personal health technology for adaptive assessment in long term management of type 000000000002 diabetes","src":["dtu","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/350251047/DiaFocus_ACM_HEALTH_2022_2_.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S02-088.49-673000","identifier":[{"id":"85132030925","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-ffd84872-1074-4309-9471-099d42eccdb9","ku-4b80de00-49db-40df-bbf4-cb3a33777931"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science","Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-43A87CED68B1A97B72014A366DF0E376"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/350251047/DiaFocus_ACM_HEALTH_2022_2_.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/405745478/DiaFocus_KU.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Health Technology","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Health Technology, Digital Health","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Health Technology, Digital Health, Personalized Health Technology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"2","ke