{"abstract":"As of April, 2023, 23 accelerated approvals for cancer indications granted by the US Food and Drug Administration (FDA) since 1992 have been withdrawn from the US market, with 17 (74%) of 23 withdrawn in the past 3 years. The marketing authorisation status of these indications in the EU has not been reported. A review of relevant documents from the FDA and the European Medicines Agency (EMA) was done to investigate whether the accelerated approvals for cancer indications withdrawn by the FDA have a marketing authorisation in the EU to date, and to compare the approval history of these indications by the EMA and FDA. We found that, as of April 20, 2023, nine (39%) of 23 withdrawn accelerated approvals for cancer indications in the USA have a marketing authorisation in the EU for a similar indication. By comparison, only two conditional marketing authorisations for cancer indications have been withdrawn from the EU; both are no longer approved in the USA. These findings indicate a discrepancy in the approval policies between the FDA and EMA and imply either that some patient groups in the USA do not get access to relevant medical treatment, or that some patient groups in the EU are treated with medicine without a positive benefit-risk balance. These discrepancies could potentially be reduced by increased collaboration and information sharing between the two agencies.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Cramer, Allan","Sørup, Freja K H","Christensen, Hanne R","Petersen, Tonny Studsgaard","Karstoft, Kristian"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-731235"],"filters":{"added":"2024-05","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Humans","Information Dissemination","Marketing","Medicine","Neoplasms drug therapy","United States","United States Food and Drug Administration"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"withdrawn accelerated approvals for cancer indications in the usa what is the marketing authorisation status in the eu","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"djr","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-731235","identifier":[{"id":"85169510108","type":"scopus"},{"id":"37657479","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-5a851296-facf-42e9-8c55-245a15169b40"],"keyword":["Humans","Information Dissemination","Marketing","Medicine","Neoplasms/drug therapy","United States","United States Food and Drug Administration"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-DAB29E17615BE40F6F2F569E398A9A95"],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital - Bispebjerg and Frederiksberg"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Clinical Pharmacology","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Allan","key":"cramerpau","last":"Cramer","name":"Cramer, Allan","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Freja K H","key":"søruppau","last":"Sørup","name":"Sørup, Freja K H","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Hanne R","key":"christensenpau","last":"Christensen","name":"Christensen, Hanne R","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","first":"Tonny S","key":"petersenpau","last":"Petersen","locid":"95e21f85-7cd9-443d-88c7-cc0b6e7bc844","name":"Petersen, Tonny Studsgaard","name_org":"Petersen, Tonny S","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","first":"Kristian","key":"karstoftpau","last":"Karstoft","locid":"80f306e9-a560-493c-b7d4-4e18b694660f","name":"Karstoft, Kristian","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["37657479"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/s1470-2045(23)00357-1","issn":["14702045","14745488"],"issn_org":["14702045"],"issue":"9","journal":"The Lancet Oncology","status":"p","title":"The Lancet Oncology","title_org":"The Lancet. Oncology","volume":"24"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85169510108"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-5a851296-facf-42e9-8c55-245a15169b40"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Withdrawn accelerated approvals for cancer indications in the USA : what is the marketing authorisation status in the EU?","type":"Journal Review","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-731235","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"Purpose: The aim of this study was to evaluate work ability, activity limitations and physical activity in adults that had gone through major bone sarcoma resection and reconstruction surgery in hip and knee. Materials and methods: Twenty patients, of 72 enrolled, and 20 controls were included in this cross-sectional study. Work Ability Index scores (general [0–10 points], physical and mental [1–5 points]), the Patient Specific Functional Scale (0–10 points), step counts and the International Physical Activity Questionnaire (IPAQ) were assessed. Adjusted and unadjusted general linear models were applied. Results: The patients had a mean age of 43 (range, 20–71) years and were assessed 7 years (range, 2–12) after surgery (proximal femoral n = 9, distal femoral n = 7, proximal tibia n = 4). Compared with controls, patients had lower general work ability (mean difference [95%CI], −1.3 points [−2.1, −0.5]) and work ability in relation to physical demands at work (−1.4 points [−2.0, −0.8]). The patients reported higher severities of activity limitation (−6.7 points [−7.9, −5.4]). There were no between-group differences in step counts or IPAQ-scores. Conclusion: Despite similar levels of physical activity, patients showed poorer work ability and severe activity limitation. Post-operative rehabilitation in patients of the working-age population should include assessments of work ability and activities important to the individual.IMPLICATIONS FOR REHABILITATION Adults that have gone through resection and reconstruction surgery following bone sarcoma in lower extremity show clinically relevant reductions in work ability and self-selected activities To tailor post-operative rehabilitation at short and long term, initial assessment and monitoring should include work ability and activities important to the individual patient.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Fernandes, Linda","Villadsen, Allan","Holm, Christina Enciso","Sørensen, Michala Skovlund","Zebis, Mette Kreutzfeldt","Andersen, Lars Louis","Mørk Petersen, Michael"],"cuid":["S03-098.15-768581"],"filters":{"added":"2023-09","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":3,"corresponding_author":["Fernandes, Linda"],"keyword":["Adult","Artificial Limbs","Bone Neoplasms surgery","Bone tumour","Cross Sectional Studies","Exercise","Fysisk aktivitet","Humans","Journal Article","Limb sparing surgery","Lower Extremity","Physical activity","Physical function","Retrospective Studies","Sarcoma surgery","Treatment Outcome","Work Capacity Evaluation","Work ability","bone sarcoma"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-HO","DI-OT","DI-U","DI-UC"],"level3":{"GV":["DI-GV-ALL","DI-GV-WORK"],"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-KEN"],"OT":["Department of Midwifery, Physiotherapy, Occupational Therapy and Psychomotor Therapy, Faculty of Health, University College Copenhagen, Copenhagen, Denmark."],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"],"UC":["DI-UC-ALL","DI-UC-KP"]},"level3all":["DI-GV-WORK","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-KEN","DI-U-KU","DI-UC-KP"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"work ability and physical activity after major bone sarcoma resection and reconstruction with tumour prosthesis of the lower extremities a cross sectional study","src":["kp","ku","nfa"],"src-code":["DI-GV-WORK","DI-U-KU","DI-UC-KP"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85134591680","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S03-098.15-768581","identifier":[{"id":"85134591680","type":"scopus"},{"id":"35867957","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["kp-f3a30a62-6a83-4c4f-9d02-a56847d0c3d0","ku-efb3bbd4-8029-42c2-96a7-9b6ce4291273","nfa-f2098b03-058b-441a-a1ed-99186e476fe8"],"keyword":["Adult","Artificial Limbs","Bone Neoplasms/surgery","Bone tumour","Cross-Sectional Studies","Exercise","Fysisk aktivitet","Humans","Journal Article","Lower Extremity","Retrospective Studies","Sarcoma/surgery","Treatment Outcome","Work Capacity Evaluation","bone sarcoma","limb-sparing surgery","physical activity","physical function","work ability"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-6-A5CEDF21ACD37DB5A01B1C0538618EAC"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"kp university college copenhagen","l2":"DI-UC","l2n":"University Colleges","l3":"DI-UC-KP","l3nl":"KP","l3nn":"KP University College Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KP University College Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Professionshøjskole, Rektors område, Fakultet for sundhedsuddannelser - Dekan, Fysioterapeutuddannelsen i Hillerød","Sundhed for børn og voksne – Institut for Terapeut og Jordemoderuddannelser, Børneliv - Sund tilknytning og aktiv livsstil for børn og unge"],"nora_code":"DI-UC-KP","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["Department of Midwifery, Physiotherapy, Occupational Therapy and Psychomotor Therapy, Faculty of Health, University College Copenhagen, Copenhagen, Denmark."],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"kennedy center","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-KEN","l3nn":"Kennedy Center","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Kennedy Center","namevar":["Kennedy Center"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-KEN","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital - Rigshospitalet"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"5","key":"nfa national research centre for the working environment","l2":"DI-GV","l2n":"Go