","last":"Andersen","locid":"7918e862-7513-454a-874b-3fdb31af5e48","name":"Andersen, Lars Louis","orcid":"0000-0003-2777-8085","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"6","first":"Michael Mørk","key":"petersenpau","last":"Petersen","locid":"9eb5f936-2e76-4f2f-917e-a3b50f56f0e6","name":"Petersen, Michael Mørk","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Michael","key":"mørkpetersenpau","last":"Mørk Petersen","name":"Mørk Petersen, Michael","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["35867957"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1080/09638288.2022.2101696","issn":["09638288","14645165"],"issn_org":["09638288"],"issue":"16","journal":"Disability and Rehabilitation","pages":"2597-2603","publisher":"Informa Healthcare","status":"p","title":"Disability and Rehabilitation","title_org":"Disability and rehabilitation","volume":"45"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85134591680"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Governmental Institutions","All Hospitals","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","All University Colleges","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-GV-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","DI-UC","DI-UC-ALL","Governmental Institutions","Hospitals","KP","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Universities","University Colleges","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["kp-f3a30a62-6a83-4c4f-9d02-a56847d0c3d0","ku-efb3bbd4-8029-42c2-96a7-9b6ce4291273","nfa-f2098b03-058b-441a-a1ed-99186e476fe8"],"src":["KP University College Copenhagen","KU University of Copenhagen","NFA National Research Centre for the Working Environment"],"title":"Work ability and physical activity after major bone sarcoma resection and reconstruction with tumour prosthesis of the lower extremities. A cross-sectional study","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S03-098.15-768581","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"Objectives: The objective of this longitudinal cohort study was to investigate if preoperative pain mechanisms, anxiety, and depression increase risk of developing chronic post-thoracotomy pain (CPTP) after lung cancer surgery. Methods: Patients with suspected or confirmed lung cancer undergoing surgery by either video-assisted thoracoscopic surgery or anterior thoracotomy were recruited consecutively. Preoperative assessments were conducted by: quantitative sensory testing (QST) (brush, pinprick, cuff pressure pain detection threshold, cuff pressure tolerance pain threshold, temporal summation and conditioned pain modulation), neuropathic pain symptom inventory (NPSI), and the Hospital Anxiety and Depression Scale (HADS). Clinical parameters in relation to surgery were also collected. Presence of CPTP was determined after six months and defined as pain of any intensity in relation to the operation area on a numeric rating scale form 0 (no pain) to 10 (worst pain imaginable). Results: A total of 121 patients (60.2%) completed follow-up and 56 patients (46.3%) reported CPTP. Development of CPTP was associated with higher preoperative HADS score (p=0.025), higher preoperative NPSI score (p=0.009) and acute postoperative pain (p=0.042). No differences were observed in relation to preoperative QST assessment by cuff algometry and HADS anxiety and depression sub-scores. Conclusions: High preoperative HADS score preoperative pain, acute postoperative pain intensity, and preoperative neuropathic symptoms were was associated with CPTP after lung cancer surgery. No differences in values of preoperative QST assessments were found. Preoperative assessment and identification of patients at higher risk of postoperative pain will offer opportunity for further exploration and development of preventive measures and individualised pain management depending on patient risk profile.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Danielsen, Allan Vestergaard","Andreasen, Jan Jesper","Dinesen, Birthe","Hansen, John","Petersen, Kristian Kjær","Simonsen, Carsten","Arendt-Nielsen, Lars"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-674024"],"filters":{"added":"2023-07","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Danielsen, Allan Vestergaard"],"keyword":["Chronic pain","Hospital anxiety and depression scale","Pain assessment","Pain prediction","Persistent postsurgical pain","Quantitative sensory testing","Thoracic surgery"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"chronic post thoracotomy pain after lung cancer surgery a prospective study of preoperative risk factors","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/545269989/10.1515_sjpain-2023-0016.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-674024","identifier":[{"id":"85164368978","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-b35d136d-48d3-4dba-a543-cf8419fe35c7"],"keyword":["Hospital Anxiety and Depression Scale","chronic pain","chronic post-thoracotomy pain","pain assessment","pain prediction","persistent postsurgical pain","quantitative sensory testing","thoracic surgery"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-EAB3E9085A7B026008D949F0569C862B"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/545269989/10.1515_sjpain-2023-0016.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Aalborg University Hospital"