olt","key":"christensenpau","last":"Christensen","locid":"7ce8714e-25d1-49af-ab75-6bb2a9b6b0f0","name":"Christensen, Anders Holt","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Carina Lykke","key":"westedpau","last":"Wested","locid":"fda5c9c3-73e1-41d5-ab9d-59e2c2884c42","name":"Wested, Carina Lykke","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Kristian Aagaard Lund","key":"petersenpau","last":"Petersen","locid":"20885b75-c5d8-45fe-ba06-afbb9899ea92","name":"Petersen, Kristian Aagaard Lund","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Tobias","key":"abildtruppau","last":"Abildtrup","name":"Abildtrup, Tobias","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"pages":"14-15","status":"p","title":"Abstraktbog, Nordjysk Forsknings- og udviklingssymposium 2023"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","All University Colleges","DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","DI-UC","DI-UC-ALL","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Universities","University College of Northern Denmark","University Colleges"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-7d3be9a7-21e7-4364-8dbb-a16d48c5f020"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Flere skridt mod et aktivt liv med høj intensitet gangtræning efter erhvervet hjerneskade: et samarbejde mellem kommuner, sygehuse og UCN","type":"Conference Abstract","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-705469","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"INTRODUCTION: Vitamin K has been suggested to have protective effects against progression of vascular calcification and development of cardiovascular disease (CVD). However, few well-powered randomised controlled trials have examined whether vitamin K prevents progression of vascular calcification in individuals from the general population. The aim of the InterVitaminK trial is to investigate the effects of vitamin K supplementation (menaquinone-7, MK-7) on cardiovascular, metabolic, respiratory and bone health in a general ageing population with detectable vascular calcification. METHODS AND ANALYSIS: The InterVitaminK trial is a randomised, double-blinded, placebo-controlled, trial. A total of 450 men and women aged 52-82 years with detectable coronary artery calcification (CAC), but without manifest CVD, will be randomised (1:1) to receive daily MK-7 (333 µg/day) or placebo tablets for 3 years. Health examinations are scheduled at baseline, and after 1, 2 and 3 years of intervention. Health examinations include cardiac CT scans, measurements of arterial stiffness, blood pressure, lung function, physical function, muscle strength, anthropometric measures, questionnaires on general health and dietary intake, and blood and urine sampling. The primary outcome is progression of CAC from baseline to 3-year follow-up. The trial has 89% power to detect a between-group difference of at least 15%. Secondary outcomes are bone mineral density, pulmonary function and biomarkers of insulin resistance. ETHICS AND DISSEMINATION: Oral MK-7 supplementation is considered safe and has not been found to cause severe adverse events. The Ethical Committee of the Capital Region (H-21033114) approved the protocol. Written informed consent is obtained from all participants and the trial is conducted in accordance with the Declaration of Helsinki II. Both negative and positive findings will be reported. TRIAL REGISTRATION NUMBER: NCT05259046.","author_count":14,"contributors":["Kampmann, Freja Bach","Thysen, Sanne Marie","Nielsen, Camilla Friis Bryde","Kofoed, Klaus Fuglsang","Køber, Lars","Pham, Michael Huy Cuong","Vaag, Allan","Jørgensen, Niklas Rye","Petersen, Janne","Jacobsen, Rikke Kart","Kårhus, Line Lund","Diederichsen, Axel Cosmus Pyndt","Frimodt-Møller, Marie","Linneberg, Allan"],"cuid":["S02-099.91-698217"],"filters":{"added":"2023-08","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Linneberg, Allan"],"country":["Sweden"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Lund University","Skåne University Hospital"],"keyword":["Bone Density","Calcium bone","Cardiology","Coronary Artery Disease drug therapy","Denmark","Dietary Supplements","Double Blind Method","Female","General endocrinology","Humans","Lung","Male","Nutrition dietetics","Randomized Controlled Trials as Topic","Vascular Calcification prevention control","Vitamin K","Vitamin K 2 pharmacology"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-SDR"],"OT":["Steno Diabetes Centre, Gentofte, Denmark."],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-SDR","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"study protocol of the intervitamink trial a danish population based randomised double blinded placebo controlled trial of the effects of vitamin k menaquinone 000000000007 supplementation on cardiovascular metabolic and bone health","src":["ku","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1136/bmjopen-2023-071885","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-099.91-698217","identifier":[{"id":"37208133","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC10201225","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"85159691396","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-