:"Breen","name":"Breen, Gerome","rank":176,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 12 4","first":"Cynthia M.","key":"bulikcynthiampau","last":"Bulik","name":"Bulik, Cynthia M.","rank":177,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["36324647"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.bpsgos.2021.09.001","issn":["26671743"],"issue":"4","journal":"Biological Psychiatry Global Open Science","pages":"368-378","publisher":"Elsevier","status":"p","title":"Biological Psychiatry Global Open Science","title_org":"Biological Psychiatry: Global Open Science","volume":"2"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85129769148"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Miscellaneous","All Non-Profit Organisations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-NP","DI-NP-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Miscellaneous","Non-Profit Organisations","Other Research","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-f6342e2e-b543-444c-bebd-194cbb3d69d5","ku-34a1c6f2-fb4d-4618-b050-886bfe5f95e5"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Common Genetic Variation and Age of Onset of Anorexia Nervosa","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-100.00-672841","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"Multiple chemical sensitivity (MCS) is a multifactorial somatic disorder characterized by physical reactions triggered by even extremely low levels of different airborne chemicals. In most individuals with MCS, these reactions have substantial negative impact on social, occupational, and everyday life often including limited or no engagement in physical activities. The aim of this study was to explore associations between MCS and objective measurements of anthropometry, cardiorespiratory health, and physical performance. From the Danish population-based cohort DanFunD counting 9656 participants aged 18-76 years, 1.95% (n = 188) were categorized as MCS individuals (MCS All). Of those 188, 109 participants were subcategorized as having MCS without functional somatic disorders (FSD) (MCS with no comorbid FSD). The remaining study population without any FSD were regarded controls. We used adjusted multiple linear regression analyses to evaluate associations between MCS and anthropometry, cardiorespiratory fitness, and physical performance. Compared with the general population, MCS All had less optimal body composition, increased risk of obesity, impaired cardiorespiratory fitness, and physical performance which was not seen in MCS with no comorbid FSD. MCS individuals may be inhibited to maintain an active lifestyle which can increase risk of obesity and consequently have negatively impact on general health, which may not be the case among MCS with no comorbid FSD.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Bjerregaard, Anne A","Petersen, Marie Weinreich","Skovbjerg, Sine","Gormsen, Lise Kirstine","Cedeño-Laurent, José G","Jørgensen, Torben","Linneberg, Allan","Dantoft, Thomas Meinertz"],"cuid":["S02-100.00-018505"],"filters":{"added":"2022-09","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["America, North","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Bjerregaard, Anne A"],"country":["United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Harvard University"],"keyword":["DanFunD","Danish","Functional somatic disorders","Humans","Inhalation","Life Style","MSC","Multiple Chemical Sensitivity epidemiology","Multiple chemical sensitivity","Obesity","Physical Functional Performance","Prevalence","Symptoms"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"physiological health and physical performance in multiple chemical sensitivity described in the general population","src":["au","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3390/ijerph19159039","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-100.00-018505","identifier":[{"id":"35897408","type":"pmid"},{"id":"000839227800001","type":"wos"},{"id":"PMC9331319","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"85135371433","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-504b304c-f936-460d-9fb9-b620c1c27f4e","ku-4fc4586e-2fca-43bf-a855-f68adbc18764"],"keyword":["DANISH","DanFunD","Humans","INHALATION","Life Style","MSC","Multiple Chemical Sensitivity/epidemiology","Obesity","PREVALENCE","Physical Functional Performance","SYMPTOMS","functional somatic disorders","multiple chemical sensitivity"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-5ED30701467717396CD904164F7DCBFB"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/317206287/ijerph_19_09039.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3390/ijerph19159039","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.au.dk/ws/files/335002656/Physiological_Health_and_Physical_Performance_in_Multiple_Chemical_Sensitivity_Described_in_the_General_Population.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2022","yearSub":"2022"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital - Bispebjerg and Frederiksberg"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - Clinic for Functional Disorder"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"central denmark region","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CDR","l3nl":"Central Denmark Region","l3nn":"Central Denmark Region","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Central Denmark Region","namevar":["Aarhus University Hospital"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CDR","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"us","key":"harvard university","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"Harvard University","used":1},{"affno":"5","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Public Health, Section of Social Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Anne A.","key":"bjerregaardpau","last":"Bjerregaard","name":"Bjerregaard, Anne A.","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2