094fb8d1a3","sdu-3d7e5705-c396-4a68-aca9-29471e1f5090"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"A multi-layer functional genomic analysis to understand noncoding genetic variation in lipids","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-092.23-047671","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"Background: Persistent physical symptoms (e.g. pain, fatigue) are prevalent in the population and some persons may develop a functional somatic disorder (FSD). We still need to explore the limits between general bodily sensations and FSD, and great controversies exist as regard delimitation, occurrence, risk factors, prognosis, and costs of FSD in the general population. This is mainly due to the lack of focused, sufficient powered, population-based epidemiological studies. Material and Methods: The DanFunD study is the largest focused population-based study on FSD and has the potential to answer these crucial questions regarding the FSD disorders. DanFunD has its origin in the Copenhagen area of Denmark and was initiated in 2009 by an interdisciplinary team of researchers including basic scientists, clinical researchers, epidemiologists, and public health researchers. A population-based cohort of nearly 10,000 people have filled in detailed questionnaires, gone through a thorough health examination, and a biobank is established. The cohort was re-examined after five years. Results:The prevalence of FSD in the Danish population is about 10-15% and is twice as common in women as in men. Persons with FSD report impaired daily activities and low self-perceived health, which qualifies FSD as a major public health problem. The research plan to unravel the risk factors for FSD employs a bio-psycho-social approach according to a detailed plan. Preliminary results are presented, and work is in progress. Likewise, plans for assessing prognosis and health care costs are provided. Conclusion: We invite researchers in the field to collaborate on this unique data material.","author_count":21,"contributors":["Jørgensen, Torben","Dantoft, Thomas Meinertz","Petersen, Marie Weinreich","Eriksen Benros, Michael","Poulsen, Chalotte Heinsvig","Falgaard Eplov, Lene","Gormsen, Lise Kirstine","Frostholm, Lisbeth","Carstensen, Tina","Holm Eliasen, Marie","Kårhus, Line Lund","Skovbjerg, Sine","Bjerregaard, Anne Ahrendt","Brix, Susanne","Linneberg, Allan","Fink, Per"],"cuid":["S03-092.65-021584"],"filters":{"added":"2022-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":3,"corresponding_author":["Jørgensen, Torben"],"keyword":["Bodily distress","Epidemiology","Epidemology","Functional somatic disorders","General population","Long term","Population based studies","Primary care","Public health","Symptoms"],"level":"sci","mra":["med","sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR"],"OT":["Copenhagen Research Centre for Mental Health"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR","DI-U-AU","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"examine the public health impacts of functional somatic disorders using the danfund study","src":["au","dtu","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85139887611","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S03-092.65-021584","identifier":[{"id":"85139887611","type":"scopus"},{"id":"36245407","type":"pmid"},{"id":"000869293200023","type":"wos"}],"ids":["au-7a370655-0da1-4094-b99b-962ba8c01d20","dtu-96878b61-719a-4cdb-bcb5-3ddf427c16d6","ku-37704ccf-dae7-409a-b1ee-09ae171034fb"],"keyword":["BODILY DISTRESS","Epidemology","GENERAL-POPULATION","LONG-TERM","PRIMARY-CARE","Population-based studies","SYMPTOMS","epidemiology","functional somatic disorders","public health"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science","Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-6-1504D5F6DB6D65F6B1A37115908F081B"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2022","yearSub":"2022"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":