{"abstract":"Abstract Thermodynamic and kinetic control of a chemical process is the key to access desired products and states. Changes are made when a desired product is not accessible; one may manipulate the reaction with additional reagents, catalysts and/or protecting groups. Here we report the use of carbon dioxide to accelerate cyanohydrin synthesis under neutral conditions with an insoluble cyanide source (KCN) without generating toxic HCN. Under inert atmosphere, the reaction is essentially not operative due to the unfavored equilibrium. The utility of CO2-mediated selective cyanohydrin synthesis was further showcased by broadening Kiliani?Fischer synthesis under neutral conditions. This protocol offers an easy access to a variety of polyols, cyanohydrins, linear alkylnitriles, by simply starting from alkyl- and arylaldehydes, KCN and an atmospheric pressure of CO2.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Juhl, Martin","Petersen, Allan R.","Lee, Ji Woong"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-399900"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Carbon dioxide","Elongation","Homologation"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"co000000000002 enabled cyanohydrin synthesis and facile iterative homologation reactions","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-399900","identifier":[{"id":"85094177725","type":"scopus"},{"id":"32812672","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-0ac4f878-1a07-4c5c-9a42-4df4f0739999"],"keyword":["carbon dioxide","cyanohydrins","elongation","homologation","xanthate"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-09C18FA8BBF940592DB1DFF38BA65AC0"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2021","yearSub":"2021"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Chemistry, Department of Chemistry"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Martin","key":"juhlpau","last":"Juhl","locid":"5a99742e-d2c4-47ec-807a-88cc52d3ff71","name":"Juhl, Martin","orcid":"0000-0001-5395-9627","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Allan R.","key":"petersenpau","last":"Petersen","locid":"d1db46ef-d4a8-44f6-82b3-23da5615625a","name":"Petersen, Allan R.","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Ji-Woong","key":"leepau","last":"Lee","locid":"be232f36-45bb-4dda-9f45-f4885a4301e4","name":"Lee, Ji Woong","name_org":"Lee, Ji-Woong","orcid":"0000-0001-6177-4569","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["32812672"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1002/chem.202003623","issn":["09476539","15213765"],"issn_org":["09476539"],"issue":"1","journal":"Chemistry - A European Journal","pages":"228-232","status":"p","title":"Chemistry - A European Journal","title_org":"Chemistry: A European Journal","volume":"27"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85094177725"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-0ac4f878-1a07-4c5c-9a42-4df4f0739999"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"CO2-Enabled Cyanohydrin Synthesis and Facile Iterative Homologation Reactions","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-399900","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"Background: The use of hybrid PET/MRI for clinical staging is growing in several cancer forms and, consequently, PET/MRI has also gained interest in the assessment of non-small cell lung cancer (NSCLC) and lung lesions. However, lung evaluation with PET/MRI is associated with challenges related to technical issues and diagnostic image quality. We, therefore, investigated the published literature on PET/MRI for clinical staging in NSCLC or lung nodule detection specifically addressing diagnostic accuracy and technical issues. Methods: The data originates from a systematic search performed in PubMed/MEDLINE, Embase, and Cochrane Library on hybrid PET/MRI in patients with cancer for a scoping review published earlier (https://doi.org/10.1007/s00259-019-04402-8). Studies in English and German evaluating the diagnostic performance of hybrid PET/MRI for NSCLC or lung nodule detection in cancer patients were selected. Data reported in peer-reviewed journals without restrictions to year of publication were included. Results: A total of 3138 publications were identified from which 116 published 2012–2018 were included. Of these, nine studies addressed PET/MRI in NSCLC (4) or lung nodule detection (5). Overall, PET/MRI did not provide advantages in preoperative T- and N-staging in NSCLC compared to PET/CT. The data on M-staging were too few for conclusions to be drawn. The lung nodule detection rate of PET/MRI was comparable to that of PET/CT for FDG-avid nodules larger than 10 mm, but the sensitivity of PET/MRI for detection of non-FDG-avid nodules smaller than 5 mm was low. Conclusion: PET/MRI did not provide advantages in T- and N-staging of NSCLC compared to PET/CT. PET/MRI had a comparable sensitivity for detection of FDG-avid lung nodules and nodules over 10 mm, but PET/CT yielded a higher detection rate in non FDG-avid lung nodules under 5 mm. With PET/MRI, the overall detection rate for lung nodules in various cancer types remains inferior to that of PET/CT due to the lower diagnostic performance of MRI than CT in the lungs.","author_count":9,"contributors":["Dahlsgaard-Wallenius, Sara Elisabeth","Hildebrandt, Malene Grubbe","Johansen, Allan","Vilstrup, Mie Holm","Petersen, Henrik","Gerke, Oke","Høilund-Carlsen, Poul Flemming","Morsing, Anni","Andersen, Thomas Lund"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-627373"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Dahlsgaard-Wallenius, Sara Elisabeth"],"keyword":["18F FDG","NSCLC","PET CT","PET MRI"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-NOVO"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-PR-NOVO","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"hybrid pet mri in non small cell lung cancer nsclc and lung nodules a literature review","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/172897224/EJNM_D_19_01315_R3_1_.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-627373","identifier":[{"id":"32719914","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85088645187","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["sdu-bcec58a8-9c6d-4e29-aa05-1d82a64d9a6b"],"keyword":["18F-FDG","Lung lesions","NSCLC","PET/CT","PET/MRI"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-07707BF9B7D6511069D985065B1E2C1C"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/172897224/EJNM_D_19_01315_R3_1_.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2021","yearSub":"2021"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research, KI, OUH, Research unit of Clinical Physiology and Nuclear Medicine (Odense)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"novo nordisk","l2":"DI-PR","l2n":"Private Research","l3":"DI-PR-NOVO","l3nl":"Novo Nordisk","l3nn":"Novo Nordisk","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Novo Nordisk","namevar":["Novo Nordisk"],"nora_code":"DI-PR-NOVO","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Sara E.","key":"dahlsgaardwalleniuspau","last":"Dahlsgaard-Wallenius","locid":"09dbda03-897a-47e9-8ce4-7c2e523c417c","name":"Dahlsgaard-Wallenius, Sara Elisabeth","name_org":"Dahlsgaard-Wallenius, Sara E.","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Malene Grubbe","key":"hildebrandtpau","last":"Hildebrandt","locid":"89ec551d-ddfe-45e8-983a-f2bbc54f8a0e","name":"Hildebrandt, Malene Grubbe","orcid":"0000-0003-2720-9018","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Allan","key":"johansenpau","last":"Johansen","locid":"dc7a1a61-b703-48ec-bd87-c92b55784133","name":"Johansen, Allan","orcid":"0000-0002-3622-057X","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Mie Holm","key":"vilstruppau","last":"Vilstrup","locid":"9ceb6215-deb0-460f-8c59-bbc32b7dca27","name":"Vilstrup, Mie Holm","orcid":"0000-0002-4760-0068","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Henrik","key":"petersenpau","last":"Petersen","locid":"ea635371-4294-4379-9655-3da538fecf13","name":"Petersen, Henrik","orcid":"0000-0002-1118-1500","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Oke","key":"gerkepau","last":"Gerke","locid":"596baeb1-6754-4d53-948f-30470dd1d976","name":"Gerke, Oke","orcid":"0000-0001-6335-3303","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Poul Flemming","key":"høilundcarlsenpau","last":"Høilund-Carlsen","locid":"a1ff65cf-cdaa-4192-bef3-a915cfe6cceb","name":"Høilund-Carlsen, Poul Flemming","orcid":"0000-0001-7420-2367","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Anni","key":"morsingpau","last":"Morsing","locid":"eb322987-0180-4887-8e6c-9c9cb4f6ef39","name":"Morsing, Anni","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Thomas Lund","key":"andersenpau","last":"Andersen","locid":"8a904314-798c-4e45-9559-b997a4e1d5c7","name":"Andersen, Thomas Lund","orcid":"0000-0002-2860-6317","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["32719914"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/s00259-020-04955-z","issn":["16197070","16197089"],"issn_org":["16197070"],"issue":"2","journal":"European Journal of Nuclear Medicine and Molecular Imaging","pages":"584-591","publisher":"Springer","status":"p","title":"European Journal of Nuclear Medicine and Molecular Imaging","volume":"48"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85088645187"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Private Research","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-PR-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Novo Nordisk","Private Research","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-bcec58a8-9c6d-4e29-aa05-1d82a64d9a6b"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Hybrid PET/MRI in non-small cell lung cancer (NSCLC) and lung nodules—a literature review","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-627373","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"Multiple chemical sensitivity (MCS) is a multisystem syndrome, and limited knowledge of its pathophysiology exists. Based on the population-based Danish cohort DanFunD, this study investigated metabolic health in people with MCS compared to individuals who did not have MCS. From 9656 cohort participants aged 18-76 years old, 1.95% were categorized as MCS individuals with comorbid functional somatic disorders (MCS +FSD, n = 188), and 1.13% were categorized as MCS without functional somatic disorders (MCS ÷FSD, n = 109). MCS was characterized based on three criteria: the experience of symptoms upon exposure to common odors and airborne chemicals, symptoms related the central nervous systems and others organ symptoms, and significant impact on every day, social, and occupational life. The remaining study population without MCS or any other functional somatic disorders were regarded as controls. We used adjusted multiple linear regression with link-function to evaluate the associations between lipid and glucose metabolism markers and MCS. We also tested the odds ratio of metabolic syndrome in MCS. Results did not point to statistically significant associations between lipid biomarkers or metabolic syndrome and both MCS groups compared to the controls. We found that MCS individuals may be more insulin resistant and that MCS ÷ FSD may have an impaired glucose metabolism when compared to controls.","author_count":13,"contributors":["Bjerregaard, Anne Ahrendt","Petersen, Marie Weinreich","Gormsen, Lise Kirstine","Skovbjerg, Sine","Jørgensen, Niklas Rye","Linneberg, Allan","Cedoño-Laurent, José G.","Torben, Jørgensen","Dantoft, Thomas Meinertz"],"cuid":["S02-096.28-027125"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["America, North","OECD"],"country":["United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Harvard University"],"keyword":["DanFunD","Functional somatic disorders","MSC","Multiple chemical sensitivity"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"GV":["DI-GV-ALL","DI-GV-SSI"],"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-GV-SSI","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"insulin resistance is associated with multiple chemical sensitivity in a danish population based study danfund","src":["au","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3390/ijerph182312654","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-096.28-027125","identifier":[{"id":"85120045971","type":"scopus"},{"id":"34886380","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC8657139","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["au-c7682a46-e7c9-4f31-9a14-731ac9feb021","ku-e902d52f-9cfc-4868-a861-9a3c3f4607c9"],"keyword":["DanFunD","Functional somatic disorders","MSC","Multiple chemical sensitivity"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-CA26AE75196301947F279D9D32EA3E0C"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3390/ijerph182312654","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/286496579/ijerph_18_12654_v2.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2021","yearSub":"2021"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital - Bispebjerg and Frederiksberg"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"ssi statens serum institut