ersen, Marie Weinreich","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","first":"Marie W.","key":"petersenmariewpau","last":"Petersen","name":"Petersen, Marie W.","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3 4","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Lise Kirstine","key":"gormsenlisekirstinepau","last":"Gormsen","locid":"5516e253-cc95-468b-b53d-b6d1758f9884","name":"Gormsen, Lise Kirstine","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Sine","key":"skovbjergsinepau","last":"Skovbjerg","name":"Skovbjerg, Sine","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5","first":"Niklas R.","key":"jørgensenniklasryepau","last":"Jørgensen","locid":"3dc68a95-e26c-4b82-a4f0-7548313f8045","name":"Jørgensen, Niklas Rye","name_org":"Jørgensen, Niklas R.","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5","first":"Allan","key":"linnebergallanpau","last":"Linneberg","locid":"09da8aa6-fd95-4ace-a2f1-19f38d7d3f9e","name":"Linneberg, Allan","orcid":"0000-0002-0994-0184","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"6","corresponding":null,"first":"José G.","key":"cedoñolaurentjoségpau","last":"Cedoño-Laurent","name":"Cedoño-Laurent, José G.","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"6","first":"José G.","key":"cedeñolaurentjoségpau","last":"Cedeño-Laurent","name":"Cedeño-Laurent, José G.","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5","first":"Torben","key":"jørgensentorbenpau","last":"Jørgensen","locid":"368044df-7d2b-4204-9103-8c0272f1baca","name":"Jørgensen, Torben","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jørgensen","key":"torbenjørgensenpau","last":"Torben","name":"Torben, Jørgensen","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Thomas Meinertz","key":"dantoftthomasmeinertzpau","last":"Dantoft","name":"Dantoft, Thomas Meinertz","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Thomas M.","key":"dantoftthomasmpau","last":"Dantoft","name":"Dantoft, Thomas M.","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["34886380"],"pub":{"doi":"10.3390/ijerph182312654","issn":["16604601","16617827"],"issn_org":["16617827"],"issue":"23","journal":"International Journal of Environmental Research and Public Health","paperid":"12654","publisher":"Multidisciplinary Digital Publishing Institute (MDPI)","status":"p","title":"International Journal of Environmental Research and Public Health","volume":"18"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85120045971"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Governmental Institutions","All Hospitals","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","Central Denmark Region","DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-GV-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Governmental Institutions","Hospitals","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-c7682a46-e7c9-4f31-9a14-731ac9feb021","ku-e902d52f-9cfc-4868-a861-9a3c3f4607c9"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Insulin Resistance Is Associated with Multiple Chemical Sensitivity in a Danish Population-Based Study—DanFunD","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-096.28-027125","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"Type 2 diabetes mellitus represents a multi-dimensional challenge for European and global societies alike. Building on an iterative six-step disease management process that leverages feedback loops and utilizes commodity digital tools, the PDM-ProValue study program demonstrated that integrated personalized diabetes management, or iPDM, can improve the standard of care for persons living with diabetes in a sustainable way. The novel “iPDM Goes Europe” consortium strives to advance iPDM adoption by (1) implementing the concept in a value-based healthcare setting for the treatment of persons living with type 2 diabetes, (2) providing tools to assess the patient's physical and mental health status, and (3) exploring new avenues to take advantage of emerging big data resources.","author_count":19,"contributors":["Jones, Allan","Bardram, Jakob Eyvind","Bækgaard, Per","Cramer-Petersen, Claus Lundgaard","Skinner, Timothy","Vrangbæk, Karsten","Starr, Laila","Nørgaard, Kirsten","Lind, Nanna","Bechmann Christensen, Merete","Glümer, Charlotte","Wang-Sattler, Rui","Laxy, Michael","Brander, Erik","Heinemann, Lutz","Heise, Tim","Schliess, Freimut","Ladewig, Katharina","Kownatka, Dagmar"],"cuid":["S02-100.00-035974"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Jones, Allan"],"country":["Germany","Switzerland"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","EIT Health Germany","F. Hoffmann-La Roche","German Center for Diabetes Research","Helmholtz Zentrum München - German Research Center for Environmental Health","Institute for Diabetes and Obesity (IDO)","Profil","Roche Diabetes Care GmbH"],"keyword":["Artificial intelligence","Delivery of Health Care Integrated","Diabetes Mellitus Type 2","Patient Reported Outcome Measures","Value based health insurance"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci","soc"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-NP","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-ZEA"],"NP":["DI-NP-ALL","DI-NP-NOVO"],"OT":["Steno Diabetes Centre, Gentofte, Denmark."],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-ZEA","DI-NP-NOVO","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"integrated personalized diabetes management goes europe a multi disciplinary approach to innovating type 000000000002 diabetes care in europe","src":["dtu","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"djr","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.pcd.2020.10.008","version":"Published Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["The author(s) disclosed receipt of the following financial support for the research, authorship, and/or publication of this article: iPDM-GO has received funding from the European Institute for Innovation and Technology (EIT) through its Knowledge and Innovation Community (KIC) EIT Health. The EIT is a body of the European Union which receives support from the European Union’s Horizon 2020 research and innovation programme. The authors thank Annette Moritz from Roche Diabetes Care Deutschland GmbH and Bettina Blees from EIT Health Germany GmbH for critical review and editorial assistance in developing the manuscript. We further acknowledge the management support from Claudia Schacht (Managing Director) and Julia Büch (Project Manager) from LINQ Management GmbH."],"id":"S02-100.00-035974","identifier":[{"id":"85095835886","type":"scopus"},{"id":"33184011","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["dtu-9406b24a-fa56-4df0-a637-404a8dfba5df","ku-be8865bf-19a6-4f39-88b3-fc0e80bdf124"],"keyword":["Artificial intelligence","Delivery of health care, integrated","Diabetes mellitus, type 2","Patient reported outcome measures","Value-based health insurance"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology","Social Science"],"noi":[