{"author_count":3,"contributors":["Køster, Allan"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-084556"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["hum"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"krop og sorg om kropshukommelsens betydning for relationen til den afdøde","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dba","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://klim.dk/bog/menneskets_sorg.htm%23","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-084556","ids":["aau-76d34fd4-3cdc-4622-ac73-099069da8ead"],"lang":"Danish","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities"],"noi":["Local-1-1-460245083F82676EBBE893F2C1D8154C"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Humanities","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences and Humanities, Department of Communication and Psychology","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences and Humanities, Department of Communication and Psychology, Qualitative Studies"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Allan","key":"køsterpau","last":"Køster","locid":"8d28c411-9345-4852-b4d0-27d081359e65","name":"Køster, Allan","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Anders","key":"petersenpedh","last":"Petersen","name":"Petersen, Anders","rank":2,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Svend","key":"brinkmannpedh","last":"Brinkmann","name":"Brinkmann, Svend","rank":3,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"isbn":["9788772047263"],"pages":"237-256","publisher":"Klim","status":"p","subtitle":"Et vilkår i forandring","title":"Menneskets Sorg"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-76d34fd4-3cdc-4622-ac73-099069da8ead"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Krop og sorg : Om kropshukommelsens betydning for relationen til den afdøde","type":"Book Chapter","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-084556","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"Patients with severe COVID-19 have overwhelmed healthcare systems worldwide. We hypothesized that machine learning (ML) models could be used to predict risks at different stages of management and thereby provide insights into drivers and prognostic markers of disease progression and death. From a cohort of approx. 2.6 million citizens in Denmark, SARS-CoV-2 PCR tests were performed on subjects suspected for COVID-19 disease; 3944 cases had at least one positive test and were subjected to further analysis. SARS-CoV-2 positive cases from the United Kingdom Biobank was used for external validation. The ML models predicted the risk of death (Receiver Operation Characteristics-Area Under the Curve, ROC-AUC) of 0.906 at diagnosis, 0.818, at hospital admission and 0.721 at Intensive Care Unit (ICU) admission. Similar metrics were achieved for predicted risks of hospital and ICU admission and use of mechanical ventilation. Common risk factors, included age, body mass index and hypertension, although the top risk features shifted towards markers of shock and organ dysfunction in ICU patients. The external validation indicated fair predictive performance for mortality prediction, but suboptimal performance for predicting ICU admission. ML may be used to identify drivers of progression to more severe disease and for prognostication patients in patients with COVID-19. We provide access to an online risk calculator based on these findings.","author_count":35,"contributors":["Jimenez-Solem, Espen","Petersen, Tonny Studsgaard","Hansen, Casper","Hansen, Christian","Lioma, Christina","Igel, Christian","Boomsma, Wouter","Krause, Oswin","Lorenzen, Stephan Sloth","Selvan, Raghavendra","Petersen, Janne","Nyeland, Martin Erik","Ankarfeldt, Mikkel Zöllner","Virenfeldt, Gert Mehl","Winther-Jensen, Matilde","Linneberg, Allan","Mehdipour Ghazi, Mostafa","Detlefsen, Nicki","Lauritzen, Andreas D.","Smith, Abraham George","de Bruijne, Marleen","Ibragimov, Bulat","Petersen, Jens","Lillholm, Martin","Middleton, Jon","Mogensen, Stine Hasling","Thorsen-Meyer, Hans-Christian","Perner, Anders","Helleberg, Marie","Kaas-Hansen, Benjamin Skov","Bonde, Mikkel","Bonde, Alexander","Pai, Akshay Sadananda Uppinakudru","Nielsen, Mads","Sillesen, Martin"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-399979"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"OT":["Danish Medicines Agency, Copenhagen"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"developing and validating covid 000000000019 adverse outcome risk prediction models from a bi national european cohort of 000000005594 patients","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/s41598-021-81844-x","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-399979","identifier":[{"id":"33547335","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC7864944","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"85100461546","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-0ae374c8-ae42-48c3-93d9-78cb6f45d2dd"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-5C13440B5AF7F127AF61F236396AAFC2"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/s41598-021-81844-x","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/256879260/Developing_and_validating_COVID_19_adverse_outcome_risk_prediction_models_from_a_bi_national_European_cohort_of_5594_patients.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2021","yearSub":"2021"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capi