name":"Philips, Allan","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Sine Olsson","key":"heltbergsineolssonpau","last":"Heltberg","name":"Heltberg, Sine Olsson","rank":13,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Mariya","key":"krestyanskamariyapau","last":"Krestyanska","name":"Krestyanska, Mariya","rank":14,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Pernille Eva","key":"agerskovpernilleevapau","last":"Agerskov","name":"Agerskov, Pernille Eva","rank":15,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Eva Ask","key":"olesenevaaskpau","last":"Olesen","name":"Olesen, Eva Ask","rank":16,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"issue":"2019/26","pages":"100","place":"København","publisher":"Københavns Universitet","repno":"IFRO udredning, 2019/26","series":"IFRO udredning","status":"p"},"review":"No Review","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Technical University of Denmark","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-7753e0ea-2237-405c-91f7-8ab2ebdd23e6","ku-fb076016-b8dd-4fa7-be32-584d1028736d"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Situationsbeskrivelse af den danske fiskeri-, akvakultur og fiskeindustrisektor: : Den Europæiske Hav- og Fiskerifond 2021-2027","type":"Report","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-085.71-035331","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"CONTEXT: The lack of sensitive and robust analytical methods has hindered the reliable quantification of estrogen metabolites in subjects with low concentrations. OBJECTIVE: To establish sex-specific reference ranges for estrone (E1) and estradiol (E2) throughout life and to evaluate sex-differences using the state-of-the-art liquid chromatography tandem mass spectrometry (LC-MS/MS) method for quantification of E1, E2, and estriol (E3). DESIGN: LC-MS/MS method development and construction of estrogen reference ranges. SETTINGS: Population-based cross-sectional cohorts from the greater Copenhagen and Aarhus areas. PARTICIPANTS: Healthy participants aged 3 months to 61 years (n = 1838). RESULTS: An isotope diluted LC-MS/MS method was developed and validated for measurements of serum E1, E2, and E3. Limits of detections (LODs) were 3 pmol/L (E1), 4 pmol/L (E2), and 12 pmol/L (E3), respectively. This sensitive method made it possible to differentiate between male and female concentration levels of E1 and E2 in children. In girls, E2 levels ranged from <LOD to 100 pmol/L during mini-puberty, whereas it was ≤20 pmol/L during childhood. E1 and E2 increased with age and pubertal breast stage and varied during the menstrual cycle; E1 was lower than E2 in girls and premenopausal women, and higher than E2 in postmenopausal women. In boys, E1 and E2 increased with age and pubertal stage, whereas little changes with age were observed in men. High E3 concentrations were confirmed in pregnant women. CONCLUSION: Reference ranges of simultaneous quantification of E1 and E2 by this novel specific and highly sensitive LC-MS/MS method provide an invaluable tool in clinical practice and in future research studies.","author_count":14,"contributors":["Frederiksen, Hanne","Johannsen, Trine Holm","Andersen, Stine Ehlern","Albrethsen, Jakob","Landersoe, Selma Kløve","Petersen, Jørgen Holm","Andersen, Anders Nyboe","Vestergaard, Esben Thyssen","Schjørring, Mia Elbek","Linneberg, 