en Thyssen","key":"vestergaardesbenthyssenpau","last":"Vestergaard","locid":"2cbff962-cbb0-43fa-8fc3-648dc685070a","name":"Vestergaard, Esben Thyssen","orcid":"0000-0003-4263-1815","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Mia Elbek","key":"schjørringmiaelbekpau","last":"Schorring","locid":"f7c4212d-ba6e-4f6c-9bcb-1eb920be645d","name":"Schjørring, Mia Elbek","name_org":"Schorring, Mia Elbek","orcid":"0009-0002-6614-857X","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Mia Elbek","key":"schorringmiaelbekpau","last":"Schorring","name":"Schorring, Mia Elbek","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Allan","key":"linnebergallanpau","last":"Linneberg","locid":"09da8aa6-fd95-4ace-a2f1-19f38d7d3f9e","name":"Linneberg, Allan","orcid":"0000-0002-0994-0184","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Katharina M","key":"mainkatharinampau","last":"Main","locid":"1770eebd-1659-4088-b44c-c9de22a4bb0b","name":"Main, Katharina M.","name_org":"Main, Katharina M","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Anna-Maria","key":"anderssonannamariapau","last":"Andersson","name":"Andersson, Anna-Maria","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Anders","key":"juulanderspau","last":"Juul","locid":"f9b11983-c7c8-4111-b119-4de471572898","name":"Juul, Anders","orcid":"0000-0002-0534-4350","rank":13,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["31720688"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1210/clinem/dgz196","issn":["0021972X","19457197"],"issn_org":["0021972X"],"issue":"3","journal":"Journal of Clinical Endocrinology and Metabolism","pages":"754-768","paperid":"dgz196","publisher":"Endocrine Society","status":"p","title":"Journal of Clinical Endocrinology and Metabolism","title_org":"The Journal of clinical endocrinology and metabolism","volume":"105"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85079201858"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-d0fdd103-1cd3-4d95-a4fe-b4bdd56f0a62","ku-4a68d78d-b1d6-41cb-a838-71baf337dbd1"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Sex-specific Estrogen Levels and Reference Intervals from Infancy to Late Adulthood Determined by LC-MS/MS","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-100.00-027825","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"INTRODUCTION: Infective endocarditis (IE) has high mortality, partly due to delayed diagnosis. No biomarker can identify IE in patients with fever and clinical picture of infection. To find putative biomarkers we analyzed serum levels of two proteins found in cardiac valves, fibulin-1 (n = 696) and osteoprotegerin (n = 689) among patients on clinical suspicion of IE. Proteomic analyses were performed in 24 patients with bacteremia, 12 patients with definite IE and 12 patients with excluded IE. METHODS: Fibulin-1 and osteoprotegerin and were studied by enzyme linked immunosorbent assay (ELISA). Proteomic analyses were conducted by 2-dimensional gel electrophoresis (2D-PAGE) and label free quantitative liquid chromatography - tandem mass spectrometry (LFQ LC-MS/MS). Controls had bacteremia and excluded IE. RESULTS: Osteoprotegerin levels were significantly increased in IE patients compared with non-IE patients. Fibulin-1 showed no difference. 2D-PAGE showed significant differences of 6 proteoforms: haptoglobin, haptoglobin-related protein, α-2-macroglobulin, apolipoprotein A-I and ficolin-3. LFQ LC-MS/MS analysis revealed significant level changes of 7 proteins: apolipoprotein L1, complement C1q subcomponent B and C, leukocyte immunoglobulin-like receptor subfamily A member 3, neuropilin-2, multimerin-1 and adiponectin. CONCLUSIONS: The concentration changes in a set of proteoforms/proteins suggest that stress and inflammation responses are perturbed in patients with IE compared to patients with bacteremia without IE.","author_count":9,"contributors":["Snipsøyr, Magnus Giske","Wiggers, Henrik","Ludvigsen, Maja","Stensballe, Allan","Vorum, Henrik","Poulsen, Steen Hvitfeldt","Rasmussen, Lars Melholt","Petersen, Eskild","Honoré, Bent"],"cuid":["S03-100.00-000365"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":3,"corresponding_author":["Honoré, Bent"],"keyword":["2D PAGE","Biomarkers","Infective endocarditis","LFQ LC MS MS","Non infective endocarditis","Serum proteomics"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-SDR"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-SDR","DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"towards identification of novel putative biomarkers for infective endocarditis by serum proteomic analysis","src":["aau","au","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.ijid.2020.02.026","version":"Published Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["The authors would like to thank Inge Kjærgaard Nielsen, Mona Britt Hansen, Lone Pødenphant and Anne-Marie Jakobsen for expert technical assistance. This work was supported by the Danish Heart Foundation (MGS), the John and Birthe Meyer Foundation (BH), the Eiler and Tatiana Filtenborg scholarship (MGS), the Copenhagen University fund for medical students (MGS) and the MEMBRANE Center at Aarhus University (BH). The Obelske family foundation, the Svend Andersen Foundation and the Spar Nord foundation are acknowledged for grants to the analytical platform enabling parts of this study (AS). The Danish Agency for Science and Higher Education (AS) is acknowledged for the funding to Danish National Mass Spectrometry Platform for Functional Proteomics enabling parts of this study (PRO-MS; grant no. 5072-00007B ). The mass spectrometry proteomics data have been deposited to the ProteomeXchange Consortium via the PRIDE ( Vizcaino et al., 2016 ) partner repository with the dataset identifier PXD010149."],"id":"S03-100.00-000365","identifier":[{"id":"32087365","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85084346204","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-070eca17-af1b-4200-b339-42bd974ba351","au-c1ccb2ea-142a-4b67-b