:"<i>HARS2</i> sequence variants identified in young individuals with severe sensorineural hearing impairment","type":"Conference Abstract","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-083774","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"Intraarticular gold may decrease osteoarthritis (OA) inflammation. Gold implant treatment correlate with clinically significant improvements in joint movement and pain management. Gold may decrease inflammation because of various mechanisms such as regulation of the NF-kB (nuclear factor kappa-light-chain-enhancer of activated B cells) pathway. The aim of this study was to investigate if treatment with intra-articular solid gold micro particles induces any significant proteomic changes in the synovial fluid (SF) in knee OA.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Rasmussen, Sten","Kaae Kristiansen, Martin","Andersen, Jacob Skallerup","Hansen, Joachim Bavnhøj","Petersen, Kristian Kjær","Arendt-Nielsen, Lars","Stensballe, Allan"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-094553"],"event":{"end":"2019-09-07","place":"Valencia, es","start":"2019-09-04","title":"Pain in Europe, Congress of the European Pain Federation, EFIC","year":"2019"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Gold microparticles","Knee osteoarthritis"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"a proteomic investigation of synovial fluid in patients with knee osteoarthritis treated with intra articular metallic gold micro particles","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dco","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/309701871/Rasmussen_et_al_2019_A_proteomic_investigation_of_synovial_fluid_in_patients_with_knee.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-094553","ids":["aau-9972740d-8e1c-497c-8f04-d30a8fb76fda"],"keyword":["Knee Osteoarthritis","gold microparticles"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Local-1-1-AA04E4A8D62830EC9C06569665DD0628"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/309701871/Rasmussen_et_al_2019_A_proteomic_investigation_of_synovial_fluid_in_patients_with_knee.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Aalborg University Hospital","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Aalborg University Hospital, Department of Orthopaedic Surgery","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Aalborg University Hospital, Klinik Hoved-Orto","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Department of Health Science and Technology, Center for Neuroplasticity and Pain","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Department of Health Science and Technology, Center for Sensory-Motor Interaction"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Sten","key":"rasmussenpau","last":"Rasmussen","locid":"05d1d595-13be-4295-8ad1-8d29206859c8","name":"Rasmussen, Sten","orcid":"0000-0002-8664-352X","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Martin","key":"kaaekristiansenpau","last":"Kaae Kristiansen","locid":"1baf9b35-a950-46ed-a17f-1f344d735567","name":"Kaae Kristiansen, Martin","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jacob Skallerup","key":"andersenpau","last":"Andersen","locid":"08c304cd-7865-4f96-9a93-64b48d329321","name":"Andersen, Jacob Skallerup","orcid":"0000-0002-9519-7146","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Joachim Bavnhøj","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","name":"Hansen, Joachim Bavnhøj","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Kristian Kjær","key":"petersenpau","last":"Petersen","locid":"03b38a92-c53c-4b31-a786-05e4893a3e14","name":"Petersen, Kristian Kjær","orcid":"0000-0003-4506-000X","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Lars","key":"arendtnielsenpau","last":"Arendt-Nielsen","locid":"1794f9ec-22f1-47af-96c1-88c23c3b06a2","name":"Arendt-Nielsen, Lars","orcid":"0000-0003-0892-1579","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Allan","key":"stensballepau","last":"Stensballe","locid":"31ce2dbc-d5bc-4266-8c26-1b38838c7346","name":"Stensballe, Allan","orcid":"0000-0002-9888-1955","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-9972740d-8e1c-497c-8f04-d30a8fb76fda"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"A proteomic investigation of synovial fluid in patients with knee osteoarthritis treated with intra-articular metallic gold micro particles","type":"Conference Poster","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-094553","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"Family studies have established that the heritability of blood pressure is significant and genome-wide association studies (GWAS) have identified numerous susceptibility loci, including one within the non-coding part of Rho GTPase-activating protein 42 gene (ARHGAP42) on chromosome 11q22.1. Arhgap42-deficient mice have significantly elevated blood pressure, but the phenotypic effects of human variants in the coding part of the gene are unknown. In a Danish cohort of carriers with apparently balanced chromosomal rearrangements, we identified a family where a reciprocal translocation t(11;18)(q22.1;q12.2) segregated with hypertension and obesity. Clinical re-examination revealed that four carriers (age 50–77 years) have had hypertension for several years along with an increased body mass index (34–43 kg/m 2 ). A younger carrier (age 23 years) had normal blood pressure and body mass index. Mapping of the chromosomal breakpoints with mate-pair and Sanger sequencing revealed truncation of ARHGAP42. A decreased expression level of ARHGAP42 mRNA in the blood was found in the translocation carriers relative to controls and allele-specific expression analysis showed monoallelic expression in the translocation carriers, confirming that the truncated allele of ARHGAP42 was not expressed. These findings support that haploinsufficiency of ARHGAP42 leads to an age-dependent hypertension. The other breakpoint truncated a regulatory domain of the CUGBP Elav-like family member 4 (CELF4) gene on chromosome 18q12.2 that harbours several GWAS signals for obesity. We thereby provide additional support for an obesity locus in the CELF4 domain.","author_count":13,"contributors":["Fjorder, Amanda S.","Rasmussen, Malene Bøgehus","Mehrjouy, Mana M.","Nazaryan-Petersen, Lusine","Hansen, Claus","Bak, Mads","Grarup, Niels","Nørremølle, Anne","Larsen, Lars Allan","Vestergaard, Henrik","Hansen, Torben","Tommerup, Niels","Bache, Iben"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-459485"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"haploinsufficiency of i arhgap000000000042 i is associated with hypertension","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"http://europepmc.org/Copyright","type":"rem","url":"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC6777610/pdf/41431_2019_Article_382.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-459485","identifier":[{"id":"85063326419","type":"scopus"},{"id":"000474847300017","type":"wos"},{"id":"30903111","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC6777610","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["ku-6e8c6baf-d0ef-485e-b4d4-ab5f023d54a8"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-5CC4014B8513275AF801C0BF711BD3CA"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"http://europepmc.org/Copyright","type":"rem","url":"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC6777610/pdf/41431_2019_Article_382.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2019","yearSub":"2019"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Cellular and Molecular Medicine, Medical Genetics Program"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Amanda S.","key":"fjorderamandaspau","last":"Fjorder","locid":"f9de1f16-491b-49ef-baa8-db4297291726","name":"Fjorder, Amanda S.","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Malene B.","key":"rasmussenmalenebøgehuspau","last":"Rasmussen","locid":"cbc0afb5-3f57-43c0-9c62-d513e2c6bcf1","name":"Rasmussen, Malene Bøgehus","name_org":"Rasmussen, Malene B.","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Mana M.","key":"mehrjouymanampau","last":"Mehrjouy","locid":"c574200c-2bbe-4273-8c3f-dded36efa39b","name":"Mehrjouy, Mana M.","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Lusine","key":"nazaryanpetersenlusinepau","last":"Nazaryan-Petersen","locid":"2df25b57-365c-436a-89aa-37a8db1a6548","name":"Nazaryan-Petersen, Lusine","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Claus","key":"hansenclauspau","last":"Hansen","locid":"f003dc69-a9de-4062-9b88-7f83ce439cf4","name":"Hansen, Claus","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Mads","key":"bakmadspau","last":"Bak","locid":"27735c1e-695f-402f-9776-be3185b87444","name":"Bak, Mads","orcid":"0000-0003-2762-1002","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Niels","key":"grarupnielspau","last":"Grarup","locid":"824a7159-a059-4de1-bf3f-e116ef59e0de","name":"Grarup, Niels","orcid":"0000-0001-5526-1070","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Anne","key":"nørremølleannepau","last":"Nørremølle","locid":"277a477a-5004-4189-b69c-a2942c25dad0","name":"Nørremølle, Anne","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Lars A.","key":"larsenlarsallanpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"78031d9d-4c66-4f3b-9dd4-e5aa1d6b19a5","name":"Larsen, Lars Allan","name_org":"Larsen, Lars A.","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Henrik","key":"vestergaardhenrikpau","last":"Vestergaard","locid":"9f96726b-f4da-443d-9645-43c6ad321468","name":"Vestergaard, Henrik","orcid":"0000-0003-3090-269X","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Torben","key":"hansentorbenpau","last":"Hansen","locid":"6b6bfff1-8b14-468b-af77-e71b375018e0","name":"Hansen, Torben","orcid":"0000-0001-8748-3831","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Niels","key":"tommerupnielspau","last":"Tommerup","locid":"a1378adf-8d70-4c4d-bf14-9e107b13fccb","name":"Tommerup, Niels","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Iben","key":"bacheibenpau","last":"Bache","locid":"bb160617-68f4-4c3a-aac6-4788391d391e","name":"Bache, Iben","orcid":"0000-0001-7562-8546","rank":13,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["30903111"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1038/s41431-019-0382-9","issn":["10184813","14765438"],"issn_org":["10184813"],"issue":"8","journal":"European Journal of Human Genetics","pages":"1296-1303","status":"p","title":"European Journal of Human Genetics","volume":"27"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85063326419"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-6e8c6baf-d0ef-485e-b4d4-ab5f023d54a8"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Haploinsufficiency of <i>ARHGAP42</i> is associated with hypertension","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-459485","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"Objective: To identify general practitioners’ (GPs) barriers and facilitators regarding the use of health information technology (HIT) in the treatment of patients with low back pain (LBP). Design: A qualitative study employing a participatory design approach, with an inductive analytical thematic approach utilising semi-structured interviews. Empirical data was analysed using the qualitative data analysis software (QDAS) Nvivo. Setting: General practices in Denmark. Subjects: Eight interviews were conducted with an average duration of 60 min. The interviewees were GPs from different geographical settings and different organisational structures, varying in age and professional interests. Main outcome measures: Barriers and facilitators for future use of the HIT application for patients with LBP. Results: Through the inclusion of healthcare professionals in the design process, this study found that in order for GPs to recommend a HIT application it is essential to target the application towards their patients. Furthermore, GPs required that the HIT application should support patient self-management. Additionally, the content of the HIT application should support the initiated treatment and it should be easy for GPs to recommend the HIT application. Finally, healthcare professionals need to be involved in the design process. Conclusion: When designing health IT applications for patients with LBP in general practice it is important to include both patients and GPs in the design process. GPs would be more willing to recommend a HIT application that: applies content in line with frequently used recommendations; targets patients; supports patients’ self-management; and supports the patients’ needs.KEY POINTS Online information is currently applied in general practice to some patients with low back pain Online information cannot replace the GP, but can rather be a bonding tool between the patient and the GP It is important to address both GP and patient barriers to applying new technology and to consider the literacy level Participatory methods could play a central role in the future development of online information material.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Hjelmager, Ditte Meulengracht","Vinther, Line Dausel","Poulsen, Søren Herold","Petersen, Lone Stub","Jensen, Martin Bach","Riis, Allan"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-124157"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Adult","Attitude of Health Personnel","Denmark","Female","General Practitioners","General practice","Humans","Information Dissemination methods","Information technology","Internet","Low Back Pain therapy","Low back pain","Male","Medical Informatics","Middle Aged","Patient Education as Topic","Patient Education as Topic methods","Qualitative Research","Self Care","Self management","Software Design","Surveys and Questionnaires"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"requirements for implementing online information material for patients with low back pain in general practice an interview study","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY 4.0","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1080/02813432.2019.1569413","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-124157","identifier":[{"id":"30700191","type":"pmid"},{"id":"000462849900008","type":"wos"},{"id":"85060945849","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-ff4baf9f-33d0-4a91-8e16-4f641e4399cd"],"keyword":["Adult","Attitude of Health Personnel","Denmark","Female","General Practitioners","General practice","Humans","Information Dissemination/methods","Information Technology","Internet","Low Back Pain/therapy","Male","Middle Aged","Patient Education as Topic/methods","Qualitative Research","Self Care","Surveys and Questionnaires","low back pain","medical informatics","patient education as topic","self-management","software design"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-535C34F9668F3C76BDBE078BA421963A"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY 4.0","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1080/02813432.2019.1569413","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY 4.0","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/328879456/Requirements_for_implementing_online_information_material_for_patients_with_low_back_pain_in_general_practice_an_interview_study.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2019","yearSub":"2019"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Sustainability and Planning"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Ditte Meulengracht","key":"hjelmagerpau","last":"Hjelmager","locid":"36604b3b-8b21-44e7-843e-8625538d4537","name":"Hjelmager, Ditte Meulengracht","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Line Dausel","key":"vintherpau","last":"Vinther","locid":"91dfd153-7da9-4e62-b6b1-9f78c881fd83","name":"Vinther, Line Dausel","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Søren Herold","key":"poulsenpau","last":"Poulsen","locid":"39d52899-128d-4238-a437-bf7dea822366","name":"Poulsen, Søren Herold","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Lone Stub","key":"petersenpau","last":"Petersen","locid":"59eaa6e1-99d2-4d5a-820d-fd12d1a46e61","name":"Petersen, Lone Stub","orcid":"0000-0003-1844-0592","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Martin Bach","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","locid":"929fc31a-f5b6-45b8-b3ed-29bd2c4b4bf7","name":"Jensen, Martin Bach","orcid":"0000-0003-2162-7390","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Allan","key":"riispau","last":"Riis","locid":"dd013e16-1de8-4499-aab3-cf50e4361e58","name":"Riis, Allan","orcid":"0000-0002-7009-3025","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["30700191"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1080/02813432.2019.1569413","issn":["02813432","15027724"],"issn_org":["02813432"],"issue":"1","journal":"Scandinavian Journal of Primary Health Care","pages":"60-68","publisher":"Informa Healthcare","status":"p","title":"Scandinavian Journal of Primary Health Care","volume":"37"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85060945849"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-ff4baf9f-33d0-4a91-8e16-4f641e4399cd"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Requirements for implementing online information material for patients with low back pain in general practice : an interview study","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-124157","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"PURPOSE: PET/MRI was introduced for clinical use in 2011 and is now an established modality for the imaging of brain and certain pelvic cancers, whereas clinical use for the imaging of other forms of cancer is not yet widespread. We therefore systematically investigated what has been published on the use of PET/MRI compared to PET/CT in the imaging of cancers outside the brain, focusing on clinical areas of application related to diagnosis, staging and restaging. METHODS: A systematic search of PubMed/MEDLINE, Embase and the Cochrane Library was performed. Studies evaluating the diagnostic performance of simultaneous PET/MRI in cancer patients were chosen. RESULTS: A total of 3,138 publications were identified and 116 published during the period 2012-2018 were included and were grouped according to the major cancer forms: 13 head and neck (HNC), 9 breast (BC), 21 prostate (PC), 14 gynaecological, 13 gastrointestinal (GIC), and 46 various cancers. Data from studies comparing PET/MRI and PET/CT for staging/restaging suggested the superiority of 18F-FDG PET/MRI for the detection of tumour extension and retropharyngeal lymph node metastases in nasopharyngeal cancer, and for the detection of liver metastases and possibly bone marrow metastases in high-risk BC. FDG PET/MRI tended to be inferior for the detection of lung metastases in HNC and BC. 68Ga-PSMA-11 PET/MRI was superior to PET/CT for the detection of local PC recurrence. FDG PET/MRI was superior to FDG PET/CT for the detection of local tumour invasion in cervical cancer and had higher accuracy for the detection of liver metastases in colorectal cancer. CONCLUSION: The scoping review methodology resulted in the identification of a huge number of records, of which less than 5% were suitable for inclusion and only a limited number allowed conclusions on the advantages/disadvantages of PET/MRI compared to PET/CT in the oncological setting. There was evidence to support the use of FDG PET/MRI in staging of nasopharyngeal cancer and high-risk BC. Preliminary data indicate the superiority of PET/MRI for the detection of local recurrence in PC, local tumour invasion in cervical cancer, and liver metastases in colorectal cancer. These conclusions are based on small datasets and need to be further explored.","author_count":9,"contributors":["Morsing, Anni","Hildebrandt, Malene Grubbe","Vilstrup, Mie Holm","Dahlsgaard-Wallenius, Sara Elisabeth","Gerke, Oke","Petersen, Henrik","Johansen, Allan","Andersen, Thomas Lund","Høilund-Carlsen, Poul Flemming"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-627312"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["F FDG","Oncology","PET CT","PET MRI","Staging"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"hybrid pet mri in major cancers a scoping review","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/151944864/EJNM_D_19_00325_R1_SDU_homepage.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-627312","identifier":[{"id":"31267161","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85068748562","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["sdu-bcb3558f-2726-4e80-afd8-f995998f19f5"],"keyword":["F-FDG","Oncology","PET/CT","PET/MRI","Staging"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-4D3D428698BA389F006834346FCB8CF2"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/151944864/EJNM_D_19_00325_R1_SDU_homepage.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2019","yearSub":"2019"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research, KI, OUH, Research unit of Clinical Physiology and Nuclear Medicine (Odense)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Anni","key":"morsingpau","last":"Morsing","locid":"eb322987-0180-4887-8e6c-9c9cb4f6ef39","name":"Morsing, Anni","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Malene Grubbe","key":"hildebrandtpau","last":"Hildebrandt","locid":"89ec551d-ddfe-45e8-983a-f2bbc54f8a0e","name":"Hildebrandt, Malene Grubbe","orcid":"0000-0003-2720-9018","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Mie Holm","key":"vilstruppau","last":"Vilstrup","locid":"9ceb6215-deb0-460f-8c59-bbc32b7dca27","name":"Vilstrup, Mie Holm","orcid":"0000-0002-4760-0068","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Sara Elisabeth","key":"walleniuspau","last":"Wallenius","locid":"09dbda03-897a-47e9-8ce4-7c2e523c417c","name":"Dahlsgaard-Wallenius, Sara Elisabeth","name_org":"Wallenius, Sara Elisabeth","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Oke","key":"gerkepau","last":"Gerke","locid":"596baeb1-6754-4d53-948f-30470dd1d976","name":"Gerke, Oke","orcid":"0000-0001-6335-3303","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Henrik","key":"petersenpau","last":"Petersen","locid":"ea635371-4294-4379-9655-3da538fecf13","name":"Petersen, Henrik","orcid":"0000-0002-1118-1500","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Allan","key":"johansenpau","last":"Johansen","locid":"dc7a1a61-b703-48ec-bd87-c92b55784133","name":"Johansen, Allan","orcid":"0000-0002-3622-057X","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Thomas Lund","key":"andersenpau","last":"Andersen","locid":"8a904314-798c-4e45-9559-b997a4e1d5c7","name":"Andersen, Thomas Lund","orcid":"0000-0002-2860-6317","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Poul Flemming","key":"høilundcarlsenpau","last":"Høilund-Carlsen","locid":"a1ff65cf-cdaa-4192-bef3-a915cfe6cceb","name":"Høilund-Carlsen, Poul Flemming","orcid":"0000-0001-7420-2367","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["31267161"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/s00259-019-04402-8","issn":["16197070","16197089"],"issn_org":["16197070"],"issue":"10","journal":"European Journal of Nuclear Medicine and Molecular Imaging","pages":"2138-2151","publisher":"Springer","status":"p","title":"European Journal of Nuclear Medicine and Molecular Imaging","volume":"46"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85068748562"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-bcb3558f-2726-4e80-afd8-f995998f19f5"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Hybrid PET/MRI in major cancers : a scoping review","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-627312","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"OBJECTIVE: Monitoring the influence of cautious iodine fortification (IF) on the incidence rate of overt thyrotoxicosis in Denmark with formerly frequent multinodular toxic goitre. DESIGN: A 21 year (1997-2017) prospective population-based study identified all new cases of overt biochemical thyrotoxicosis in two open cohorts: a Western cohort with moderate iodine deficiency (ID) and an Eastern cohort with mild ID (total n=533,969 by January 1st , 1997). A diagnostic algorithm was applied to all thyroid function tests performed within the study areas. Mandatory IF of salt was initiated in mid-2000 (13 p.p.m.). The present study is a part of DanThyr. RESULTS: The standardized incidence rate (SIR) of thyrotoxicosis at baseline (1997-1998) was 128.5/100.000/year in the cohort with moderate ID and 80.1 in the cohort with mild ID. SIR increased markedly in both cohorts during the initial years of IF (moderate/mild ID: +39/+52% in 2000-01/2004-05) and subsequently decreased to baseline level (mild ID) or below (moderate ID) by 2008. The decline was due to a marked decrease in the incidence rate among elderly subjects and a moderate decrease among the middle aged. The follow-up period for the mildly iodine deficient cohort was restricted to 2008. A continuous decline in SIR was observed for the remainder of the study period in the area with moderate ID (33% below baseline in 2016-17). CONCLUSION: The rise in thyrotoxicosis incidence with cautious mandatory IF returned to baseline level after 7-8 years and levelled out at 33% below baseline in the population with previously moderate ID after 16-17 years. This article is protected by copyright. All rights reserved.","author_count":14,"contributors":["Petersen, Mads","Knudsen, Nils","Carlé, Allan","Andersen, Stig","Jørgensen, Torben","Perrild, Hans","Ovesen, Lars","Banke Rasmussen, Lone","Heinsbaek Thuesen, Betina","Pedersen, Inge Bülow"],"cuid":["S02-094.95-004816"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"keyword":["Epidemiology","Hyperthyroidism","Incidence","Iodine","Thyrotoxicosis"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-NDR","DI-HO-ZEA"],"OT":["Centre for Clinical Research and Prevention, Glostrup University Hospital, Copenhagen, Denmark"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU","DI-U-UND"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-NDR","DI-HO-ZEA","DI-U-AAU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-UND"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"thyrotoxicosis after iodine fortification a 000000000021 year danish population based study","src":["aau","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/293589326/Thyrotoxicosis_after_iodine_fortification._A_21_year_Danish_population_based_study.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S02-094.95-004816","identifier":[{"id":"29851122","type":"pmid"},{"id":"000440987500013","type":"wos"},{"id":"85051240202","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-63216608-698e-4f18-9c39-0ff51eeafb17","ku-11da9f78-8e45-423c-9320-e2fbcdf8307b"],"keyword":["epidemiology","hyperthyroidism","incidence","iodine","thyrotoxicosis"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-96D9AE097281720A15EB6E4A7611DB6C"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/293589326/Thyrotoxicosis_after_iodine_fortification._A_21_year_Danish_population_based_study.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2018","yearSub":"2018"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","na