{"author_count":8,"contributors":["Madsen, Christoffer","Granqvist, Henrik","Petersen, Jørgen Holm","Rasmussen, Ase","Lund, Allan","Oturai, Peter","Sørensen, Søren Schwartz","Feldt-Rasmussen, Ulla"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-540411"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"age related attrition of renal function in fabry disease patients on enzyme replacement therapy long term observation in a nationwide family screened cohort based on cr edta clearance compared with renal healthy population","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dca","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-540411","identifier":[{"id":"000433059801142","type":"wos"}],"ids":["ku-f63a0beb-f7db-417c-a509-69e5886db381"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Local-1-1-4A50E8A00740179A515B4594986BA9D1"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Public Health, Section of Biostatistics"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","first":"Christoffer","key":"madsenpau","last":"Madsen","name":"Madsen, Christoffer","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Henrik","key":"granqvistpau","last":"Granqvist","name":"Granqvist, Henrik","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jorgen","key":"petersenpau","last":"Petersen","locid":"33c1c5b2-2e1e-4259-b4d7-04657a2bdb9b","name":"Petersen, Jørgen Holm","name_org":"Petersen, Jorgen","orcid":"0000-0003-3979-7443","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Ase","key":"rasmussenpau","last":"Rasmussen","name":"Rasmussen, Ase","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Allan","key":"lundpau","last":"Lund","name":"Lund, Allan","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Peter","key":"oturaipau","last":"Oturai","name":"Oturai, Peter","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Soren","key":"sorensenpau","last":"Sorensen","locid":"115ed8b6-8f6c-468a-9217-994613816c8e","name":"Sørensen, Søren Schwartz","name_org":"Sorensen, Soren","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Ulla","key":"feldtrasmussenpau","last":"Feldt-Rasmussen","locid":"b5898535-d448-4e2f-9f41-d5199873676b","name":"Feldt-Rasmussen, Ulla","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1093/ndt/gfy104","issn":["09310509","14602385"],"issn_org":["09310509"],"journal":"Nephrology Dialysis Transplantation","status":"p","title":"Nephrology Dialysis Transplantation","volume":"33"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-f63a0beb-f7db-417c-a509-69e5886db381"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"AGE RELATED ATTRITION OF RENAL FUNCTION IN FABRY DISEASE PATIENTS ON ENZYME REPLACEMENT THERAPY: LONG-TERM OBSERVATION IN A NATIONWIDE, FAMILY-SCREENED COHORT BASED ON CR-EDTA CLEARANCE COMPARED WITH RENAL HEALTHY POPULATION","type":"Conference Abstract","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-540411","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"Background: In human immunodeficiency virus (HIV)-infected patients on combination antiretroviral therapy (cART), lipodystrophy shares many similarities with metabolic syndrome, but only metabolic syndrome has objective classification criteria. We examined adipose tissue changes related to lipodystrophy and metabolic syndrome to clarify whether it may be acceptable to focus diagnosis on metabolic syndrome rather than lipodystrophy. Methods: This is a cross-sectional study of 60 HIV-infected men on cART and 15 healthy men. We evaluated lipodystrophy (clinical assessment) and metabolic syndrome (JIS-2009). We compared adipocyte size, leukocyte infiltration, and gene expression in abdominal subcutaneous adipose tissue biopsies of patients with and without lipodystrophy and with and without metabolic syndrome. Results: Lipodystrophy was only associated with increased macrophage infiltration (P = .04) and adiponectin messenger ribonucleic acid ([mRNA] P = .008), whereas metabolic syndrome was associated with larger adipocytes (P < .0001), decreased expression of genes related to adipogenesis and adipocyte function (P values between <.0001 and .08), increased leptin mRNA (P = .04), and a trend towards increased expression of inflammatory genes (P values between .08 and .6). Conclusions: Metabolic syndrome rather than lipodystrophy was associated with major unfavorable abdominal subcutaneous adipose tissue changes. In a clinical setting, it may be more relevant to focus on metabolic syndrome diagnosis in HIV-infected patients on cART with regards to adipose tissue dysfunction and risk of cardiometabolic complications.","author_count":12,"contributors":["Langkilde, Anne","Tavenier, Juliette","Danielsen, Allan Vestergaard","Eugen-Olsen, Jesper","Therkildsen, Christina","Jensen, Frank Krieger","Henriksen, Jens Henrik","Langberg, Henning","Steiniche, Torben","Petersen, Janne","Holck, Susanne","Andersen, Ove"],"cuid":["S02-097.07-013132"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"keyword":["Adipose tissue","HIV infection","Lipodystrophy","Metabolic syndrome"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"histological and molecular adipose tissue changes are related to metabolic syndrome rather than lipodystrophy in human immunodeficiency virus infected patients a cross sectional study","src":["au","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85055002224","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S02-097.07-013132","identifier":[{"id":"29788076","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85055002224","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-0757c703-f298-429f-b0ea-9db12c7c2a04","ku-159188d3-0de9-4d3f-90ff-e2d092d289b0"],"keyword":["Adipose tissue","HIV-infection","Lipodystrophy","Metabolic syndrome"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-3C9F6F329B84C8D55F7EE2870989180F"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2018","yearSub":"2018"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital - Amager and Hvidovre"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - The Department of Pathology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"central denmark region","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CDR","l3nl":"Central Denmark Region","l3nn":"Central Denmark Region","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Central Denmark Region","namevar":["Aarhus University Hospital"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CDR","used":1},{"affno":"4","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Public Health, Section of Social Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Anne","key":"langkildepau","last":"Langkilde","name":"Langkilde, Anne","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Juliette","key":"tavenierpau","last":"Tavenier","name":"Tavenier, Juliette","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 3","corresponding":null,"first":"Allan Vestergaard","key":"danielsenpau","last":"Danielsen","locid":"44c82b53-6e9b-49ae-ac50-0311aca488e6","name":"Danielsen, Allan Vestergaard","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jesper","key":"eugenolsenpau","last":"Eugen-Olsen","name":"Eugen-Olsen, Jesper","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Christina","key":"therkildsenpau","last":"Therkildsen","name":"Therkildsen, Christina","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Frank Krieger","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","name":"Jensen, Frank Krieger","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jens Henrik","key":"henriksenpau","last":"Henriksen","name":"Henriksen, Jens Henrik","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","country":"dk","first":"Henning","key":"langbergpau","last":"Langberg","locid":"aa9694cb-06fd-4f81-a6f7-c5862f8d3499","name":"Langberg, Henning","orcid":"0000-0001-8454-6534","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 3","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Torben","key":"steinichepau","last":"Steiniche","locid":"7e538367-420a-4384-ba76-033652a0ea41","name":"Steiniche, Torben","orcid":"0000-0001-5689-3555","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 4","first":"Janne","key":"petersenpau","last":"Petersen","locid":"1cb72724-54f8-4ca1-a201-bfa4a354a129","name":"Petersen, Janne","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Susanne","key":"holckpau","last":"Holck","name":"Holck, Susanne","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 4","first":"Ove","key":"andersenpau","last":"Andersen","locid":"251ac7c3-391a-4cd6-8696-6d5f1ee26911","name":"Andersen, Ove","orcid":"0000-0002-2274-548X","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["29788076"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1093/infdis/jiy284","issn":["00221899","15376613"],"issn_org":["00221899"],"issue":"7","journal":"The Journal of Infectious Diseases","pages":"1090-1098","publisher":"Oxford University Press","status":"p","title":"The Journal of Infectious Diseases","volume":"218"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85055002224"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","Central Denmark Region","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-0757c703-f298-429f-b0ea-9db12c7c2a04","ku-159188d3-0de9-4d3f-90ff-e2d092d289b0"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Histological and Molecular Adipose Tissue Changes Are Related to Metabolic Syndrome Rather Than Lipodystrophy in Human Immunodeficiency Virus-Infected Patients : A Cross-Sectional Study","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-097.07-013132","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"BACKGROUND: Spinocerebellar ataxia type 14 is a rare form of autosomal dominant cerebellar ataxia caused by mutations in protein kinase Cγ gene. Clinically, it presents with a slowly progressive, mainly pure cerebellar ataxia. METHODS: Using next generation sequencing, we screened 194 families with autosomal dominant cerebellar ataxia and normal polyglutamine repeats. In-depth phenotyping was performed using validated clinical rating scales neuroimaging and electrophysiological investigations. RESULTS: We identified 25 individuals from 13 families carrying pathogenic mutations in protein kinase Cγ gene. A total of 10 unique protein kinase Cγ gene mutations have been confirmed of which 5 are novel and 5 were previously described. Our data suggest that the age at onset is highly variable; disease course is slowly progressive and rarely associated with severe disability. However, one third of patients presented with a complex ataxia comprising severe focal and/or task-induced dystonia, peripheral neuropathy, parkinsonism, myoclonus, and pyramidal syndrome. The most complex phenotype is related to a missense mutation in the catalytic domain in exon 11. CONCLUSION: We present one of the largest genetically confirmed spinocerebellar ataxia type 14 cohorts contributing novel variants and clinical characterisation. We show that although protein kinase Cγ gene mutations present mainly as slowly progressive pure ataxia, more than a third of cases had a complex phenotype. Overall, our case series extends the phenotype and suggests that protein kinase Cγ gene mutations should be considered in patients with slowly progressive autosomal dominant cerebellar ataxia, particularly when myoclonus, dystonia, or mild cognitive impairment are present in the absence of polyglutamine expansion. © 2018 The Authors. Movement Disorders published by Wiley Periodicals, Inc. on behalf of International Parkinson and Movement Disorder Society.","author_count":23,"contributors":["Chelban, Viorica","Wiethoff, Sarah","Fabian-Jessing, Bjørn K.","Haridy, Nourelhoda A","Khan, Alaa","Efthymiou, Stephanie","Becker, Esther B E","O'Connor, Emer","Hersheson, Joshua","Newland, Katrina","Højland, Allan Thomas","Gregersen, Pernille A","Lindquist, Suzanne G","Petersen, Michael Bjørn","Nielsen, Jørgen E","Nielsen, Michael","Wood, Nicholas W","Giunti, Paola","Houlden, Henry"],"cuid":["S03-100.00-000031"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":3,"continent":["Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"country":["Germany","United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","University College London","University College London Hospitals NHS Foundation Trust","University of Cambridge","University of Tübingen"],"keyword":["Ataxia","Dystonia","Genetics","PRKCG","SCA14"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-NDR"],"OT":["Department of Neurology and Psychiatry, Assiut University Hospital, Faculty of Medicine, Assiut, Egypt."],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-NDR","DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"genotype phenotype correlations dystonia and disease progression in spinocerebellar ataxia type 000000000014","src":["aau","au","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1002/mds.27334","version":"Published Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["We would like to thank the patients for their participation in this study. This study was supported by the Medical Research Council (MRC UK MR/J004758/1, G0802760, G1001253), The Wellcome Trust in equipment and strategic award (Synaptopathies) funding (WT093205MA and WT104033/Z/14/Z), The Brain Research Trust, The MSA Trust, the European Union Seventh Framework Programme FP7/2007-2013 under grant agreement number 2012-305121 (NeurOmics), Ataxia UK, British Neurological Surveillance Unit, the National Institute for Health Research, University College London Hospitals, and the Biomedical Research Centre. Acknowledgments: We would like to thank the patients for their participation in this study. This study was supported by the Medical Research Council (MRC UK MR/J004758/1, G0802760, G1001253), The Wellcome Trust in equipment and strategic award (Synaptopathies) funding (WT093205MA and WT104033/Z/14/Z), The Brain Research Trust, The MSA Trust, the European Union Seventh Framework Programme FP7/2007-2013 under grant agreement number 2012-305121 (NeurOmics), Ataxia UK, British Neurological Surveillance Unit, the National Institute for Health Research, University College London Hospitals, and the Biomedical Research Centre."],"id":"S03-100.00-000031","identifier":[{"id":"29603387","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85044596874","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC6175136","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"000442851800012","type":"wos"}],"ids":["aau-0075f0c5-7383-4b74-a06e-c42a065bfd8e","au-7bac6780-45cd-463b-9c7c-90e30c20afe9","ku-e1051a15-e209-405e-9a54-4880e94a573a"],"keyword":["PRKCG","SCA14","ataxia","dystonia","genetics"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-6-074DEF0E2A43DF731E81440E2EB11BB2"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1002/mds.27334","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY 4.0","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/288427580/Chelban_et_al_2018_Movement_Disorders.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.au.dk/ws/files/168153990/Chelban_et_al_2018_Movement_Disorders.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"http://europepmc.org/Copyright","type":"rem","url":"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC6175136/pd