{"abstract":"Kapitlet indeholder en introduktion til en række forskellige begreber, som kan have betydning for den måde ambulancepersonalet møder patienten på. Får det f.eks. betydning for behandlingen, hvis patient og behandler har forskellige opfattelser af, hvad det vil sige at være sund, rask eller syg? Er det muligt at indtænke sundhedsfremme og forebyggelse i ambulancetjenesten? Hvad er folkesygdomme og livsstilssygdomme og hvilken betydning har de for de patientkategorier og de problemstillinger, som ambulancepersonalet bliver kaldt ud til? Formålet med den præhospitale indsats er ifølge Danske Regioner bl.a. at yde omsorg og skabe tryghed for patienten. Kapitlet giver dog også nogle bud på hvad vil det egentligt sige at yde omsorg?","author_count":6,"contributors":["Fock, Lotte"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-650420"],"filters":{"added":"2023-01","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Ambulance","Præhospital","Sygdom sundhedsvidenskab og sygepleje"],"level":"edu","oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-UC"],"level3":{"UC":["DI-UC-ALL","DI-UC-UCN"]},"level3all":["DI-UC-UCN"]},"review":"und","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"sundhed og sygepleje","src":["ucn"],"src-code":["DI-UC-UCN"],"type":"dba","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"http://munksgaard.dk/Erhvervsuddannelser/Den-pr%C3%A6hospitale-patient/9788762814462","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-650420","ids":["ucn-24986514-d85b-48db-af0e-0b4e2d3f9c7e"],"keyword":["Sygdom, sundhedsvidenskab og sygepleje","ambulance","præhospital"],"lang":"Danish","level":"Educational","noi":["Local-1-1-F25B555909085F2AFD40179649782247"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ucn university college of northern denmark","l2":"DI-UC","l2n":"University Colleges","l3":"DI-UC-UCN","l3nl":"University College of Northern Denmark","l3nn":"UCN University College of Northern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"UCN University College of Northern Denmark","namevar":["Professionshøjskolen UCN, UCN Direktion, UCN Velfærd, UCN act2learn Sundhed og Social"],"nora_code":"DI-UC-UCN","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Lotte","key":"fockpau","last":"Fock","locid":"97cace43-abdd-4d66-ade9-6ae04f1c7fb2","name":"Fock, Lotte","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Torben","key":"bastholmpedh","last":"Bastholm","name":"Bastholm, Torben","rank":2,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Kim","key":"dalgaardpedh","last":"Dalgaard","name":"Dalgaard, Kim","rank":3,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Kenneth","key":"lübckepedh","last":"Lübcke","name":"Lübcke, Kenneth","rank":4,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Jan","key":"nørtvedpedh","last":"Nørtved","name":"Nørtved, Jan","rank":5,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Allan","key":"petersenpedh","last":"Petersen","name":"Petersen, Allan","rank":6,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"isbn":["9788762814462"],"pages":"133-154","place":"København","publisher":"Munksgaard","status":"p","title":"Den præhospitale patient"},"review":"Undetermined","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All University Colleges","DI-ALL","DI-UC","DI-UC-ALL","University College of Northern Denmark","University Colleges"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ucn-24986514-d85b-48db-af0e-0b4e2d3f9c7e"],"src":["UCN University College of Northern Denmark"],"title":"Sundhed og sygepleje","type":"Book Chapter","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-650420","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"abstract":"Simvastatin reduces the blood concentration of cholesterol by inhibiting hydroxymethylglutaryl-coenzyme A reductase, the rate-limiting enzyme in cholesterol synthesis, and thereby reduces the risk of cardiovascular disease. In addition, simvastatin treatment leads to a reduction in fluxes in mitochondrial respiratory complexes I and II and might thereby reduce the formation of reactive oxygen species, which have been implicated in the pathogenesis of arteriosclerosis. Therefore, we hypothesized that simvastatin may reduce oxidative stress in humans in vivo. We conducted a randomized, double-blinded, placebo-controlled study in which subjects were treated with either 40 mg of simvastatin or placebo for 14 days. The endpoints were six biomarkers for oxidative stress, which represent intracellular oxidative stress to nucleic acids, lipid peroxidation and plasma antioxidants, that were measured in urine and plasma samples. A total of 40 participants were included, of which 39 completed the trial. The observed differences between simvastatin and placebo groups in the primary outcomes, DNA and RNA oxidation, were small and nonsignificant (p=0.68), specifically, 3% in the simvastatin group compared to 7.1% in the placebo group for DNA oxidation and 7.3% in the simvastatin group compared to 3.4% in the placebo group. The differences in biomarkers related to plasma were not statistically significant between the treatments groups, with the exception of total vitamin E levels, which, as expected, were reduced in parallel with the reduction in plasma cholesterol. In healthy young male volunteers, short-term simvastatin treatment, which considerably reduces cholesterol, does not lead to a clinically relevant reduction in a panel of measures of oxidative stress. Whether simvastatin has effects on oxidative stress in diseased populations, such as diabetes or hemochromatosis, where oxidative stress is prominent, is unknown but seems unlikely.","author_count":9,"contrib