{"abstract":"OBJECTIVE: The primary aim is to identify, summarise and quality assess the available literature on the cost-effectiveness of implementing low back pain guidelines in primary care. The secondary aim is to assess the transferability of the results to determine whether the identified studies can be included in a comparison with a Danish implementation study to establish which strategy procures most value for money. DESIGN: Systematic review. DATA SOURCES: The search was conducted in Embase, PubMed, Cochrane Library, NHS Economic Evaluation Database, Scopus, CINAHL and EconLit. No restrictions were made concerning language, year of publication or publication type. The bibliographies of the included studies were searched for any studies not captured in the literature search. ELIGIBILITY CRITERIA FOR SELECTING STUDIES: To be included, a study must be: (1) based on a randomised controlled trial comparing implementation strategies, (2) the guideline must concern treatment of low back pain in primary care and (3) the economic evaluation should contain primary data on cost and cost-effectiveness. RESULTS: The title and abstract were assessed for 308 studies; of these, three studies were found eligible for inclusion. The Consensus Health Economic Criteria (CHEC) list showed that the 3 studies were of moderate methodological quality while application of Welte's model showed that cost results from two studies could, with adjustments, be transferred to a Danish setting. It was questionable whether the associated effects could be transferred. CONCLUSIONS: Despite the resemblance of the implementation strategies, the 3 studies report conflicting results on cost-effectiveness. This review showed that transferring the results from the identified studies is not straightforward and underlines the importance of transparent reporting. Future research should focus on transferability of effects, for example, development of a supplement to Welte's model.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Jensen, Cathrine Elgaard","Jensen, Martin Bach","Riis, Allan","Petersen, Karin Dam"],"cuid":["S02-082.35-665838"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["soc"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"systematic review of the cost effectiveness of implementing guidelines on low back pain management in primary care is transferability to other countries possible","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1136/bmjopen-2016-011042","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-082.35-665838","identifier":[{"id":"27267108","type":"pmid"},{"id":"000380237100090","type":"wos"}],"ids":["aau-66ecf55f-1792-40ec-b26e-006e7f962bcd","aau-eb379e9d-e771-44b9-ba38-11bc111117e4"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Social Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-192E0A977498F5BC78791251915EE29A"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1136/bmjopen-2016-011042","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Social Science (SOC)"],"yearPub":"2016","yearSub":"2016"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences, Department of Business and Management","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences, Department of Business and Management, Danish Center for Healthcare Improvements (Business)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Cathrine Elgaard","key":"jensencathrineelgaardpau","last":"Jensen","locid":"078e71ca-9113-46d8-907c-9ec548aa6792","name":"Jensen, Cathrine Elgaard","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Martin Bach","key":"jensenmartinbachpau","last":"Jensen","locid":"929fc31a-f5b6-45b8-b3ed-29bd2c4b4bf7","name":"Jensen, Martin Bach","orcid":"0000-0003-2162-7390","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Allan","key":"riisallanpau","last":"Riis","locid":"dd013e16-1de8-4499-aab3-cf50e4361e58","name":"Riis, Allan","orcid":"0000-0002-7009-3025","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Karin Dam","key":"petersenkarindampau","last":"Petersen","locid":"2e36a0d6-1251-4e37-a8f6-8f0a16c9875e","name":"Petersen, Karin Dam","orcid":"0000-0002-6491-1757","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["27267108"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1136/bmjopen-2016-011042","issn":["20446055"],"issue":"6","journal":"BMJ Open","paperid":"e011042","publisher":"BMJ Publishing Group","status":"p","title":"BMJ Open","title_org":"B M J Open","volume":"6"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84974577048"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-66ecf55f-1792-40ec-b26e-006e7f962bcd","aau-eb379e9d-e771-44b9-ba38-11bc111117e4"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Systematic review of the cost-effectiveness of implementing guidelines on low back pain management in primary care : is transferability to other countries possible?","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-082.35-665838","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
