{"abstract":"By a retrospective medical record review it is studied if 334 admissions of acute short-term hospitalization (< 24 hours) of elderly medical patients could have been substituted by alternative solutions. 27% of these admissions were evaluated as substitutable. This study cannot confirm that the number of medical short-term admissions of elderly patients could be reduced by one or more specific interventions, nor that the medical short-term hospitalization generally is inappropriate.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Hermansen, Signe","Ellekilde, Gertrude","Rytter, Lars","Sales, Yves","Kønig, Karen Bay","Andersen, Allan","Petersen, Lars","Andersen, Ove"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-542039"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"analyse af medicinske korttidsindlæggelser af ældre patienter med fokus på alternative løsninger","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"http://ugeskriftet.dk/videnskab/V10140554","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-542039","identifier":[{"id":"84976504574","type":"scopus"},{"id":"25749287","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-f8f86005-479c-422c-bf53-db04b4d9e54c"],"lang":"Danish","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-95F28871F4DAB9D709E0B1CF8C4FBB9F"],"oai":{"class":"Blocked","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2015","yearSub":"2015"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","first":"Signe","key":"hermansensignepau","last":"Hermansen","name":"Hermansen, Signe","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Gertrude","key":"ellekildegertrudepau","last":"Ellekilde","name":"Ellekilde, Gertrude","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Lars","key":"rytterlarspau","last":"Rytter","name":"Rytter, Lars","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Yves","key":"salesyvespau","last":"Sales","name":"Sales, Yves","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Karen Bay","key":"kønigkarenbaypau","last":"Kønig","name":"Kønig, Karen Bay","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Allan","key":"andersenallanpau","last":"Andersen","name":"Andersen, Allan","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Lars","key":"petersenlarspau","last":"Petersen","name":"Petersen, Lars","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Ove","key":"andersenovepau","last":"Andersen","locid":"251ac7c3-391a-4cd6-8696-6d5f1ee26911","name":"Andersen, Ove","orcid":"0000-0002-2274-548X","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["25749287"],"pub":{"issn":["00415782","13994174"],"issn_org":["00415782"],"issue":"6","journal":"Ugeskrift for Læger","pages":"561-3","paperid":"V10140554","status":"p","title":"Ugeskrift for Læger","title_org":"Ugeskrift for Laeger","volume":"177"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84976504574","2-s2.0-85016458374"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-f8f86005-479c-422c-bf53-db04b4d9e54c"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Analyse af medicinske korttidsindlæggelser af ældre patienter med fokus på alternative løsninger","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-542039","year":"2015","yearsub":"2015"}
{"abstract":"AIMS/HYPOTHESIS: We investigated whether urinary markers of nucleic acid oxidation are associated with an increased risk of cancer in type 2 diabetes patients. METHODS: Urine samples from 1381 newly diagnosed diabetes patients were assayed for the oxidatively modified guanine nucleosides 8-oxo-7,8-dihydro-2'-deoxyguanosine (8-oxodG) and 8-oxo-7,8-dihydroguanosine (8-oxoGuo). Cox proportional hazards regression was used to examine the relationship between the urinary markers and cancer incidence. RESULTS: The crude analyses showed an association between overall cancer and urinary excretion of the RNA oxidation marker 8-oxoGuo (unadjusted hazard ratio for cancer per natural log increase in 8-oxoGuo 1.35 [95% CI, 1.01-1.81]), however, in the adjusted analyses, no significant associations between 8-oxodG or 8-oxoGuo and overall cancer were found. For site-specific cancers 8-oxodG was associated with breast cancer in the crude analyses (unadjusted hazard ratio for breast cancer per natural log increase in 8-oxodG was 2.37 [95% CI, 1.07-5.26]), although the association was attenuated in the adjusted analyses (sex- and age-adjusted hazard ratio 2.15 [95% CI, 0.92-5.02] and multivariate adjusted hazard ratio1.98 [95% CI, 0.95-4.10]). CONCLUSIONS: Urinary excretion of the nucleic acid oxidation markers 8-oxodG and 8-oxoGuo at the time of diagnosis was not associated with cancer overall in type 2 diabetes patients. For site-specific cancers, risk elevations were seen for breast cancer (8-oxodG). These findings should be examined in future and larger studies.","author_count":16,"contributors":["Broedbaek, Kasper","Siersma, Volkert","Henriksen, Trine Foged","Weimann, Allan","Petersen, Morten","Andersen, Jon T.","Solem, Espen Victor Jimenez","Hansen, L.J.","Henriksen, Jan Erik","Bonnema, Steen J","Olivarius, Niels de Fine","Friis, Søren","Poulsen, Henrik Enghusen"],"cuid":["S02-099.18-043601"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"keyword":["8 Oxo 7 8 dihydro 2 deoxyguanosine","8 oxo 7 8 dihydroguanosine","Cancer","DNA oxidation","RNA oxidation","Type 2 diabetes"],"level":"sci","mra":["med","sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-NP","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"NP":["DI-NP-ALL","DI-NP-CAN"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-NP-CAN","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"urinary markers of nucleic acid oxidation and cancer in type 000000000002 diabetes","src":["ku","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.redox.2014.11.010","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-099.18-043601","identifier":[{"id":"PMC4309851","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"84917690923","type":"scopus"},{"id":"25498965","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-784df43f-2e31-4128-aa40-386e0f97be90","sdu-a1d1612f-6528-4775-8ba5-d9047931a99c"],"keyword":["8-oxo-7,8-dihydro-2'-deoxyguanosine","8-oxo-7,8-dihydroguanosine","Cancer","DNA oxidation","RNA oxidation","Type 2 diabetes"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science","Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-83003F4D543513778A7D9C90D1153CBF"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.redox.2014.11.010","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/121294469/Urinary_markers_of_nucleic_acid_oxidation_and_cancer_in_type_2_diabetes.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2015","yearSub":"2015"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenh