"north denmark region","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-NDR","l3nl":"North Denmark Region","l3nn":"North Denmark Region","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"North Denmark Region","namevar":["Research Unit for General Practice in the North Denmark region"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-NDR","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Cathrine Elgaard","key":"jensencathrineelgaardpau","last":"Jensen","locid":"078e71ca-9113-46d8-907c-9ec548aa6792","name":"Jensen, Cathrine Elgaard","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Allan","key":"riisallanpau","last":"Riis","locid":"dd013e16-1de8-4499-aab3-cf50e4361e58","name":"Riis, Allan","orcid":"0000-0002-7009-3025","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Martin Bach","key":"jensenmartinbachpau","last":"Jensen","locid":"929fc31a-f5b6-45b8-b3ed-29bd2c4b4bf7","name":"Jensen, Martin Bach","orcid":"0000-0003-2162-7390","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Karin Dam","key":"petersenkarindampau","last":"Petersen","locid":"2e36a0d6-1251-4e37-a8f6-8f0a16c9875e","name":"Petersen, Karin Dam","orcid":"0000-0002-6491-1757","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","North Denmark Region","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-fc2cd50d-9ffa-47bc-987a-47a47c607c08"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Combining data from randomised controlled trials with registry data to improve health econimic evaluation of low back pain treatment in Denmark","type":"Conference Abstract","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-123282","year":"2014","yearsub":"2014"}
{"abstract":"The aim of the present study was to investigate the population dynamics and potential interactions between Trichuris suis and Oesophagostomum dentatum in experimentally co-infected pigs, by quantification of parasite parameters such as egg excretion, worm recovery and worm location. Forty-eight helminth naïve pigs were allocated into four groups. Group O was inoculated with 20 O. dentatum L3/kg/day and group T with 10 T. suis eggs/kg/day. Group OT was inoculated with both 20 O. dentatum L3/kg/day and 10 T. suis eggs/kg/day, while Group C was kept as an uninfected control group. All inoculations were trickle infections administered twice weekly and were continued until slaughter. Faecal samples were collected from the rectum of all pigs at day 0, and twice weekly from 2 to 9 weeks post first infection (wpi). Six pigs from each group were necropsied 5 wpi and the remaining 6 pigs from each group were necropsied 10 wpi. The faecal egg counts (FEC) and total worm burdens of O. dentatum were dramatically influenced by the presence of T. suis, with significantly lower mean FECs and worm burdens at 5 and 10 wpi compared to single infected pigs. Furthermore, in the presence of T. suis we found that O. dentatum was located more posteriorly in the gut. The changes in the Trichuris population were less prominent, but faecal egg counts, worm counts 5 wpi (57% recovered vs. 39%) and the proportion of infected animals at 10 wpi were higher in group OT compared to group T. The location of T. suis was unaffected by the presence of O. dentatum. These results indicate an antagonistic interaction between T. suis and O. dentatum which is dominated by T. suis.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Petersen, Heidi Huus","Andreasen, Annette","Kringel, Helene","Roepstorff, Allan Knud","Thamsborg, Stig Milan"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-515185"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"parasite population dynamics in pigs infected with i trichuris suis i and i oesophagostomum dentatum i","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.vetpar.2013.09.030","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-515185","identifier":[{"id":"24126087","type":"pmid"},{"id":"84888349244","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-cbdcc678-e98d-4273-b8c9-027a9f7c3f50"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-C460608D65AC306D3476E335A920E4FC"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.vetpar.2013.09.030","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2014","yearSub":"2014"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Veterinary and Animal Sciences, Parasitology and Aquatic Pathobiology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Heidi Huus","key":"petersenpau","last":"Petersen","locid":"92221d79-a107-49d9-a754-5268636557eb","name":"Petersen, Heidi Huus","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Annette","key":"andreasenpau","last":"Andreasen","locid":"a541f897-837f-4cef-adf8-385481b18b54","name":"Andreasen, Annette","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Helene","key":"kringelpau","last":"Kringel","locid":"2968aa8e-e170-44d6-9847-3289f1403877","name":"Kringel, Helene","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Allan Knud","key":"roepstorffpau","last":"Roepstorff","locid":"086303f2-0ce6-4201-81e4-1bb595ae520a","name":"Roepstorff, Allan Knud","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Stig Milan","key":"thamsborgpau","last":"Thamsborg","locid":"e1ff513c-cc7f-43e8-ac3d-742aee7fe1da","name":"Thamsborg, Stig Milan","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["24126087"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.vetpar.2013.09.030","issn":["03044017","18732550"],"issn_org":["03044017"],"issue":"1-2","journal":"Veterinary Parasitology","pages":"73-80","status":"p","title":"Veterinary Parasitology","volume":"199"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84888349244"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-cbdcc678-e98d-4273-b8c9-027a9f7c3f50"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Parasite population dynamics in pigs infected with <i>Trichuris suis </i>and <i>Oesophagostomum dentatum</i>","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-515185","year":"2014","yearsub":"2014"}
{"abstract":"Mayer-Rokitansky-Küster-Hauser (MRKH) syndrome is a congenital disorder of still unknown etiology, characterized by uterovaginal agenesis and can be associated with renal, skeletal and cardiac malformations. Most cases are sporadic. We report on a familial case of two female cousins with MRKH syndrome and unilateral renal agenesis. Family history revealed two cases of renal agenesis in male relatives and ultrasonographic (US) examination of healthy relatives diagnosed an uncle with multiple renal cysts. We have reviewed the literature on familial occurrence of MRKH syndrome and its associated anomalies and collected a total of 67 familial cases. We found familial cases to share the same associated anomalies as sporadic cases and we discuss the necessity of US examination of healthy relatives. © 2014 Wiley Periodicals, Inc.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Herlin, Morten","Højland, Allan Thomas","Petersen, Michael Bjørn"],"cuid":["S02-099.62-009738"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"corresponding_author":["Herlin, Morten Krogh"],"keyword":["Amenorrhea","Familial occurrence","Mayer Rokitansky Küster Hauser syndrome","Müllerian aplasia"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"OT":["Unspecified organisation"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"familial occurrence of mayer rokitansky küster hauser syndrome a case report and review of the literature","src":["aau","au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/84905922649","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S02-099.62-009738","identifier":[{"id":"24975471","type":"pmid"},{"id":"WOS:000340669200020","type":"wos"},{"id":"84905922649","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-cb0ad73f-30a7-466e-b173-bfca940d6713","au-0384cca2-4c70-4e48-b2ad-f0b0e81f1ec8"],"keyword":["Amenorrhea","Familial occurrence","Hereditary renal agenesis","Mayer-Rokitansky-Küster-Hauser syndrome","Müllerian aplasia","Uterovaginal agenesis","Uterus, Müllerian duct anomalies"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-FADAA9C4C4C3895FDF4A332533CB2C9B"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2014","yearSub":"2014"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Aalborg University Hospital","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Aalborg University Hospital, Department of Clinical Genetics","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Aalborg University Hospital, Klinik Diagnostik"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Aarhus University, Faculty of Health Sciences, The Department of Paediatrics"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["Unspecified organisation"],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2 3","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Morten","key":"herlinpau","last":"Herlin","locid":"f1a76c6a-cd16-4888-a1f3-25bd9b078217","name":"Herlin, Morten","orcid":"0000-0001-7179-4643","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Allan T","key":"højlandpau","last":"Højland","locid":"115e8cf1-489c-4a6b-93c5-11d69d2e0d51","name":"Højland, Allan Thomas","name_org":"Højland, Allan T","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Michael B","key":"petersenpau","last":"Petersen","locid":"8512b77d-bdf2-4889-bda3-d399e6867e28","name":"Petersen, Michael Bjørn","name_org":"Petersen, Michael B","orcid":"0000-0003-0316-8207","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["24975471"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1002/ajmg.a.36652","issn":["10403787","15524825"],"issn_org":["15524825"],"issue":"9","journal":"American Journal of Medical Genetics Part A","pages":"2276-2286","publisher":"John Wiley & Sons Inc.","status":"p","title":"American Journal of Medical Genetics Part A","title_org":"American Journal of Medical Genetics - Part A","volume":"164"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84905922649"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-cb0ad73f-30a7-466e-b173-bfca940d6713","au-0384cca2-4c70-4e48-b2ad-f0b0e81f1ec8"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University","AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Familial occurrence of Mayer-Rokitansky-Küster-Hauser syndrome : A case report and review of the literature","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-099.62-009738","year":"2014","yearsub":"2014"}
{"abstract":"AIMS: Urinary 8-oxo-7,8-dihydro-2'-deoxyguanosine (8-oxodG) and 8-oxo-7,8-dihydroguanosine (8-oxoGuo) are biomarkers of oxidative stress with clinical potential in a variety of diseases. As part of their clinical validation, this study aimed to investigate whether the urinary excretion of 8-oxodG and 8-oxoGuo undergoes diurnal variation and to evaluate the validity of 6-hour sampling as well as creatinine corrected spot urine sampling. METHODS: A total of 23 healthy study subjects collecting their 24-h urine in four fractions covering 6 hours each. Urinary 8-oxodG and 8-oxoGuo levels were quantified using a modified version of UPLC-MS/MS. RESULTS: No significant difference in excretion levels between the 12-h diurnal and 12-h nocturnal state or between the four 6-h periods during the day was found for either biomarker. A strong linear relationship between the excretion levels in each of the 6-h periods and the 24-h excretion level was shown for both biomarkers. Creatinine correction of the 6-h levels reduced the biological variation of the excretion levels and weakened the linear relationship with the uncorrected 24-h excretion level for both biomarkers. The correlations were strengthened when the 24-h excretion level was expressed per kg body weight. CONCLUSION: The results showed that 8-oxodG and 8-oxoGuo did not undergo diurnal variation in the study population overall and hence that the time of sampling is not crucial. Furthermore, 6-h sampling can be used as a substitute for 24-h sampling, and creatinine corrected sampling may be rational due to the reduction in biological variation of the biomarkers and the reasonable correlation with body weight-adjusted 24-h levels.","author_count":9,"contributors":["Grew, Ida S","Cejvanovic, Vanja","Broedbaek, Kasper","Henriksen, Trine","Petersen, Morten","Andersen, Jon Trærup","Jimenez-Solem, Espen","Weimann, Allan","Poulsen, Henrik Enghusen"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-472936"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Adult","Aged","Biological Markers","Circadian rhythm","Creatinine","Deoxyguanosine","Female","Guanosine","Humans","Male","Middle Aged","Oxidation Reduction","Oxidative stress","Reproducibility of Results"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"diurnal variation of urinary markers of nucleic acid oxidation","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3109/00365513.2014.891258","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-472936","identifier":[{"id":"84902276686","type":"scopus"},{"id":"24628455","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-84d4198c-ec5f-41d2-8469-02ec72189bbe"],"keyword":["Adult","Aged","Biological Markers","Circadian Rhythm","Creatinine","Deoxyguanosine","Female","Guanosine","Humans","Male","Middle Aged","Oxidation-Reduction","Oxidative Stress","Reproducibility of Results"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-0AC9F536BEE13132E7FB06E8730FD0D7"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3109/00365513.2014.891258","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2014","yearSub":"2014"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","first":"Ida S","key":"grewpau","last":"Grew","name":"Grew, Ida S","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Vanja","key":"cejvanovicpau","last":"Cejvanovic","locid":"6f76a562-9452-432b-9e1e-3907f1cf81fa","name":"Cejvanovic, Vanja","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Kasper","key":"broedbaekpau","last":"Broedbaek","locid":"fd11f672-8791-466e-b4da-418fb8a1db93","name":"Broedbaek, Kasper","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Trine","key":"henriksenpau","last":"Henriksen","name":"Henriksen, Trine","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Morten","key":"petersenpau","last":"Petersen","name":"Petersen, Morten","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jon T","key":"andersenpau","last":"Andersen","locid":"2fe4a9af-2462-4bba-8df4-2a518ea59342","name":"Andersen, Jon Trærup","name_org":"Andersen, Jon T","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Espen","key":"jimenezsolempau","last":"Jimenez-Solem","name":"Jimenez-Solem, Espen","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Allan","key":"weimannpau","last":"Weimann","name":"Weimann, Allan","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Henrik E","key":"poulsenpau","last":"Poulsen","locid":"8fb54acd-3a26-48f0-9111-b8e5535a0431","name":"Poulsen, Henrik Enghusen","name_org":"Poulsen, Henrik E","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["24628455"],"pub":{"doi":"10.3109/00365513.2014.891258","issn":["00365513","0085591X"],"issn_org":["00365513"],"issue":"4","journal":"Scandinavian Journal of Clinical & Laboratory Investigation","pages":"336-343","status":"p","title":"Scandinavian Journal of Clinical & Laboratory Investigation","volume":"74"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84902276686"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-84d4198c-ec5f-41d2-8469-02ec72189bbe"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Diurnal variation of urinary markers of nucleic acid oxidation","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-472936","year":"2014","yearsub":"2014"}
{"abstract":"Infection with murine gammaherpes virus 68 has become an accepted model for studying the virus/host interactions with regard to gammaherpes virus infections. Previous studies using gene deficient mice have revealed that neither IFNγ nor perforin are essential in controlling the course of infection or the virus load during chronic infection in C57BL/6 mice. However, transient multiorgan fibrosis and splenic atrophy is observed in mice lacking IFNγ or the IFNγ receptor. To study the interplay between perforin and IFNγ in controlling the virus-induced pathology and the viral load during chronic gamma herpes virus infection, we infected IFNγ/perforin double deficient C57BL/6 mice and followed the outcome of infection. While absence of perforin prevented the splenic atrophy in IFNγ deficient mice, fibrosis did not disappear. Moreover, double deficient mice developed extreme splenomegaly, were unable to control the viral load and displayed chronic immune activation. Thus IFNγ and perforin act in concert to minimize pathology and control the viral load in mice chronically infected with MHV68. Furthermore, while certain aspect of the virus-induced pathology in IFNγ deficient mice may be alleviated in double deficient mice, other aspects are exaggerated, and the normal architecture of the spleen is completely destroyed. Thus, IFNγ and perforin work in concert to minimize pathology and control the viral load. In the absence of both effector molecules, the balancing race between the virus and the host is tipped in favour of the virus causing chronic immune activation and fatal disease. This article is protected by copyright. All rights reserved.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Bartholdy, Christina","Høgh-Petersen, Mette","Storm, Pernille","Holst, Peter Johannes","Ørskov, Cathrine","Christensen, Jan Pravsgaard","Thomsen, Allan Randrup"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-514900"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"ifnγ and perforin cooperate to control infection and prevent fatal pathology during persistent gammaherpesvirus infection in mice","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1111/sji.12176","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-514900","identifier":[{"id":"24684620","type":"pmid"},{"id":"84901236972","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-cb68db87-fbaa-44c3-ad5c-b5c1b8ce32e6"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-367D8C7E148E244994AC2C11786BCDE5"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1111/sji.12176","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2014","yearSub":"2014"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Immunology and Microbiology, Department of Immunology and Microbiology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","first":"Christina","key":"bartholdypau","last":"Bartholdy","locid":"b8354948-be5f-4a10-b18c-9831d3b40c48","name":"Bartholdy, Christina","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Mette","key":"høghpetersenpau","last":"Høgh-Petersen","name":"Høgh-Petersen, Mette","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Pernille","key":"stormpau","last":"Storm","name":"Storm, Pernille","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Peter Johannes","key":"holstpau","last":"Holst","locid":"c82a82a3-3d64-429e-b441-d0910cbbed22","name":"Holst, Peter Johannes","orcid":"0000-0002-1279-304X","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Cathrine","key":"orskovpau","last":"Orskov","locid":"6c050cc2-8dd3-4ace-9eeb-a9be01301868","name":"Ørskov, Cathrine","name_org":"Orskov, Cathrine","orcid":"0000-0002-7762-2372","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jan Pravsgaard","key":"christensenpau","last":"Christensen","locid":"042fb583-4cb8-4de1-bcb5-5ac3b53d0d48","name":"Christensen, Jan Pravsgaard","orcid":"0000-0002-4299-9479","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Allan Randrup","key":"thomsenpau","last":"Thomsen","locid":"fdf0ac42-94d9-4cd6-ae66-be91f73c0dbe","name":"Thomsen, Allan Randrup","orcid":"0000-0002-2392-9803","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["24684620"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1111/sji.12176","issn":["03009475","03016323"],"issn_org":["03009475"],"issue":"6","journal":"Scandinavian Journal of Immunology","pages":"395-403","status":"p","title":"Scandinavian Journal of Immunology","volume":"79"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84901236972"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-cb68db87-fbaa-44c3-ad5c-b5c1b8ce32e6"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"IFNγ and perforin cooperate to control infection and prevent fatal pathology during persistent gammaherpesvirus infection in mice","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-514900","year":"2014","yearsub":"2014"}
{"abstract":"INTRODUCTION: The aim of this study was to compare cancer mortality among migrant patients with cancer mortality in Danish-born patients. MATERIAL AND METHODS: This was a historical prospective cohort study. All non-Western migrants (n = 56,273) who were granted a right to residency in Denmark between 1 January 1993 and 31 December 1999 were included and matched 1:4 on age and sex with Danish-born patients. Cancer patients in the cohort were identified through the Danish Cancer Registry and deaths and emigrations through the Central Population Register. Using a Cox regression model, mean sex-specific hazard ratio (HR) for all-cause mortality were estimated by ethnicity; adjusting for age, income, co-morbidity and disease stage. RESULTS: No significant differences were observed in mortality for gynaecological cancers between migrant women (HR = 1.12; 95% confidence interval (CI): 0.70-1.80) and Danish-born women. Correspondingly, migrant women (HR = 0.76; 95% CI: 0.49-1.17) showed no significant differences in breast cancer mortality compared with Danish-born women. Regarding lung cancer, neither migrant women (HR = 0.79; 95% CI: 0.45-1.40) nor men (HR = 0.73; 95% CI: 0.53-1.14) presented statistical variances in mortality rates compared with Danish-born patients. Similarly, for colorectal cancer, migrant women (HR = 0.64; 95% CI: 0.27-1.55) and men (HR = 1.58; 95% CI: 0.75-3.36) displayed no significant differences compared with Danish-born patients. CONCLUSION: Different trends were observed according to cancer type, but cancer mortality did not differ significantly between migrants and Danish-born patients. This may imply that the Danish health-care system provides equity in cancer care.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Norredam, Marie","Larsen, Maja Olsbjerg","Petersen, Jørgen Holm","Hutchings, Martin","Krasnik, Allan"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-411254"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"cancer mortality does not differ between migrants and danish born patients","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://www.danmedj.dk/portal/pls/portal/!PORTAL.wwpob_page.show?_docname=10569273.PDF","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-411254","identifier":[{"id":"84901639442","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-1df47a38-cf1e-4d55-bb9e-c4af362da1dc"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Local-1-1-C8A02857F0DC0F5C474B8A8083A4A86D"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://www.danmedj.dk/portal/pls/portal/!PORTAL.wwpob_page.show?_docname=10569273.PDF","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Blocked","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2014","yearSub":"2014"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Public Health","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Public Health, Section of Health Services Research"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital - Rigshospitalet"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Marie Louise","key":"nørredampau","last":"Nørredam","locid":"b2ded723-225a-455c-ae7b-9be191ab1b53","name":"Norredam, Marie","name_org":"Nørredam, Marie Louise","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Maja Olsbjerg","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"3340586c-5d0f-448c-8643-ee0e0dc8fafe","name":"Larsen, Maja Olsbjerg","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jørgen Holm","key":"petersenpau","last":"Petersen","locid":"33c1c5b2-2e1e-4259-b4d7-04657a2bdb9b","name":"Petersen, Jørgen Holm","orcid":"0000-0003-3979-7443","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Martin","key":"hutchingspau","last":"Hutchings","name":"Hutchings, Martin","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Allan","key":"krasnikpau","last":"Krasnik","locid":"d1a42a6c-e3d6-4d5b-803e-e80b13314d46","name":"Krasnik, Allan","orcid":"0000-0003-1612-6129","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"issn":["00415782","13994174"],"issn_org":["00415782"],"issue":"6","journal":"Ugeskrift for Læger","pages":"1-5","status":"p","title":"Ugeskrift for Læger","title_org":"Danish Medical Journal","volume":"61"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-1df47a38-cf1e-4d55-bb9e-c4af362da1dc"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Cancer mortality does not differ between migrants and Danish-born patients","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-411254","year":"2014","yearsub":"2014"}
{"abstract":"OBJECTIVES: The 'healthy migrant effect' (HME) hypothesis postulates that health selection has a positive effect on migrants' health outcomes, especially in the first years after migration. We examined the potential role of the HME by assessing the association between residence duration and disease occurrence. METHODS: We performed a historical prospective cohort study. We included migrants who obtained residence permits in Denmark between 1 January 1993 and 31 December 2010 (n = 114 331). Occurrence of severe conditions was identified through linkage to the Danish National Patient Register. Hazard Ratios (HRs) were modelled for disease incidence by residence duration since arrival (0-5 years; 0-10 years; 0-18 years) adjusting for age and sex. RESULTS: Compared with Danish-born individuals, refugees and family reunited immigrants had lower HRs of stroke and breast cancer within 5 years after arrival; however, HRs increased at longer follow-up. For example, HRs of stroke among refugees increased from 0.77 (95% CI: 0.66; 0.91) to 0.96 (95% CI: 0.88; 1.05). For ischaemic heart disease (IHD) and diabetes, refugees and family reunited migrants had higher HRs within 5 years after arrival, and most HRs had increased by end of follow-up. For example, HRs of IHD among family reunited migrants increased from 1.29 (95% CI: 1.17; 1.42) to 1.43 (95% CI: 1.39; 1.52). In contrast, HRs for TB and HIV/AIDS showed a consistent decrease over time. CONCLUSION: Our analyses of the effect of duration of residence on disease occurrence among migrants imply that, when explaining migrants' advantageous health outcomes, the ruling theory of the HME should be used with caution, and other explanatory models should be included.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Norredam, Marie","Agyemang, Charles","Hoejbjerg Hansen, Oluf K","Petersen, Jørgen Holm","Byberg, Stine","Krasnik, Allan","Kunst, Anton E"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-460499"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"