{"abstract":"I bogen beskrives 16 innovative inklusionsprojekter rundt om i Danmark. Marginaliserede grupper som i praksis har været opgivet af systemet, lykkes det projekter, institutioner og enkeltpersoner at inkludere, så de får et socialt netværk, en meningsfuld hverdag og et personligt ståsted i det danske samfund.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Petersen, Lis Holm","Aagaard, Niels","Hansen, Søren","Uggerby, Ole","Clauson-Kaas, Per","Kræmmer, Mette","Elm, Allan"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-648312"],"filters":{"added":"2023-01","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"pop","oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-UC"],"level3":{"OT":["Landsforeningen for økosamfund"],"UC":["DI-UC-ALL","DI-UC-UCL"]},"level3all":["DI-UC-UCL"]},"review":"und","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"inklusion et socialpolitisk indspark","src":["ucl"],"src-code":["DI-UC-UCL"],"type":"db","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-648312","ids":["ucl-84bf9378-ccb2-4030-8685-84386cba8abd"],"lang":"Danish","level":"Popular","noi":["Local-1-1-93EA31192749415CE9BBDD9AC34FAAF7"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ucl university college","l2":"DI-UC","l2n":"University Colleges","l3":"DI-UC-UCL","l3nl":"UCL University College","l3nn":"UCL University College","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"UCL University College","namevar":["UCL Erhvervsakademi og Professionshøjskole, Direktion, Kompetence- og Organisationsudvikling, Anvendt Velfærdsforskning"],"nora_code":"DI-UC-UCL","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["Landsforeningen for økosamfund"],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Lis Holm","key":"petersenpau","last":"Petersen","locid":"3dbb350e-aa48-4a50-ba2a-e2027415cf93","name":"Petersen, Lis Holm","orcid":"0000-0002-5986-5055","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Niels","key":"aagaardpau","last":"Aagaard","name":"Aagaard, Niels","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Søren","key":"hansenped","last":"Hansen","name":"Hansen, Søren","rank":3,"role":"Editor","rolecode":"ped"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Ole","key":"uggerbypau","last":"Uggerby","name":"Uggerby, Ole","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Per","key":"clausonkaaspau","last":"Clauson-Kaas","name":"Clauson-Kaas, Per","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Mette","key":"kræmmerpau","last":"Kræmmer","name":"Kræmmer, Mette","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Allan","key":"elmped","last":"Elm","name":"Elm, Allan","rank":7,"role":"Editor","rolecode":"ped"}],"pub":{"isbn":["9788771183399"],"place":"Frederiksberg","publisher":"Frydenlund","status":"p"},"review":"Undetermined","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Miscellaneous","All University Colleges","DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-UC","DI-UC-ALL","Miscellaneous","Other Research","UCL University College","University Colleges"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ucl-84bf9378-ccb2-4030-8685-84386cba8abd"],"src":["UCL University College"],"title":"Inklusion : Et socialpolitisk indspark","type":"Book","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-648312","year":"2014","yearsub":"2014"}
{"abstract":"BackgroundIn Denmark, guidelines on low back pain management are currently being implemented; in association with this, a clinical trial is conducted. A health economic evaluation is carried out alongside the clinical trial to assess the cost-effectiveness of an extended implementation strategy to increase the general practitioners¿ adherence to the guidelines. In addition to usual dissemination, the extended implementation strategy is composed of visits from a guideline facilitator, stratification tools, and feedback on guideline adherence. The aim of this paper is to provide the considerations on the design of the health economic evaluation.Methods/designThe economic evaluation is carried out alongside a cluster randomised controlled trial consisting of 60 general practices in the North Denmark Region. An expected 1,200 patients between the age of 18 and 65 years with a low back pain diagnosis will be enrolled. The economic evaluation comprises both a cost-effectiveness analyses and a cost-utility analysis. Effectiveness measures include referral to secondary care, health-related quality of life measured by EQ-5D-5 L, and disability measured by the Roland Morris disability questionnaire. Cost measures include all relevant additional costs of the extended implementation strategy compared to usual implementation. The economic evaluation will be performed from both a societal perspective and a health sector perspective with a 12-month time horizon.DiscussionIt is expected that the extended implementation strategy will reduce the number of patients referred to secondary care. It is hypothesised that the additional upfront cost of extended implementation will be counterbalanced by improvements in clinical practice and patient-related outcomes, thereby rendering the extended implementation strategy cost-effective.Trial registrationClinicalTrials.gov: NCT01699256.","author_count":9,"contributors":["Jensen, Cathrine Elgaard","Riis, Allan","Pedersen, Kjeld Møller","Jensen, Martin Bach","Petersen, Karin Dam"],"cuid":["S02-098.19-008660"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"keyword":["Adolescent","Adult","Aged","Cost Benefit Analysis","Female","General Practice economics","Humans","Low Back Pain economics","Male","Middle Aged","Program Development","Quality of Life","Young Adult"],"level":"sci","mra":["soc"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"OT":["Danish Center for Healthcare Improvements"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"study protocol of an economic evaluation of an enhanced implementation strategy for the treatment of low back pain in general practice a cluster randomised controlled trial","src":["aau","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/s13012-014-0140-x","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-098.19-008660","identifier":[{"id":"WOS:000345436700001","type":"wos"},{"id":"25293975","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC4198798","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"84928701344","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-b3bb987c-6af4-44cc-9511-f88636e0959d","sdu-504a5539-6632-4b3b-b17b-b1f30c7e9e42"],"keyword":["Adolescent","Adult","Aged","Cost-Benefit Analysis","Female","General Practice/economics","Guideline Adherence/economics","Humans","Low Back Pain/economics","Male","Middle Aged","Program Development","Quality of Life","Young Adult"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Social Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-860EE6CE248AC22BA7889C5CA79C34D2"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://www.implementationscience.com/content/9/1/140","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/s13012-014-0140-x","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Reali