{"abstract":"Urinary adiponectin (u-adiponectin) excretion has been suggested to reflect early glomerular damage. Inspired by this, we studied the levels of u-adiponectin in type 1 diabetic patients with different levels of urinary albumin excretion (UAE).","author_count":9,"contributors":["Jorsal, Anders","Petersen, Emilie Hein","Tarnow, Lise","Hess, Georg","Zdunek, Dietmar","Frystyk, Jan","Flyvbjerg, Allan","Lajer, Maria Stenkil","Rossing, Peter"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-170129"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"urinary adiponectin excretion rises with increasing albuminuria in type 000000000001 diabetes","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jdiacomp.2013.06.008","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-170129","identifier":[{"id":"84887073603","type":"scopus"},{"id":"23969018","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["au-478ea277-1cd3-4d33-b45d-66e83a932e54"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-93A2F9555E76092E1F6D6A195588C4F8"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jdiacomp.2013.06.008","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2013","yearSub":"2013"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - The Department of Cardiological Medicine B"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Anders","key":"jorsalpau","last":"Jorsal","locid":"16e0eff8-d885-41bc-afb7-89c374f7c0c9","name":"Jorsal, Anders","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Emilie Hein","key":"petersenpau","last":"Petersen","name":"Petersen, Emilie Hein","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Lise","key":"tarnowpau","last":"Tarnow","locid":"6b6dbace-aade-4f49-a8d0-dc2002ee9119","name":"Tarnow, Lise","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Georg","key":"hesspau","last":"Hess","name":"Hess, Georg","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Dietmar","key":"zdunekpau","last":"Zdunek","name":"Zdunek, Dietmar","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jan","key":"frystykpau","last":"Frystyk","locid":"e3650a02-322d-46c8-9d0e-d467831ea56a","name":"Frystyk, Jan","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Allan","key":"flyvbjergpau","last":"Flyvbjerg","locid":"29cf36bd-c1a0-4026-8c90-a70cb1f46402","name":"Flyvbjerg, Allan","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Maria Stenkil","key":"lajerpau","last":"Lajer","name":"Lajer, Maria Stenkil","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Peter","key":"rossingpau","last":"Rossing","name":"Rossing, Peter","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["23969018"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.jdiacomp.2013.06.008","issn":["10568727","1873460X"],"issn_org":["10568727"],"issue":"6","journal":"Journal of Diabetes and its Complications","pages":"604-8","publisher":"Elsevier Inc.","status":"p","title":"Journal of Diabetes and its Complications","volume":"27"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84887073603"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-478ea277-1cd3-4d33-b45d-66e83a932e54"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Urinary adiponectin excretion rises with increasing albuminuria in type 1 diabetes","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-170129","year":"2013","yearsub":"2013"}
{"abstract":"Schizophrenia is associated with auditory processing impairments that could arise as a result of primary auditory cortex excitatory circuit pathology. We have previously reported a deficit in dendritic spine density in deep layer 3 of primary auditory cortex in subjects with schizophrenia. As boutons and spines can be structurally and functionally co-regulated, we asked whether the densities of intracortical excitatory or thalamocortical presynaptic boutons are also reduced. We studied 2 cohorts of subjects with schizophrenia and matched controls, comprising 27 subject pairs, and assessed the density, number, and within-bouton vesicular glutamate transporter (VGluT) protein level of intracortical excitatory (VGluT1-immunoreactive) and thalamocortical (VGluT2-immunoreactive) boutons in deep layer 3 of primary auditory cortex using quantitative confocal microscopy and stereologic sampling methods. We found that VGluT1- and VGluT2-immunoreactive puncta densities and numbers were not altered in deep layer 3 of primary auditory cortex of subjects with schizophrenia. Our results indicate that reduced dendritic spine density in primary auditory cortex of subjects with schizophrenia is not matched by a corresponding reduction in excitatory bouton density. This suggests excitatory boutons in primary auditory cortex in schizophrenia may synapse with structures other than spines, such as dendritic shafts, with greater frequency. The discrepancy between dendritic spine reduction and excitatory bouton preservation may contribute to functional impairments of the primary auditory cortex in subjects with schizophrenia.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Moyer, Caitlin E","Delevich, Kristen M","Fish, Kenneth N","Asafu-Adjei, Josephine K","Sampson, Allan R","Dorph-Petersen, Karl-Anton","Lewis, David A","Sweet, Robert A"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-177368"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"intracortical excitatory and thalamocortical boutons are intact in primary auditory cortex in schizophrenia","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.schres.2013.06.024","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-177368","identifier":[{"id":"PMC3756893","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"23830684","type":"pmid"},{"id":"84881230289","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-54362108-5cc5-4833-977e-fd68e365c6dc"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-BD22821B27F9412E55DBBEF297C8695D"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.schres.2013.06.024","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2013","yearSub":"2013"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - Translational Neuropsychiatry Unit"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Caitlin E","key":"moyerpau","last":"Moyer","name":"Moyer, Caitlin E","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Kristen M","key":"delevichpau","last":"Delevich","name":"Delevich, Kristen M","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Kenneth N","key":"fishpau","last":"Fish","name":"Fish, Kenneth N","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Josephine K","key":"asafuadjeipau","last":"Asafu-Adjei","name":"Asafu-Adjei, Josephine K","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Allan R","key":"sampsonpau","last":"Sampson","name":"Sampson, Allan R","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Karl-Anton","key":"dorphpetersenpau","last":"Dorph-Petersen","locid":"fb25cb46-a24f-4759-9fe8-58e620eb7ea2","name":"Dorph-Petersen, Karl-Anton","orcid":"0000-0002-6676-034X","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"David A","key":"lewispau","last":"Lewis","name":"Lewis, David A","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Robert A","key":"sweetpau","last":"Sweet","name":"Sweet, Robert A","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["23830684"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.schres.2013.06.024","issn":["09209964","15732509"],"issn_org":["09209964"],"issue":"1-3","journal":"Schizophrenia Research","pages":"127-34","publisher":"Elsevier BV","publisher_org":"Elsevier B.V.","status":"p","title":"Schizophrenia Research","volume":"149"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84881230289"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-54362108-5cc5-4833-977e-fd68e365c6dc"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Intracortical excitatory and thalamocortical boutons are intact in primary auditory cortex in schizophrenia","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-177368","year":"2013","yearsub":"2013"}
{"abstract":"This project investigates the potential of a Compressed Air Energy Storage system (CAES system). CAES systems are used to store mechanical energy in the form of compressed air. The systems use electricity to drive the compressor at times of low electricity demand with the purpose of converting the mechanical energy into electricity at times of high electricity demand. Two such systems are currently in operation; one in Germany (Huntorf) and one in the USA (Macintosh, Alabama). In both cases, an underground cavern is used as a pressure vessel for the storage of the compressed air. Both systems are in the range of 100 MW electrical power output with several hours of production stored as compressed air. In this range, enormous volumes are required, which make underground caverns the only economical way to design the pressure vessel. Both systems use axial turbine compressors to compress air when charging the system. The compression leads to a significant increase in temperature, and the heat generated is dumped into the ambient. This energy loss results in a low efficiency of the system, and when expanding the air, the expansion leads to a temperature drop reducing the mechanical output of the expansion turbines. To overcome this, fuel is burned to heat up the air prior to expansion. The fuel consumption causes a significant cost for the storage. Several suggestions have been made to store compression heat for later use during expansion and thereby avoid the use of fuel (so called Adiabatic CAES units), but no such units are in operation at present. The CAES system investigated in this project uses a different approach to avoid compression heat loss. The system uses a pre-compressed pressure vessel full of air. A liquid is pumped into the bottom of the vessel when charging and the same liquid is withdrawn through a turbine when discharging. In this case, the liquid works effectively as a piston compressing the gas in the vessel, hence the name “Adiabatic Liquid Piston Compressed Air Energy Storage” (ALP-CAES). The compression ratio of the gas in the vessel (ratio between maximum and minimum pressure) is relatively low; typical values would be < 1,5, whereas the compression ratio in existing CAES systems can be higher than 100, because the air is compressed from atmospheric pressure to the storage pressure. This investigation leads to the conclusion that: •The mechanical/electrical efficiency of the ALP-CAES system is significantly higher than existing CAES systems due to a low or nearly absent compression heat loss. Furthermore, pumps/turbines, which use a liquid as a medium, are more efficient than air/gas compressors/turbines. In addition, the demand for fuel during expansion does not occur. •The energy density of the ALP-CAES system is much lower than that of existing CAES systems (by a factor of 15-30) leading to a similar increase in investment in pressure vessel volume per stored MWh. Since the pressure vessel constitutes a relatively large fraction of the overall cost of a CAES system, an increase of 15-30 times renders the system economically unfeasible unless the operating conditions and the system design are very carefully selected to compensate the low energy density. Future electricity prices may increase to the extent that the efficiency benefit of ALP-CAES partly compensates the added investment. •When comparing ALP-CAES to an adiabatic CAES system, where compression heat is stored in thermal oil, the ALP-CAES system is found only to be competitive under a very specific set of operating/design conditions, including very high operation pressure and the use of very large caverns. •New systems are under development, which show an interesting trend in that they use near-isothermal compression and expansion of air (compression/expansion at almost constant temperature), eliminate compression heat loss and still maintain nearly the same level of energy density as existing CAES systems. This combination of features may make these systems superior to the ALP-CAES solution. The new systems are delivered by companies such as LightSail Energy and General Compression. Apparently, these new systems use piston compressors/expanders, at least for the prototypes. However, for large scale systems, piston mechanisms are not the most economical solution. In terms of large scale systems, turbo machinery is the only economical solution. •Even adiabatic CAES systems seem to add more cost to the electricity than can be accepted in the Danish power system. This added cost is primarily due to the investment in turbine/generator, heat exchangers, and a large quantity of thermal oil. To improve the economy, it would be relevant to investigate the possibility of replacing the thermal oil by water, for example by injecting the water directly into the air flow between the different compression stages to get a direct heat exchange between water and air. This investigation would focus on direct heat exchange in combination with turbo machinery.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Petersen, Tage","Elmegaard, Brian","Pedersen, Allan Schrøder"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-306052"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-GTS","DI-U"],"level3":{"GTS":["DI-GTS-ALL","DI-GTS-DTCI"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-GTS-DTCI","DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"nr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"adiabatic liquid piston compressed air energy storage","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dr","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/55753680/Adiabatic_Liquid_Piston.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-306052","ids":["dtu-04dd964d-7541-4c61-ad99-e39dc7edac21"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-1BCC7600007404C9CC6B29826EDBBBC1"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/55753680/Adiabatic_Liquid_Piston.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"danish technological institute","l2":"DI-GTS","l2n":"GTS Institutes","l3":"DI-GTS-DTCI","l3nn":"Danish Technological Institute","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Danish Technological Institute","namevar":["Danish Technological Institute"],"nora_code":"DI-GTS-DTCI","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Mechanical Engineering","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Mechanical Engineering, Thermal Energy"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Tage","key":"petersenpau","last":"Petersen","name":"Petersen, Tage","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Brian","key":"elmegaardpau","last":"Elmegaard","locid":"2f4e4dc0-1af4-4333-a85b-94d72ebec780","name":"Elmegaard, Brian","orcid":"0000-0002-0503-6286","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Allan Schrøder","key":"pedersenpau","last":"Pedersen","locid":"9d94f06f-c5ea-40dd-a915-f7b0f7a68664","name":"Pedersen, Allan Schrøder","orcid":"0000-0003-3709-3194","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"pages":"52","publisher":"Danish Technological Institute","status":"p"},"review":"No Review","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All GTS Institutes","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-GTS","DI-GTS-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","GTS Institutes","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-04dd964d-7541-4c61-ad99-e39dc7edac21"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Adiabatic Liquid Piston Compressed Air Energy Storage","type":"Report","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-306052","year":"2013","yearsub":"2013"}
{"abstract":"Det kollektive transportsystem er af vital betydning for specielt de større byer. Uden det kollektive udbud af trafik vil vejene sande til, og mobiliteten (fremkommeligheden) mindskes væsentligt. De fleste mennesker, der gør brug af det kollektive transportsystem, stiller sig spørgsmål som: Kan det mon ikke gøres bedre? Hvorfor kommer næste bus ikke, når jeg har brug for den? Kunne det ikke lade sig gøre at lave en køreplan med bedre korrespondance mellem de enkelte busafgange? Svaret på disse spørgsmål er som regel: Jo, det kan ofte gøres bedre, men på bekostning af noget andet, herunder (ofte økonomiske) ressourcer. Derudover er planlægningen af det kollektive transportsystem en særdeles kompliceret og udfordrende opgave. Kompleksiteten kommer dels af, at der som oftest er tale om meget store systemer med tusindvis af daglige afgange, der skal koordineres med fysiske og menneskelige ressourcer, dels af de økonomiske rammer, som planlægningen er underlagt.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Larsen, Allan","Petersen, Hanne Løhmann"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-357288"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"edu","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"nr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"optimering af kollektiv transport","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dba","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/376463996/118.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-357288","ids":["dtu-b08d4d99-800c-4bc5-8520-7d8844186cff"],"lang":"Danish","level":"Educational","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-E8125E7CAB30E937088DA02A42C57DBB"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/376463996/118.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Transport","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Transport, Transport optimisation and technique"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Allan","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"f830d213-0db6-43ef-969f-af088d969a4d","name":"Larsen, Allan","orcid":"0000-0002-6647-6832","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Hanne Løhmann","key":"petersenpau","last":"Petersen","locid":"02e0db26-d08e-4919-a69a-0925e5447720","name":"Petersen, Hanne Løhmann","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Carsten","key":"broderhansenpedh","last":"Broder Hansen","name":"Broder Hansen, Carsten","rank":3,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"isbn":["9788773272497"],"pages":"118-129","place":"Kgs. Lyngby","publisher":"DTU Transport","status":"p","title":"Transporthorisonter"},"review":"No Review","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-b08d4d99-800c-4bc5-8520-7d8844186cff"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Optimering af kollektiv transport","type":"Book Chapter","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-357288","year":"2013","yearsub":"2013"}
{"abstract":"We examined the relationship between urinary excretion of the RNA oxidation marker 8-oxo-7,8-dihydroguanosine (8-oxoGuo) and kidney injury comparing type 1 diabetes patients with different levels of albuminuria (normoalbuminuria: N=58, microalbuminuria: N = 46, macroalbuminuria: N =46) and a nondiabetic control group (N=57). Urinary 8-oxoGuo was measured in spot urine samples using ultraperformance liquid chromatography and tandem mass spectrometry. Urinary 8-oxoGuo was significantly higher in the patients [2.85 (2.45-3.33) vs. 2.49 (2.12-2.96)nmol/mmol creatinine, P=0.01]. However, after adjustment for possible confounders of oxidative stress, the differences reduced slightly and became statistically nonsignificant (P = 0.07). There were no significant differences in the level of 8-oxoGuo between the three groups of patients (P = 0.53) and there were no significant associations between 8-oxoGuo and estimated glomerular filtration rate or albumin-creatinine ratio. In conclusion, urinary excretion of the RNA oxidation marker 8-oxoGuo does not differ between type 1 diabetes patients with different levels of albuminuria.","author_count":10,"contributors":["Broedbaek, Kasper","Andersen, Jon Trærup","Jimenez-Solem, Espen","Petersen, Morten","Lajer, Maria","Henriksen, Trine","Weimann, Allan","Parving, Hans-Henrik","Rossing, Peter","Poulsen, Henrik Enghusen"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-739447"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["8 oxo 7 8 dihydroguanosine","Albuminuria","Diabetes","Oxidative stress"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"rna oxidation and albuminuria in type 000000000001 diabetes patients","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1097/XCE.0000000000000008","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-739447","identifier":[{"id":"84954359389","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-8bc9299a-2b20-48a1-a980-3872b8d422c9"],"keyword":["8-oxo-7,8-dihydroguanosine","Albuminuria","Diabetes","Oxidative stress"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-1827771B7B4B876C04039B396ABCFB4B"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1097/XCE.0000000000000008","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, External Centres, Forskningsenheden for Almen Praksis"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital - Bispebjerg and Frederiksberg"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Kasper","key":"broedbaekpau","last":"Broedbaek","locid":"fd11f672-8791-466e-b4da-418fb8a1db93","name":"Broedbaek, Kasper","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jon T.","key":"andersenpau","last":"Andersen","locid":"2fe4a9af-2462-4bba-8df4-2a518ea59342","name":"Andersen, Jon Trærup","name_org":"Andersen, Jon T.","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Espen","key":"jimenezsolempau","last":"Jimenez-Solem","locid":"683c5d73-a774-4aba-978d-da52ea4a866c","name":"Jimenez-Solem, Espen","orcid":"0000-0002-3777-147X","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Morten","key":"petersenpau","last