{"abstract":"Recent studies suggest that proton pump inhibitor treatment may increase insulin secretion and improve glucose metabolism in type 2 diabetes. In a randomised double-blind prospective placebo-controlled 2 × 2 factorial study, we examined the effect of esomeprazole on insulin secretion, HbA(1c) and cardiovascular risk factors in type 2 diabetes.","author_count":9,"contributors":["Hove, K D","Brøns, Cecilie","Færch, Kai Erik Vinther","Lund, S S","Petersen, J S","Karlsen, A E","Rossing, Pia","Rehfeld, J F","Vaag, Allan"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-414347"],"filters":{"added":"2022-04","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"OT":["Finance Division"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU","DI-U-UND"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU","DI-U-UND"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"effects of 000000000012 weeks treatment with a proton pump inhibitor on insulin secretion glucose metabolism and markers of cardiovascular risk in patients with type 000000000002 diabetes a randomised double blind prospective placebo controlled study","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/s00125-012-2714-y","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-414347","identifier":[{"id":"23011351","type":"pmid"},{"id":"84871614569","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-23072be3-5ac6-4f30-92a7-a5388c9a097c"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-C180CA2CB87B9B44103FF98D219296A1"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/s00125-012-2714-y","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2013","yearSub":"2013"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["University of Copenhagen"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"unclear universities","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-UND","l3nl":"Undetermined","l3nn":"Unclear Universities","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Unclear Universities","namevar":["Institut for Kultur og Globale Studier"],"nora_code":"DI-U-UND","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["Finance Division"],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","first":"K D","key":"hovepau","last":"Hove","name":"Hove, K D","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Cecilie","key":"brønspau","last":"Brøns","name":"Brøns, Cecilie","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Kai Erik Vinther","key":"færchpau","last":"Færch","name":"Færch, Kai Erik Vinther","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"S S","key":"lundpau","last":"Lund","name":"Lund, S S","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"J S","key":"petersenpau","last":"Petersen","name":"Petersen, J S","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"A E","key":"karlsenpau","last":"Karlsen","name":"Karlsen, A E","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Pia","key":"rossingpau","last":"Rossing","name":"Rossing, Pia","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"J F","key":"rehfeldpau","last":"Rehfeld","name":"Rehfeld, J F","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"A","key":"vaagpau","last":"Vaag","locid":"4b68020d-63cf-4701-ad10-cbc4845d0f1c","name":"Vaag, Allan","name_org":"Vaag, A","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["23011351"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/s00125-012-2714-y","issn":["0012186X","14320428"],"issn_org":["0012186X"],"issue":"1","journal":"Diabetologia","pages":"22-30","status":"p","title":"Diabetologia","volume":"56"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84871614569"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Undetermined","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-23072be3-5ac6-4f30-92a7-a5388c9a097c"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Effects of 12 weeks' treatment with a proton pump inhibitor on insulin secretion, glucose metabolism and markers of cardiovascular risk in patients with type 2 diabetes : a randomised double-blind prospective placebo-controlled study","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-414347","year":"2013","yearsub":"2013"}
{"abstract":"Purpose: To examine which of stress myocardial flow (MBF) and coronary flow reserve (CFR) determined by (15)-water-PET (PET) correspond most closely with diameter stenosis assessed by quantitative coronary angiography (QCA). Methods: Twenty-three patients with a C40% QCA stenosis underwent baseline and adenosine stress PET. Baseline MBF measures were corrected for myocardial workload and stress MBF and CFR calculated in 17 standard AHA myocardial segments and reassigned to respective feeding vessels. If multiple stenoses, only the most severe stenosis was considered. Pearson’s correlation coefficients were calculated and compared using Fisher r-to-z transformation. Results: A total of 35 QCA stenoses were identified with a mean diameter stenosis of 75% ± 18%, range 45-100%. Stress MBF and CFR in corresponding vascular territories were: 1.84 ± 0.78 and 1.86 ± 1.05 mL/minute/g, respectively. MBF was significantly correlated to QCA stenosis severity: r = -0.46, P = .006, whereas CFR was not, r = -0.28, P = .097. These two r values did not differ significantly, P = .42. In contrast, stress MBF and CFR were significantly correlated (C): r = 0.86, P\\.001. Conclusions: The correlation between anatomic and functional stenosis was poor, suggesting that the hemodynamic consequences of angiographically proven coronary stenoses should be examined by functional imaging like PET.","author_count":10,"contributors":["Thomassen, Anders","Braad, Poul-Erik","Johansen, Allan","Petersen, Henrik","Diederichsen, Axel Cosmus Pyndt","Mickley, Hans","Jensen, Lisette Okkels","Thayssen, Per","Blomberg, Björn","Høilund-Carlsen, Poul Flemming"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-594677"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-SDR"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-SDR","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"angiographic coronary stenosis versus 000000000015 o water pet myocardial blood flow","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dca","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/77522526/JNC_abstracts.pdf","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-594677","ids":["sdu-4ae38639-92a4-443c-ac37-8bd69091d1ee"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Local-1-1-7321A54559A18B6FCE621CAA015439E6"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/77522526/JNC_abstracts.pdf","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research, KI, OUH, Research unit of Clinical Physiology and Nuclear Medicine (Odense)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"region of southern denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-SDR","l3nl":"Region of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"Region of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Region of Southern Denmark","namevar":["Odense University Hospital"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-SDR","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Anders","key":"thomassenpau","last":"Thomassen","locid":"1c7f11fb-cf64-4085-909d-b78f183b9364","name":"Thomassen, Anders","orcid":"0000-0001-9839-1158","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Poul-Erik","key":"braadpau","last":"Braad","locid":"7df4b5a6-a971-420c-b424-ccc861b7f5ff","name":"Braad, Poul-Erik","orcid":"0000-0003-4906-5422","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Allan","key":"johansenpau","last":"Johansen","locid":"dc7a1a61-b703-48ec-bd87-c92b55784133","name":"Johansen, Allan","orcid":"0000-0002-3622-057X","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Henrik","key":"petersenpau","last":"Petersen","locid":"ea635371-4294-4379-9655-3da538fecf13","name":"Petersen, Henrik","orcid":"0000-0002-1118-1500","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Axel Cosmus Pyndt","key":"diederichsenpau","last":"Diederichsen","locid":"d84be6bc-52bf-4710-9f66-0209cfab4f54","name":"Diederichsen, Axel Cosmus Pyndt","orcid":"0000-0002-1285-4826","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Hans","key":"mickleypau","last":"Mickley","locid":"f6789f9a-e23b-4ab8-bd7d-a3c168107cdb","name":"Mickley, Hans","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Lisette Okkels","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","locid":"b78c452e-5a69-41fe-ba49-0096c84d1d4d","name":"Jensen, Lisette Okkels","orcid":"0000-0002-4838-2429","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Per","key":"thayssenpau","last":"Thayssen","locid":"ac38a4d1-1115-438e-bd0a-0eac73fc3d2a","name":"Thayssen, Per","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Björn","key":"blombergpau","last":"Blomberg","name":"Blomberg, Björn","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Poul Flemming","key":"høilundcarlsenpau","last":"Høilund-Carlsen","locid":"a1ff65cf-cdaa-4192-bef3-a915cfe6cceb","name":"Høilund-Carlsen, Poul Flemming","orcid":"0000-0001-7420-2367","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"issn":["10713581","15326551"],"issn_org":["10713581"],"issue":"Supplement, May/June 2013","journal":"Journal of Nuclear Cardiology","pages":"33","publisher":"Elsevier","status":"p","title":"Journal of Nuclear Cardiology","volume":"Volume 20"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Region of Southern Denmark","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-4ae38639-92a4-443c-ac37-8bd69091d1ee"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Angiographic coronary stenosis versus (15)O-water PET myocardial blood flow","type":"Conference Abstract","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-594677","year":"2013","yearsub":"2013"}
{"abstract":"BACKGROUND: The authors studied injury mortality in Denmark among refugees and immigrants compared with that among native Danes. METHOD: A register-based, historical prospective cohort design. All refugees (n=29, 139) and family reunited immigrants (n=27, 134) who between 1 January 1993 and 31 December 1999 received residence permission were included and matched 1:4 on age and sex with native Danes. Civil registration numbers were cross-linked to the Register of Causes of Death, and fatalities due to unintentional and intentional injuries were identified based on ICD-10 diagnosis. Sex-specific mortality ratios were estimated by migrant status and region of birth, adjusting for age and income and using a Cox regression model after a median follow-up of 11-12 years. RESULTS: Compared with native Danes, both female (RR=0.44; 95% CI 0.23 to 0.83) and male (RR=0.40; 95% CI 0.29 to 0.56) refugees as well as female (RR=0.40; 95% CI 0.21 to 0.76) and male (RR=0.22; 95% CI 0.12 to 0.42) immigrants had significantly lower mortality from unintentional injuries. Suicide rates were significantly lower for male refugees (RR=0.38; 95% CI 0.24 to 0.61) and male immigrants (RR=0.24; 95% CI 0.10 to 0.59), whereas their female counterparts showed no significant differences. Only immigrant women had a significantly higher homicide rate (RR=3.09; 95% CI 1.11 to 8.60) compared with native Danes. CONCLUSIONS: Overall results were advantageous to migrant groups. Research efforts should concentrate on investigating protective factors among migrants, which may benefit injury prevention in the majority population.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Nørredam, Marie Louise","Larsen, Maja Olsbjerg","Petersen, Jørgen Holm","Laursen, Bjarne","Krasnik, Allan"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-642303"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2"