{"abstract":"Type 2 diabetes is associated with stroke and cardiac dysfunction. We therefore investigated isolated middle cerebral arteries and coronary septal arteries from the diabetic Goto-Kakizaki (GK) rat model of nonobese type 2 diabetes.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Kold-Petersen, Henrik Houmann","Brøndum, Emil Toft","Nilsson, H","Flyvbjerg, Allan","Aalkjær, Christian"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-256452"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["15 Hydroxy 11 alpha 9 alpha epoxymethano prosta 5 13 dienoic Acid","Amides","Animals","Blood Glucose","Calcium","Coronary Vessels","Diabetes Mellitus Type 2","Disease Models Animal","Male","Middle Cerebral Artery","Nitric oxide","Protein Kinase C","Pyridines","Rats","Rats Wistar","rho Associated Kinases"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"impaired myogenic tone in isolated cerebral and coronary resistance arteries from the goto kakizaki rat model of type 000000000002 diabetes","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1159/000335487","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-256452","identifier":[{"id":"84859713759","type":"scopus"},{"id":"22508433","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["au-deaff2c4-5d1a-4def-8583-4c9f3ce3d28a"],"keyword":["15-Hydroxy-11 alpha,9 alpha-(epoxymethano)prosta-5,13-dienoic Acid","Amides","Animals","Blood Glucose","Calcium","Coronary Vessels","Diabetes Mellitus, Type 2","Disease Models, Animal","Male","Middle Cerebral Artery","Nitric Oxide","Protein Kinase C","Pyridines","Rats","Rats, Wistar","rho-Associated Kinases"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-B6C44B422E4235AEF638CFDA78F14002"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1159/000335487","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Biomedicine, Department of Biomedicine - Danish Biomembrane Research Centre"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"H","key":"koldpetersenpau","last":"Kold-Petersen","locid":"c521af49-3e26-41dd-965b-1a9cefbd637e","name":"Kold-Petersen, Henrik Houmann","name_org":"Kold-Petersen, H","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"E","key":"brøndumpau","last":"Brøndum","locid":"c6d52a57-ff18-468b-8640-793f97d108e2","name":"Brøndum, Emil Toft","name_org":"Brøndum, E","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"H","key":"nilssonpau","last":"Nilsson","locid":"1476e776-4e5b-4516-9e5d-be15d398ef2a","name":"Nilsson, H","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"A","key":"flyvbjergpau","last":"Flyvbjerg","locid":"29cf36bd-c1a0-4026-8c90-a70cb1f46402","name":"Flyvbjerg, Allan","name_org":"Flyvbjerg, A","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"C","key":"aalkjaerpau","last":"Aalkjaer","locid":"5432bf4e-2402-4f9d-9c5b-d44af26ac406","name":"Aalkjær, Christian","name_org":"Aalkjaer, C","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["22508433"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1159/000335487","issn":["10181172","14230135"],"issn_org":["10181172"],"issue":"3","journal":"Journal of Vascular Research","pages":"267-78","publisher":"S. Karger AG","status":"p","title":"Journal of Vascular Research","volume":"49"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84859713759"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-deaff2c4-5d1a-4def-8583-4c9f3ce3d28a"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Impaired myogenic tone in isolated cerebral and coronary resistance arteries from the goto-kakizaki rat model of type 2 diabetes","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-256452","year":"2012","yearsub":"2012"}
{"abstract":"BACKGROUND: The authors studied injury mortality in Denmark among refugees and immigrants compared with that among native Danes. METHOD: A register-based, historical prospective cohort design. All refugees (n=29¿139) and family reunited immigrants (n=27¿134) who between 1 January 1993 and 31 December 1999 received residence permission were included and matched 1:4 on age and sex with native Danes. Civil registration numbers were cross-linked to the Register of Causes of Death, and fatalities due to unintentional and intentional injuries were identified based on ICD-10 diagnosis. Sex-specific mortality ratios were estimated by migrant status and region of birth, adjusting for age and income and using a Cox regression model after a median follow-up of 11-12 years. RESULTS: Compared with native Danes, both female (RR=0.44; 95% CI 0.23 to 0.83) and male (RR=0.40; 95% CI 0.29 to 0.56) refugees as well as female (RR=0.40; 95% CI 0.21 to 0.76) and male (RR=0.22; 95% CI 0.12 to 0.42) immigrants had significantly lower mortality from unintentional injuries. Suicide rates were significantly lower for male refugees (RR=0.38; 95% CI 0.24 to 0.61) and male immigrants (RR=0.24; 95% CI 0.10 to 0.59), whereas their female counterparts showed no significant differences. Only immigrant women had a significantly higher homicide rate (RR=3.09; 95% CI 1.11 to 8.60) compared with native Danes. CONCLUSIONS: Overall results were advantageous to migrant groups. Research efforts should concentrate on investigating protective factors among migrants, which may benefit injury prevention in the majority population.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Norredam, Marie","Olsbjerg, Maja","Petersen, Jørgen Holm","Laursen, Bjarne","Krasnik, Allan"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-485110"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"are there differences in injury mortality among refugees and immigrants compared with native born","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1136/injuryprev-2012-040336","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-485110","identifier":[{"id":"22627779","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC3607096","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"84875374310","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-9954ecdc-e2b7-4713-acae-e420bfa54549"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-3-5-F17DCEB540A3FA14F04A82BEBA9554FE"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1136/injuryprev-2012-040336","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Public Health","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Public Health, Section of Health Services Research"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Marie","key":"norredampau","last":"Norredam","locid":"b2ded723-225a-455c-ae7b-9be191ab1b53","name":"Norredam, Marie","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Maja","key":"olsbjergpau","last":"Olsbjerg","name":"Olsbjerg, Maja","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jorgen H","key":"petersenpau","last":"Petersen","locid":"33c1c5b2-2e1e-4259-b4d7-04657a2bdb9b","name":"Petersen, Jørgen Holm","name_org":"Petersen, Jorgen H","orcid":"0000-0003-3979-7443","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Bjarne","key":"laursenpau","last":"Laursen","locid":"3ddf813b-fcb2-461d-af51-da58fbe7fca1","name":"Laursen, Bjarne","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Allan","key":"krasnikpau","last":"Krasnik","locid":"d1a42a6c-e3d6-4d5b-803e-e80b13314d46","name":"Krasnik, Allan","orcid":"0000-0003-1612-6129","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["22627779"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1136/injuryprev-2012-040336","issn":["13538047","14755785"],"journal":"Injury Prevention","status":"p","title":"Injury Prevention","title_org":"Injury prevention : journal of the International Society for Child and Adolescent Injury Prevention"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84875374310"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-9954ecdc-e2b7-4713-acae-e420bfa54549"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Are there differences in injury mortality among refugees and immigrants compared with native-born?","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-485110","year":"2012","yearsub":"2012"}
{"abstract":"The IGF-IR density on CD4+T-lymphocytes was studied using flow cytometry in 40 early steroid- and DMARD-naïve rheumatoid arthritis (RA) patients before and after 52 weeks of treatment with methotrexate+placebo or methotrexate+cyclosporine A and in 15 controls. RA patients had increased IGF-IR density on CD4+T-lymphocytes at week 0 and week 52, irrespective of treatment. IGF-IR-positive CD4+T-lymphocytes fraction decreased during treatment, but neither at week 0 nor at week 52 did it differ from healthy controls. No correlations were found to disease activity parameters.","author_count":11,"contributors":["Laurberg, Trine Bay","Ellingsen, Torkell","Thorsen, J","Møller, Bjarne Kuno","Hansen, Ib","Tarp, Ulrik","Hetland, Merete Lund","Hørslev-Petersen, Kim","Flyvbjerg, Allan","Frystyk, Jan","Stengaard-Pedersen, Kristian"],"cuid":["S04-094.04-666498"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":4,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-UC"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"],"UC":["DI-UC-ALL","DI-UC-VIA"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU","DI-UC-VIA"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"insulin like growth factor i receptor density on cd000000000004 t lymphocytes from active early steroid and dmard naïve rheumatoid arthritis patients is up regulated and not influenced by 000000000001 year of clinically effective treatment","src":["au","ku","sdu","via"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU","DI-UC-VIA"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/s00296-010-1683-z","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S04-094.04-666498","identifier":[{"id":"21246373","type":"pmid"},{"id":"84857048795","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-ccaedadc-0f9e-47e7-a696-42552ae42a70","ku-66cf9400-2a40-44d1-89fd-ee4d0d1159c9","sdu-e56d3d3e-b3be-4