openhagen"],"title":"Use of cross-border healthcare services among ethnic Danes, Turkish immigrants and Turkish descendants in Denmark: a combined survey and registry study","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-482719","year":"2012","yearsub":"2012"}
{"abstract":"ABSTRACT: BACKGROUND: Comparisons of mortality patterns between different migrant groups, and between migrants and natives, are relevant to understanding, and ultimately reducing, inequalities in health. To date, European studies on migrants' mortality patterns are scarce and are based solely on country of birth, rather than migrant status. However, mortality patterns may be affected by implications in relation to migrant status, such as health hazards related to life circumstances before and during migration, and factors related to ethnic origin. Consequently, we investigated differences in both all-cause and cause-specific mortality from cancer and cardiovascular disease among refugees and immigrants, compared with the mortality among native Danes. METHODS: A register-based, historical prospective cohort design. All refugees (n = 29,139) and family-reunited immigrants (n = 27,134) who, between 1 January1993 and 31 December1999, were granted right of residence in Denmark were included and matched 1:4 on age and sex with native Danes. To identify deaths, civil registration numbers were cross-linked to the Register of Causes of Death (01.01.1994--31.12.2007) and the Danish Civil Registration System (01.01.1994--31.12.2008). Mortality rate ratios were estimated separately for men and women by migrant status and region of birth, adjusting for age and income and using a Cox regression model, after a median follow-up of 10--13 years after arrival. RESULTS: Compared with native Danes, all-cause mortality was significantly lower among female (RR = 0.78; 95%CI: 0.71;0.85) and male (RR = 0.64; 95%CI: 0.59-0.69;) refugees. The rates were also significantly lower for immigrants: women (RR = 0.44; 95%CI: 0.38;0.51) and men (RR = 0.43; 95%CI: 0.37;0.51). Both migrant groups also had lower cause-specific mortality from cancer and cardiovascular diseases. For both all-cause and cause-specific mortality, immigrants generally had lower mortality than refugees, and differences were observed according to ethnic origin. CONCLUSIONS: Mortality patterns were overall advantageous for refugees and immigrants compared with native Danes. Research should concentrate on disentangling the reasons behind migrants' health advantages, in order to enlighten future preventive public-health efforts, for the benefit of the entire population.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Norredam, Marie","Olsbjerg, Maja","Petersen, Jørgen Holm","Juel, Knud","Krasnik, Allan"],"cuid":["S02-091.46-044671"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"inequalities in mortality among refugees and immigrants compared to native danes a historical prospective cohort study","src":["ku","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/1471-2458-12-757","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S02-091.46-044671","identifier":[{"id":"PMC3575278","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"84865856089","type":"scopus"},{"id":"22963550","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-99f64207-761c-4fb5-983d-938bb76f30e2","sdu-ee624ecb-6a9e-4cb5-8a22-5e21b00823df"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-01A55A8C8ED1935D6CE52578754EAE88"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/1471-2458-12-757","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Public Health","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Public Health, Section of Health Services Research"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, National Institute of Public Health, Research Programme on Health and Morbidity in Denmark"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Marie","key":"norredampau","last":"Norredam","locid":"b2ded723-225a-455c-ae7b-9be191ab1b53","name":"Norredam, Marie","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Maja","key":"olsbjergpau","last":"Olsbjerg","name":"Olsbjerg, Maja","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jorgen H","key":"petersenpau","last":"Petersen","locid":"33c1c5b2-2e1e-4259-b4d7-04657a2bdb9b","name":"Petersen, Jørgen Holm","name_org":"Petersen, Jorgen H","orcid":"0000-0003-3979-7443","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Knud","key":"juelpau","last":"Juel","locid":"95a22bf7-54de-48e0-ab33-855002b210be","name":"Juel, Knud","orcid":"0000-0002-4134-1173","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Allan","key":"krasnikpau","last":"Krasnik","locid":"d1a42a6c-e3d6-4d5b-803e-e80b13314d46","name":"Krasnik, Allan","orcid":"0000-0003-1612-6129","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["22963550"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1186/1471-2458-12-757","issn":["14712458"],"issue":"1","journal":"BMC Public Health","pages":"757","status":"p","title":"BMC Public Health","title_org":"B M C Public Health","volume":"12"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84865856089"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-99f64207-761c-4fb5-983d-938bb76f30e2","sdu-ee624ecb-6a9e-4cb5-8a22-5e21b00823df"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Inequalities in mortality among refugees and immigrants compared to native Danes -- a historical prospective cohort study","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-091.46-044671","year":"2012","yearsub":"2012"}
{"abstract":"In recent years the need for greater security for storing personal and business data or accessing corporate networks on mobile devices is growing rapidly, and one of the potential solutions is to employ the innovative biometric authentication techniques. This paper presents the development of a mobile biometric authentication system based on electroencephalogram (EEG) recordings in combination with already proven technologies such as facial detection and near-field communication (NFC). The overall goal of this work is to fill the gap between mobile web technologies and wireless EEG devices and to develop a new authentication technique and a feasible application. Therefore, we review the relevant literature, conduct several EEG measurement experiments and discuss their procedure and results with experts in the EEG and digital signal processing (DSP) fields. Based on these results we build and present a mobile prototype system capable of authenticating users based on the uniqueness of their brainwaves. Furthermore, we implement a novel authentication process, which leads the authentication system to be more secure. We also give suggestions for future improvements of the system.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Klonovs, Juris","Petersen, Christoffer Kjeldgaard","Olesen, Henning","Hammershøj, Allan Dyhr"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-112617"],"event":{"end":"2012-10-25","place":"Berlin, de","start":"2012-10-23","title":"WWRF Meeting","year":"2012"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["hum"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"development of a mobile eeg based biometric authentication system","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/71244468/EEG_authentication_v1.0.pdf","version":"Pre-print"},"id":"S01-000.00-112617","ids":["aau-d761b175-fca6-45c4-ba8c-31781163d8e9"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities"],"noi":["Local-1-1-10CE9C7B2A2E99038530D36B37B18466"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/71244468/EEG_authentication_v1.0.pdf","version":"Pre-print"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science (ENG), Department of Mechanical and Manufacturing Engineering (M-TECH)","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science (TECH)","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, Department of Materials and Production, Robotics and Automation","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, Department of Materials and Production, Robotics, Vision and Machine Intelligence","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Electronic Systems, Center for Communication, Media and Information Technologies"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Juris","key":"klonovspau","last":"Klonovs","locid":"92c2c39b-a852-4afa-94c1-d0103d6e73f9","name":"Klonovs, Juris","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Christoffer Kjeldgaard","key":"petersenpau","last":"Petersen","locid":"b8d938f6-7597-4534-ab01-9f8fb359b5a4","name":"Petersen, Christoffer Kjeldgaard","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Henning","key":"olesenpau","last":"Olesen","locid":"d09c5e60-0c7f-4d62-b19e-070932b39ef3","name":"Olesen, Henning","orcid":"0000-0002-9331-4011","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Allan Dyhr","key":"hammershøjpau","last":"Hammershøj","locid":"8b9075ea-260e-46dc-a2dc-c907d1aa7342","name":"Hammershøj, Allan Dyhr","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-d761b175-fca6-45c4-ba8c-31781163d8e9"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Development of a Mobile EEG-based Biometric Authentication System","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-112617","year":"2012","yearsub":"2012"}
{"abstract":"Schizophrenia is associated with perceptual and physiological auditory processing impairments that may result from primary auditory cortex excitatory and inhibitory circuit pathology. High-frequency oscillations are important for auditory function and are often reported to be disrupted in schizophrenia. These oscillations may, in part, depend on upregulation of gamma-aminobutyric acid synthesis by glutamate decarboxylase 65 (GAD65) in response to high interneuron firing rates. It is not known whether levels of GAD65 protein or GAD65-expressing boutons are altered in schizophrenia.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Moyer, Caitlin E","Delevich, Kristen M","Fish, Kenneth N","Asafu-Adjei, Josephine K","Sampson, Allan R","Dorph-Petersen, Karl-Anton","Lewis, David A","Sweet, Robert A"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-226512"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"reduced glutamate decarboxylase 000000000065 protein within primary auditory cortex inhibitory boutons in schizophrenia","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.biopsych.2012.04.010","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-226512","identifier":[{"id":"22624794","type":"pmid"},{"id":"84867073251","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC3465514","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["au-aa627c45-644c-4ae8-96d8-e020a57cb627"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-C7DE820CA7D227A5510C2A4802771E8F"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.biopsych.2012.04.010","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - Translational Neuropsychiatry Unit"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Caitlin E","key":"moyerpau","last":"Moyer","name":"Moyer, Caitlin E","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Kristen M","key":"delevichpau","last":"Delevich","name":"Delevich, Kristen M","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Kenneth N","key":"fishpau","last":"Fish","name":"Fish, Kenneth N","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Josephine K","key":"asafuadjeipau","last":"Asafu-Adjei","name":"Asafu-Adjei, Josephine K","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Allan R","key":"sampsonpau","last":"Sampson","name":"Sampson, Allan R","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Karl-Anton","key":"dorphpetersenpau","last":"Dorph-Petersen","locid":"fb25cb46-a24f-4759-9fe8-58e620eb7ea2","name":"Dorph-Petersen, Karl-Anton","orcid":"0000-0002-6676-034X","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"David A","key":"lewispau","last":"Lewis","name":"Lewis, David A","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Robert A","key":"sweetpau","last":"Sweet","name":"Sweet, Robert A","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["22624794"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.biopsych.2012.04.010","issn":["03787354","16622774"],"issn_org":["03787354"],"issue":"9","journal":"Advances in Biological Psychiatry","pages":"734-43","publisher":"S. Karger AG","status":"p","title":"Advances in Biological Psychiatry","volume":"72"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84867073251"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-aa627c45-644c-4ae8-96d8-e020a57cb627"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Reduced glutamate decarboxylase 65 protein within primary auditory cortex inhibitory boutons in schizophrenia","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-226512","year":"2012","yearsub":"2012"}
{"author_count":5,"contributors":["Norredam, Marie","Larsen, Maja Olsbjerg","Petersen, Jørgen Holm","Bygbjerg, Ib Christian","Krasnik, Allan"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-473496"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"mortality from infectious disease among refugees and immigrants compared to native danes a historical prospective cohort study","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1111/j.1365-3156.2011.02901.x.","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-473496","identifier":[{"id":"84855948235","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-85d4d4f0-928c-427d-8e28-3f1e4e2da1e5"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-640DB0C457C119A495D5905057D79DA5"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1111/j.1365-3156.2011.02901.x.","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Public Health, Section of Health Services Research"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Marie Louise","key":"nørredampau","last":"Nørredam","locid":"b2ded723-225a-455c-ae7b-9be191ab1b53","name":"Norredam, Marie","name_org":"Nørredam, Marie Louise","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Maja Olsbjerg","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"3340586c-5d0f-448c-8643-ee0e0dc8fafe","name":"Larsen, Maja Olsbjerg","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jørgen Holm","key":"petersenpau","last":"Petersen","locid":"33c1c5b2-2e1e-4259-b4d7-04657a2bdb9b","name":"Petersen, Jørgen Holm","orcid":"0000-0003-3979-7443","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Ib Christian","key":"bygbjergpau","last":"Bygbjerg","locid":"acec49c2-8e30-45f6-8785-19112c22d379","name":"Bygbjerg, Ib Christian","orcid":"0000-0001-9100-2754","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Allan","key":"krasnikpau","last":"Krasnik","locid":"d1a42a6c-e3d6-4d5b-803e-e80b13314d46","name":"Krasnik, Allan","orcid":"0000-0003-1612-6129","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1111/j.1365-3156.2011.02901.x","issn":["13602276","13653156"],"issn_org":["13602276"],"issue":"2","journal":"Tropical Medicine & International Health","pages":"223-230","status":"p","title":"Tropical Medicine & International Health","volume":"17"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84855948235"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-85d4d4f0-928c-427d-8e28-3f1e4e2da1e5"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Mortality from infectious disease among refugees and immigrants compared to native Danes: a historical prospective cohort study","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-473496","year":"2012","yearsub":"2012"}
{"abstract":"Previous studies have shown an association between oxidative stress and various diseases in humans including cancer, cardiovascular disease, diabetes, and chronic respiratory disease. To what extents this damage is determined by genetic and environmental factors is unknown. In a classical twin study with 198 elderly twins we examined the contributions of genetic versus environmental factors to nucleic acid oxidation and lipid peroxidation. Urinary excretion of 8-oxo-7,8-dihydro-2'-deoxyguanosine (8-oxodG), 8-oxo-7,8-dihydroguanosine (8-oxoGuo), and dinor,dihydro F2-isoprostane metabolites (F2-IsoP-M) was measured using liquid chromatography-tandem mass spectrometry. The environmental influence on nucleic acid oxidation and lipid peroxidation was predominant, leaving only little influence from genetic factors, as evidenced by no differences in intraclass correlations between monozygotic (MZ) and dizygotic (DZ) twins, neither for 8-oxodG (r(MZ)=0.55, r(DZ)=0.47; P=0.43), F(2)-IsoP-M (r(MZ)=0.33, r(DZ)=0.22; P=0.42), nor 8-oxoGuo (r(MZ)=0.45, r(DZ)=0.58; P=0.21). Accordingly, heritability estimates for the three markers of oxidative damage were low (h²=0.17-0.22). The three urinary markers of oxidative stress were closely correlated (r=0.60-0.84). In conclusion, we demonstrated in a large population of elderly Danish twins that \"whole-body\" oxidative damage to nucleic acids and lipids is predominantly determined by potentially modifiable nongenetic factors.","author_count":12,"contributors":["Broedbaek, Kasper","Ribel-Madsen, Rasmus","Henriksen, Trine","Weimann, Allan","Petersen, Morten","Andersen, Jon Trærup","Afzal, Shoaib","Hjelvang, Brian","Roberts, L Jackson","Vaag, Allan","Poulsen, Pernille","Poulsen, Henrik Enghusen"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-398126"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Aged","Aged 80 and over","Biological Markers","DNA damage","Denmark","Deoxyguanosine","Environmental Exposure","F2 Isoprostanes","Female","Guanosine","Humans","Lipid Peroxidation","Male","Middle Aged","Oxidation Reduction","Oxidative stress","Twins Dizygotic","Twins Monozygotic"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"genetic and environmental influences on oxidative damage assessed in elderly danish twins","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.freeradbiomed.2011.02.017","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-398126","identifier":[{"id":"21354303","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC3090514","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"79955591924","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-07c616c1-3b32-4222-abee-6c62191be44c"],"keyword":["Aged","Aged, 80 and over","Biological Markers","DNA Damage","Denmark","Deoxyguanosine","Environmental Exposure","F2-Isoprostanes","Female","Guanosine","Humans","Lipid Peroxidation","Male","Middle Aged","Oxidation-Reduction","Oxidative Stress","Twins, Dizygotic","Twins, Monozygotic"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-D256E56C9ABFDB26F91CD3A616BFB70F"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.freeradbiomed.2011.02.017","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Novo Nordisk Foundation Center for Basic Metabolic Research, Human Genomics and Metagenomics in Metabolism"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"